The expert said that all these contributions contribute to building the RCEP, which will help boost the trade of member countries.
The Asean Agreement, which entered into force in 2022, aims to strengthen economic ties and enhance trade and investment activities, as well as contribute to narrowing the development gap between the parties.
The ASEAN Agreement provides for a comprehensive, high-quality, high-quality and mutually beneficial modern economic partnership agreement between ASEAN Member States and ASEAN Free Trade Agreement partners. The ASEAN Agreement is important for pandemics and economic recovery after the Kovid-19 outbreak in East Asia.
The year 2022 clearly demonstrates the importance of the ASEAN Agreement, the largest regional and global trade hub. AEC, a regional multilateral free trade agreement "based on legal basis", will be crucial for economic recovery from regional and global epidemic crises.
