Cambodia prepares more than 10,000 troops to protect security, order and safety for ASEAN Summit (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodia will host the ASEAN Summit and related summits starting from 08 to 8 November 13, 2022, and this meeting will be attended by the world's top leaders and many international institutions.
Speaking to Fresh News on the afternoon of November 3, 2022, Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and Spokesman of the National Police, confirmed that so far the Cambodian police force is ready. And to protect the security, order and safety of the leaders of the countries and institutions that come to attend the ASEAN Summit and related meetings in Cambodia.
According to the Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, there are more than 12,000 troops ready to defend, including the National Police, the Gendarmerie and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. This is from 14 units and institutions. In the future, the Cambodian forces have the ability to manage to maintain security, safety and order in this important event.
According to Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, in addition to the national forces, Cambodia has also received support and cooperation in the exchange of security information to prevent terrorism and the exchange of information related to the defense of the ASEAN Summit, including the promise of experience. Provide training to support the defense of the ASEAN Summit from friendly parties as well.
General Neth Savoeun said that the Cambodian authorities are also ready to cooperate with the competent forces of other countries will come to participate if requested. General Neth Savoeun also instructed the authorities and commanders at all levels to pay attention to security and order from October 25 until the end of the ASEAN Summit.
Please be informed that the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits and related meetings in 2022, which Cambodia is hosting, is the third time, the first time was held in 2002 and the second time in 2012. This is a great national pride because it will reflect the region and the world to recognize and realize the potential of Cambodia, and this is also a forum that honors Cambodia, reflecting the ability, excellence, equality in the region and internationally.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Recommends 8 Points to Improve Food Security, Food Security and Nutrition for Progress
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in a message to celebrate the 9th National Nutrition Day on November 6 under the theme "Safer Food, Better Health" recommended 8 points to promote Food security, food security and nutrition for systematic development.
First, all relevant ministries and institutions must continue to review and prepare legal documents related to hygiene, safety, quality and suitability of food, including food for sale on the streets and in educational institutions to support the implementation of food safety laws and strengthen Implement this law in consultation with the private sector and development partners.
Second, all relevant ministries and institutions must review the requirements for the formulation of policies on food safety and quality and some important guidelines in accordance with the technical regulations of food and the provisions of the law on food safety.
Third, all ministries and institutions related to food safety and quality "from farm to restaurant" must cooperate and provide information to facilitate the planning and preparation of national programs for implementation and analysis to manage potential risks. Follow the food production line and ensure that all food safety guidelines are adhered to and disseminated to the public and involved stakeholders and consumers.
Fourth, the Council for the Rehabilitation of Agriculture and Rural Development must cooperate with relevant stakeholders to organize the "World Food Safety Day" every June 7 every year to raise public awareness of the overwhelming benefits of food safety. For the health and well-being of the people.
Sixth, all Capital-Provincial Administrations must advise Commune / Sangkat Councils to integrate food safety, food security and nutrition into the Commune / Sangkat 3-Year Development Plan and Investment Program to promote the implementation of the National Strategy on Food Security and Nutrition. At the sub-national level to be highly effective.
Seventh, all ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations, development partners, civil society, the private sector and the community must join in inspiring and supporting the implementation of exclusive breastfeeding during the first six months and the continuation of breastfeeding. Up to a child at least 2 years old.
Eighth, all types of media must participate in widely disseminating the importance of food safety to the public to understand and participate with the Royal Government in implementing the law on food safety.
