(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam will lead a high-level delegation to pay an official visit to Cambodia from November 8 to 9, 2022. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, obtained by Fresh News.
On the occasion of this visit, Mr. Pham Minh Chinh will pay homage to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia in the Royal Palace.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam will pay a separate courtesy call on Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, and Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
During his stay in Phnom Penh, Mr. Pham Minh Chinh will lay a wreath at the Independence Monument, at the statue of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, "His Majesty the King" and at the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Palace.
The Vietnamese Prime Minister's visit coincides with the celebration of the 55th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries, which is designated as the "Year of Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship."
Top Cambodian official: Child sexual exploitation online is on the rise and becomes a global concern
(Phnom Penh): Chong Phat, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Rural Development, said that in the context of the age of technological advancement and the Internet, online sexual exploitation of children is spreading and becoming a global concern. Round.
He said that during the Kovid 19 period and so far, online use among students has increased dramatically in both urban and rural areas, with both positive and negative impacts. .
Mr. Chong Phat congratulated ChalFan Cambodia for launching a four-year strategic plan 2022-2025, as well as launching an online child safety project.
