Mr. Chong Phat stressed that this situation requires the attention and cooperation of all stakeholders, including the promotion of education and outreach to increase the correct understanding of child sexual exploitation online. Both strengthen the effectiveness of the implementation of protective measures.
In order to contribute to the prevention of child abuse, this morning, November 3, 2022, Chalfan Cambodia organized a launching ceremony of its strategic plan for 2022-2025 and launched a child safety project online. To protect children from abuse in an age where the Internet is booming.
For the next four years, Chaldean, a foreign and child-focused organization, will continue to prioritize education, child protection, social and psychological education, disaster response, and post-pandemic recovery. Of Kovid 19. In its strategic plan, Charles Fan will highlight investments in online child safety projects and sports development projects.
