Minister of Culture: The performance of "Moha Phearot" in the ASEAN Cultural Festival aims to promote the beautiful cultural forms of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Phoeung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, said that the multi-purpose drama "Moha Phearat" will be performed in the ASEAN Cultural Festival with the aim of promoting the beautiful cultural forms of Cambodia to national and international guests.
On that occasion, the Minister also praised and appreciated all teachers, artists and artists who have the spirit of care and hard work in rehearsing this mixed theater to perform for the audience in order. Disseminate beautiful cultural forms to national and international guests at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall in the near future.
Please be informed that the story of the Great Brotherhood carved in the gallery of Angkor Wat will be presented to the guests who attended the ASEAN Summit and related meetings in the ASEAN Cultural Festival. This classic will be performed live on the night of November 11, 2022 with 80 people for 45 minutes.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Chheang Chhadapheak, Acting Director of the Department of Performing Arts, stated that "The Great Pharaoh will be performed live by the performing arts team of the Department of Performing Arts and the Royal University of Fine Arts on the night of November 11. 2022, with 80 people, lasts 45 minutes.
The story of the Great Brotherhood has infiltrated and permeated the human society of some countries in Southeast Asia since the beginning of the Christian era, including Cambodia. Numerous inscriptions and sculptures depict scenes from the Great Pharaoh's story, such as the carvings in the Angkor Wat gallery, about the battlefields of the Kao Rop and Bandop, which researchers call the "Kuruset War".
To this day, the story that ancient Cambodia is familiar with fades from the memory of the Khmer. Some locals, especially Angkorians, when they see the sculptures at Angkor Wat, they just remember saying, "This sculpture is about a war between brothers." But in other Southeast Asian countries, such as Indonesia, the narrative is still alive and well in society. The locals know and take this story to tell or perform as other performing arts as usual.
The resurgence of tourism is a major driver of growth in Southeast Asia's second-largest economy, with the Thai Ministry of Finance on Friday forecasting a steady influx of visitors. 10.3 million foreign tourists this year and 21.5 million in 2023.
That compares with just 428,000 foreign tourists last year and nearly 40 million before the 2019 pandemic, when tourism accounted for 12 percent of Thailand's gross domestic product.
China's real estate sector, once a pillar of economic growth, fell sharply last year as government measures to curb over-borrowing from developers and the recession caused by Kovid. .
Sales of real estate in 100 cities fell about 20 percent in October from a year earlier, according to a separate CIA report.
Chen added that any recovery in the real estate market is expected to be delayed if China adheres to strict Kovid-19 prevention measures. Such a blockade is expected to remain in effect for some time after this month's Communist Party Congress.
Last month, new home prices in Shanghai and Shenzhen fell 0.05 percent and 0.32 percent in October from September, respectively. Regional home sales in Shanghai and Guangzhou fell 35 percent and 26 percent in October from a year earlier, respectively. According to Reuters.
