CLMV Tourism Minister Continues Four-Country Strategy to Boost Regional Tourism Growth
The 6th Cambodia-Laos-Myanmar-Vietnam Ministerial Meeting on Tourism was held on November 3, 2022 in Siem Reap, attended by the Lao Minister of Information, Culture and Tourism, the Minister of Tourism of Cambodia and the Deputy Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism of Vietnam.
On that occasion, the meeting commended the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his meaningful welcome message. The Minister highly appreciated the in-depth vision of CLMV tourism and committed to implementing the recommendations included in the CLMV Tourism Action Plan 2023-2025.
The meeting commended the relevant authorities and travel agencies and the Ministry of Tourism CLMV for their efforts in developing the CLV-DTA tourism development plan for 2020-2025 and the vision for 2030 adopted at the 11th CLV Summit on Development Triangle on December 9, 2022 via video.
The CLMV Minister of Tourism has approved the CLMV Tourism Cooperation Action Plan 2023-2025, continuing to focus on promoting the "four countries, one destination", covering 1. Travel facilitation 2. Capacity building 3. Participation from Private sector and local communities 4. Cooperation with third parties and 5. Ensuring sustainable and responsible tourism.
The meeting also approved the joint declaration of the 6th Cambodia-Laos-Myanmar-Vietnam Tourism Ministers' Meeting.
The CLMV Minister of Tourism commended and thanked Cambodia for hosting the 6th CLMV Ministerial Meeting on Tourism and the 5th ECMEC Ministerial Meeting on Tourism.
The 7th CLMV Senior Officials and Tourism Ministers' Meeting will be held in Myanmar in 2024.
CSX CEO: The effect of rising interest rates hinders securities trading in the market
Hong Sohour, Royal Government Delegate in charge of CSX, told Fresh News that in addition to public securities, the continued rise in global interest rates has also put pressure on private securities trading in Cambodia. The company that plans to issue bonds must set up a mechanism to ensure the successful issuance of securities.
He added, however, that the issue did not completely stop him from expecting more companies to list and issue securities in 2023.
"Admittedly, there have been some setbacks due to global interest rates, but companies can not wait for interest rates to fall, so it could take years," he said. "Before it goes down, this is a turning point for business owners who need money to learn to live with it."
Mr. Hong Sohour has said in the past that he is optimistic that securities trading on the Cambodia Securities Exchange will reach $ 1 million a day next year after a two-year period of good growth. This is because in 2022, the trading volume will increase to about 600,000 dollars per day.
It should be informed that at present, the Cambodia Securities Exchange has received 17 listed companies. Eight companies have been listed on the bond, while nine others, including Royal Railways owned by Kith Meng, have just been officially listed on October 31, 2022. CSX expects to have a new listed company by the end of 2022.
