Russia agrees to re-join agreement with Ukraine on grain exports (Video inside) (Moscow): Russia's Defense Ministry on Wednesday announced that Moscow has decided to rejoin the agreement reached. Under the coordination of Turkey and the United Nations (UN) on Ukraine grain exports through the Black Sea. This was released by the news agency RT on Wednesday, October 3, 2022.
In a statement from its Defense Ministry, Russia said the decision to rejoin the agreement came after receiving a written guarantee from Kiev that Ukraine would not use the security corridors provided by Russia. By the Russian side for military purposes.
The statement also thanked Turkey and the UN for their efforts to secure the commitments made by Ukraine. The decision to suspend Moscow's grain export agreement was announced last week after the Russian military accused Ukraine of using security corridors to launch drone strikes on the port city of Sevastopol. Crimea.
In July, Turkey and the UN reached an agreement between Moscow and Kiev to reopen grain exports from a Ukrainian port in the Black Sea after the outbreak of war. So far, about 10 million tons of food have been exported under the agreement.
Environmental cleaners ask tourists visiting Angkor to dispose of garbage properly
(Siem Reap): The Apsara Authority, as well as environmental cleaners in the Angkor resort area, has asked tourists visiting this large tourist resort to dispose of their garbage properly.
APSARA Authority said that although the current awareness of garbage as well as the tourists is better, but there are still a few cases that are not good enough to require the necessary participation. Manage garbage as well as environmental issues in the temple area of Angkor.
Ms. Kochot, an environmental cleaning agency in front of Angkor Wat, said that the most common waste today is the leaves, which require daily cleaning. In addition to this type of rubbish, there are also a small amount of plastic rubbish and bags that guests do not keep well in the bins, she suggested that tourists visiting the Angkor resort to cooperate for a clean environment.
While cutting grass in front of Angkor Wat, in front of Angkor Wat temple, another environmental cleaning agency, Ms. Yun Chanthy, also mentioned the case of plastic garbage that tourists do not keep well. Most of the plastic litter contains foam plates and straws that are thrown on the street and outside the bins, and sometimes torn by dogs all over the garden.
The agency urges tourists who visit the temple site of Angkor should have a good attitude to take care of the environment together to attract more tourists to visit Siem Reap.
However, travel agencies also observe the good behavior of most tourists who have cooperated to properly store garbage and the participation of vendors who always pack well after eating. Nowadays, there is no more selling in the grasslands, mostly in the cafeterias, which improves the management of garbage in the temples.
