On that occasion, the meeting listened to the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the occasion of the 5th ECMEC Ministerial Meeting on Tourism. After listening to this topic, Minister Thong Khon, Chairman of the meeting, stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has a deep vision on ECMEC tourism.
Minister Thong Khon and other ECEM member tourism ministers welcomed the increase in international tourists in the country to about 10 million in the first nine months of 2022, of which 4.8 million were domestic tourists. 49% of the total number of international tourists. ECM member tourism ministers have called for the integration of tourism products and the participation of the private sector to further attract tourists.
Minister Thong Khon and other ECEM member tourism ministers supported the establishment of a joint venture package from the private sector in the ECMEC region and encouraged national and international airlines to expand more direct flights between tourist destinations in the country. Long-distance destinations are also agreed to connect tourist destinations by sea and river.
The Minister of Tourism of ECMEC encourages the further strengthening of tourism cooperation among ECMEC member countries to ensure that ECMEC remains competitive and becomes a single, safe and warm destination. The meeting reaffirmed that safety, hygiene and resilience should increase awareness and expand the implementation of all tourism activities.
The Ministers of Tourism of the ECMEC member countries agreed to continue to enhance cooperation on the diversification of tourism products, including community-based tourism, ecotourism, adventure tourism, sporting events, tourism, health tourism, food tourism, and also agreed to promote tourism policy. Responsibly aim to create favorable conditions for product development and tourism business.
At the same time, the Minister of Tourism ECMEC has set out a cooperation framework to support small and medium enterprises (MSME) as the backbone for sustainable and responsible development.
Minister Thong Khon and other ECEM Tourism Ministers encouraged the exchange of experiences on the digital revolution in tourism, such as digital literacy training programs, the development of digital skills and the use of digital technologies to increase productivity and competitiveness.
ECMIC Minister of Tourism recognized the importance and supported the initiative to study the feasibility of establishing ECEM Tourism Secretariat or Office in 2023 and 2024.
The ECMEC Minister of Tourism agreed on the Siem Reap Declaration on the Future of ECMEC Tourism and also acknowledged the outcome of the first ACMECS / CLMV Tourism Dialogue held on the afternoon of November 2, 2022. Continue to support this program for sustainable tourism development, environment and resilience in the region.
The 6th ECEM Senior Officials and Tourism Minister Meeting will be held in Laos in 2024.
