This statement was made by Prof. Mam Bunheng on the occasion of presiding over the 8th Kantha Bopha International Conference, which was attended by Dr. René Schwarzenbach, President of the Kantha Bopha Swiss Foundation and Dr. John Narith, Under Secretary of State for the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Secretariat. Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, together with more than 400 doctors, nurses and nurses, on November 3, 2022 at Jayavarman VII Hospital, Siem Reap.
The first Kantha Bopha International Conference was held in 2004 in the spirit of promoting the medical profession on a regular basis to exchange medical experience between Cambodian doctors and well-known professors from the Children's Hospital of the University of Zurich, Switzerland. But it was interrupted for two years due to the global epidemic of Kovid-19.
Topics of the 8th Kantha Bopha International Conference focused on 1: Infant care, 2: Pediatric emergency care, 3: Experience in managing Kovid-19 patients at Kantha Bopha Hospital and at Children's Hospital, Switzerland And 4: Technical updates on pediatrics.
The Minister of Health conveyed the greetings and high praise of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to all the staff of Kantha Bopha Hospital who have taken care to provide child care services with high professionalism, despite In the circumstances of the Kovid-19 outbreak.
The Minister emphasized that in 1992, Kantha Bopha Hospital had only one location and 60 beds, but now the hospital has 5 locations with a total of 2,088 beds and 2,499 staff. Professionalism and ethics.
The President of the Foundation also expressed his deepest gratitude to His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King of Cambodia and His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia and the Royal Government of Cambodia for supporting the operation of Kantha Bopha Hospital and their commitment to continue to support the Fund. Kantha Bopha Switzerland and calls on the Swiss government to continue to support Kantha Bopha Hospital.
