Commentary: China and Vietnam, which are friendly as brothers, should be good and harmonious neighbors forever
The world is currently in a state of turmoil and change. How to develop Sino-Vietnamese relations to another level? Xi Jinping, secretary-general of the CPC Central Committee, said the two sides should adhere to the forward direction of socialism, strengthen the foundations of the socialist economy and promote traditional ties.
From an economic point of view, China and Vietnam are important economic and trade cooperation partners. China has maintained Vietnam's position as Vietnam's largest trading partner for several consecutive years, while Vietnam is China's largest trading partner among ASEAN countries and the world's sixth largest trading partner. By 2021, the bilateral trade volume will reach 200 billion US dollars.
China and Vietnam are neighbors with an interconnected territory and have been maintaining traditional friendship as a brotherhood. Under the new circumstances, China and Vietnam will continue to take turns and promote the traditional friendship, adding to the inexhaustible momentum in the development of bilateral relations.
Looking to the future, China and Vietnam will adhere to the strategic guidance of the two leaders' top leaders, as well as provide a new era to the traditional friendship between the two countries, which will definitely boost relations between the two countries. To reach a new level for sure.
