Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi advises private security agencies not to be involved in any kind of crime, especially drug offenses
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, on November 2, 2022, instructed and reminded all private security agencies not to be involved in any kind of crime, especially drug offenses. That is to be an important support force to the authorities to participate in the prevention, suppression and suppression of crimes.
He claimed that in the past, the General Commission of the National Police, which has the Department of Private Security Management as its staff, has been taking care to ensure that all private security agencies have the capacity, professional knowledge, and ethics to promote this sector. Continuing to grow and come to receive training in this skill to gain the trust of the target that they stand.
The Deputy Commissioner of the National Police stressed that the private security agencies must establish cooperation with the authorities and local authorities by being good citizens and good people and an important support force for the competent authorities to cooperate well and respond promptly. Time. Especially when you see or suspect any illegal activities, you must immediately report to the competent authorities or come to the department to prevent and suppress crimes in a timely manner.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi also instructed the private security agents to have a proper attitude in participating in the work by adhering to what is right after training to respect the qualifications of the private security agents, that is, discipline, ethics. Use adequate private security uniforms and equipment.
According to the Director of the Department of Affairs, this refresher course is aimed at meeting the need to increase the capacity to become a qualified and qualified private security agent for participation in the maintenance and protection of security, safety and order. And the lives of the people, as well as to improve the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
