Three suspects in an unmarked car stopped in front of a hair salon and went to put some sedatives, money and property in Svay Rieng City.
(Svay Rieng): Three suspects in an unknown car stopped in front of a hair salon and put some sedatives, money and a large amount of property on November 1, 2022 at Phanna Salon in the village. Chambok, Sangkat Chek, Svay Rieng City.
According to the police, the owner of the shop was named Koy Sophana, a 36-year-old female, the owner of Phanna Salon lived in the village where the incident took place. The missing items included $ 17,500, two platinum rings weighing six ounces, one and a half gram platinum bracelets and one gold earring.
After receiving the money and jewelry, the suspects drove out of the shop and then he regained consciousness and was shocked.
Police said that the victim's family was later sent to Svay Rieng Provincial Referral Hospital because of abnormal symptoms after being sedated by the suspects. Local authorities are making notes and questioning the owner to investigate. Find the suspect and take legal action. The Ministry of Health announces the results of research to understand the use of rapid test for Kovid-19 among people living with HIV and the general population.
