Five ECM countries launch tourism restoration plan
The launch of the action plan took place during the 5th Meeting of ECMEC Senior Officials under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Rathsak, Director General of Tourism Development and International Cooperation of the Ministry of Tourism on the morning of November 2, 2022 at Borey Angkor Hotel. Siem Reap.
Mr. Try Chhiv, Director of the Department of International and ASEAN Cooperation of the Ministry of Tourism and also the representative of Cambodia, said that the Minister of Tourism ECMEC has assessed the impact of the Kovid-19 crisis on tourism in the region. As an ECM member, they traveled more and more together during the Kovid-19 crisis.
Mr. Try Chhiv said that during the 5th Meeting of ECEM Tourism Ministers, Director General Thong Rathsak, together with ECEM Tourism Minister, put together a joint plan to promote more internal tourism movement and launched Strategies for the restoration and development of tourism in the region under the campaign "Five countries, one goal" in accordance with the action plan 2023-2025.
Mr. Try Chhiv further stated that in order to accelerate the implementation of the above action plan, the Chief Minister of Tourism has set some implementation directions, such as:
1. Promote the development of new products in the region, such as rural tourism, community tourism, ecotourism, adventure tourism, food tourism and health and comfort tourism.
2. Increase joint promotion, support each other in organizing tourism events and promote ECMEC internal tourism.
4. Strengthen the exchange of tourism information to monitor and evaluate the effectiveness of mutual cooperation.
5. Promote institutional mechanisms by examining the feasibility of establishing an ECM Secretariat or Coordinating Office.
6. Promote the connection of tourist routes in the ECMEC area by land, air and water.
He added that the high-level meeting also discussed the Declaration on the Future of ECMEC Tourism, a compass for strengthening ECMEC and other relevant partners to develop better regional tourism in line with the post-Kovid 19 context. Variable, especially tourists like to travel short distances.
"These action plans will attract more local ecotourism, create more jobs and contribute to the development of local people," he said.
It should be informed that after the 5th ECEM Tourism Minister Meeting, there will also be the CLMV Senior Officials Meeting including Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam led by the Lao side to prepare for the 5th ECEM Tourism Minister Meeting and The 6th CLMV Ministerial Meeting on November 3, 2022 tomorrow.
