70th Brigade 711 Rescue Team Ready for Disaster Relief Operation
(Phnom Penh): Lieutenant General Soy Narith, Deputy Commander of the 70th Brigade, said that the 711 Disaster Search and Rescue Operations Unit of the 70th Brigade was ready and ready for the disaster relief mission. Eventually, according to the orders of the leaders to serve the well-being of the people.
Statement by Major General Soy Narith in front of the media on November 1, 2022 after the National Disaster Management Day at the Koh Pich Convention Center in the presence of Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
Lt. Gen. Soy Narith said that the 711 Disaster Search and Rescue Task Force was established in 2005 after carrying out rescue operations on firefighting, traffic accidents, building collapses, rescuing victims from caves, etc. .
Lt. Gen. Soy Narith said that after the National Committee for Disaster Management organized the establishment of up to 16 disaster relief units, 711 Disaster Search and Rescue Operations was included in the operation. National Committee for Disaster Management to participate in rescue activities for the affected people.
Lt. Gen. Soy Narith confirmed that the 711 Disaster Search and Rescue Task Force has received human and material training from JPR of Japan, trained in emergency and firefighting skills by trainers. Japan, as in the case of car crashes, car fires and the rescue of victims by helicopter.
