The Prime Minister of Saudi Arabia has sent a message of thanks to Senior Minister Osman Hassan for congratulating him on his appointment as Prime Minister of Saudi Arabia.
(Saudi Arabia): Prince Mohammed Pin Salman al-Saud, Crown Prince and Prime Minister of Saudi Arabia, has sent a message of thanks to Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Mission, as Cambodia's Special Envoy to the Islamic Cooperation Organization. (OIC) sent a congratulatory message on the occasion of his appointment as Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia on September 27, 2022.
The above letter of thanks was given by Prince Mohammed Pin Salman al-Saud to Dr. Osman Hassan on October 24, 2022.
Saudi Arabia is one of 57 countries that are members of the Organization of Islamic Cooperation (OIC), the second largest organization in the world after the United Nations (UN). Gulf Operation (GCC), a political and economic alliance of six Middle Eastern countries. It is also one of the 22 countries in the Arab League.
Saudi Arabia also has good cooperative relations with Cambodia, and in the past the country has often sent delegations to visit Cambodia. Saudi Arabia also has its own embassy in Cambodia, currently residing in Hanoi, Vietnam, and in the near future, Saudi Arabia will also have its embassy in Cambodia to be based in Phnom Penh.
