Please be informed that Kathina is a traditional Buddhist festival that Cambodians start after the rainy season. Kathin festival is always paraded in all temples from the 1st day of the lunar month to the 15th day of the lunar month, no pagoda is missed. If the temple does not have any Kathin, the temple must also be prepared as a pagoda Kathin.
The Kathin procession to each temple is celebrated with great rejoicing, and the initiators always prepare the Kathina equipment, such as the trichivor, the monks, the deities, and other offerings such as the bottom of the plate, the knife, the needle, the needle, the guard bag and the umbrella. They marched to the designated temple. When they arrived at the pagoda, they did not immediately take the Kathin into the temple, they kept the Kathin in a school that had already been prepared.
