"Samdech Techo emphasizes that Cambodia attaches importance to negotiations and peaceful solutions and hopes that all parties concerned will work for a comprehensive solution to end the war in Ukraine so that Ukraine can regain peace, stability, territorial integrity and development." . This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs on the results of the telephone meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the President of Ukraine.
In this meeting, the head of the Royal Government expressed his regret for the tragedy that has been happening in Ukraine. He also expressed concern over the recent attacks on Kiev and other cities in Ukraine, which have resulted in loss of life, many injuries and severe damage to civilian infrastructure, power outages and water shortages. Causing a severe energy and food crisis, as well as rising global inflation.
He also reiterated Cambodia's position on the war in Ukraine that Cambodia adheres to the principles enshrined in the UN Charter and international law against aggression, threats or the use of force over sovereignty and territorial integrity. Land of an independent state and does not support the separation of states or the invasion of territory from other countries.
The President expressed his deepest gratitude and appreciation to Cambodia for its support and co-founding of the UN General Assembly Resolutions and Cambodia's specific position on the Ukraine War.
He thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for the meeting and also warmly congratulated Cambodia on its success in chairing ASEAN in organizing the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings last August. I wish Cambodia more success in organizing the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits and related summits in November 2022.
