The Ministry of Environment actively participates in the implementation of the Royal Government's reform policy by providing support to sub-national administrations.
First, public administration reform; second, public financial reform; third, decentralization and deconcentration reform; and fourth, implement safe village, commune, and sangkat policies.
The Ministry of Environment has assigned 5 functions and 6 sub-functions and 26 activities for the municipal, district and khan administration. The five functions are: 1: Nature protection and conservation administration work, 2: Local community work, 3: Environmental protection work, which includes urban solid waste management and sewage and wastewater management. Wastewater, 4th: environmental knowledge and information work, and fifth: sustainable development.
In order to implement these functions effectively and successfully, the Ministry of Environment has not only transferred the functions, but also transferred financial resources and the transfer of additional human and technical resources. Since 2015, there has been a transfer of financial resources, which is the municipal sanitation budget of 8 billion riels per year and the budget for staff and administrative causes of 3,217 million riels per year.
In addition, the Ministry of Environment provided technical equipment, including: 230 water purifiers, 118 tuk-tuks, 48 garbage trucks, 54 incinerators.
