Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked Duke Try Pheap for donating rice and funds for disaster relief work
(Phnom Penh): On behalf of the staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his deep gratitude to Tycoon Try Pheap, General Director of Try Pheap Group for donating rice and funds to help deal with disaster work with the Royal Government. Government.
Duke Try Pheap and Duke Kien Srey Neang have fully supported the Royal Government in resolving this difficult issue. Duke Try Pheap and Duke Kien Srey Neang donated a total of 1,175 tons of rice to Samdech Techo to distribute to people in need.
On Tuesday afternoon, November 1, 2022, General Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions and First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, brought a letter of thanks to Duke Try Pheap directly.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Senior Minister expressed his deep gratitude for the humanitarian gestures of the Duke. The Senior Minister considered this gesture to be invaluable in the humanitarian framework and also a noble gesture of solidarity.
On the occasion of handing over the letter of thanks, Duke Try Pheap also donated about 20,000 USD to the National Committee for Disaster Management to set up a search and rescue unit for victims who drowned in the sea, river or lake.
