Chbar Ampov District Administration Celebrates National Environment Day on November 23, 2022 under the Theme of Our Homeland Clean and Green
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Cheng Monira, Governor of Chbar Ampov District, on the morning of November 1, 2022, presided over the National Environment Day, November 23, 2022 under the theme "Our Homeland is Clean and Green" held at Boeung Chhouk Market. Flood-affected areas in O'Andong 1 village, Sangkat Prek Pra, Khan Chbar Ampov.
Speaking on the occasion of the National Environment Day, Mr. Cheng Monira, District Governor, said that the organization and participation of this important day on the occasion is a reflection of the joint efforts and contribution to the environmental cause, it will Become a driving force that promotes the initiation of environmentally friendly activities, contributes to making our planet clean, green and beautiful, healthy and well-being for everyone.
The purpose of organizing this National Environment Day is:
First, in public places, Khan and Sangkat administrations must take measures to clean up in public places regularly by cleaning and collecting garbage from the streets, riverbanks, parks, markets and planting more trees on the streets. Its basis.
Second, all public institutions, schools, pagodas, hospitals, please manage to clean and clean both inside and outside the premises by collecting garbage and solid waste properly in accordance with the 4Rs to ensure a good working environment and beauty.
Third, factories, enterprises, handicrafts, businesses must clean and clean both inside and around their locations and must educate staff, workers, food sellers and transporters about the proper management of garbage and solid waste.
Fourth, resorts, entertainment centers, restaurants and canteens must be hygienic on a regular basis to ensure the beauty, comfort and pleasure of providing leisure and tourism services by collecting garbage. Solid waste in order. Enough trash and transport on time.
Fifth: Housing: Local authorities in villages, communes and sangkats must instruct people to clean the environment in their homes according to their ownership by cleaning, collecting and storing solid waste in accordance with the actual situation of each locality and in accordance with Guidance of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration in order to ensure the quality of the environment, beauty and hygiene.
At the end, the Governor requested you, civil servants and members of the whole ceremony to clean up the environment everywhere to make Cambodia and the world more beautiful, reduce the use of plastic bags and waste management. That's right.
