Senior Minister Kun Kim calls on partner organizations and philanthropists to continue to support as much as possible to address the affected people
(Phnom Penh): General Kun Kim, Senior Minister, First Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, called on both national and international partner organizations and philanthropists to continue to join the Royal Government in providing material and financial resources to solve problems for the people. Victims of various disasters.
Senior Minister Kun Kim said that in order to express the will and commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia in accordance with the SANDY Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction adopted in 2015 in order to achieve this goal.
He also expressed his pleasure at the presence of you to participate in disaster risk reduction activities to avoid damage, loss of life, property, environment and disruption to the process of social and economic development, which is a great contribution to Enhancing community resilience to disasters.
Senior Minister Kun Kim confirmed that in 2022, Cambodia suffered from floods in 25 capitals and provinces, equal to 133 cities, districts and 606 communes, and affected a total of 158,064 families evacuated. 5,676 families were affected, 219,577 hectares of rice fields were damaged and 120,167 hectares were damaged, 75,328 hectares of mixed crops were affected and 35,986 hectares were damaged, as well as many other public and private infrastructures.
The senior minister said that with the high attention from the Royal Government, the emergency response was carried out in a timely and effective manner by all capital-provincial authorities, all kinds of forces, ministries, institutions, Cambodian Red Cross, national and international development partners. And the private sector under the coordination of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
Past disasters have damaged irrigation systems, bridges, roads, school buildings, hospitals, etc. Which needs to be rehabilitated, especially to ensure food security for the people in the affected areas. The Ministry of National Defense, through the 70th Brigade, has been actively involved in helping people affected by disasters in the capitals and provinces.
It should be noted that on the occasion of celebrating the National Day for Disaster Management on October 13, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, stated that in order for the future disaster management work to be successful, Samdech Techo called for 9 points. Contains:
