Minister of Environment urges subordinate units and the National Council for Sustainable Development to continue to pay attention to the implementation of eight priority tasks
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, urged the units under the Ministry of Environment and the National Council for Sustainable Development to continue their efforts and pay special attention to the implementation of eight priority tasks.
The Minister of Environment made such a call at the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the results of environmental work in 2022 and work direction in 2023 on the afternoon of November 1, 2022, after a day and a half.
The Minister of Environment expressed his appreciation and appreciation to all the leaders and civil servants, park rangers who have made great efforts to serve the motherland in the cause of the environment and natural resources.
Mr. Say Sam Al requested all units under the Ministry of Environment and the National Council for Sustainable Development to continue their efforts and pay special attention to the implementation of some of the following priority tasks:
First, continue to strengthen modern administration and expand financial sustainability in a way that responds to the actual social and economic context of Cambodia, national environmental priorities, as well as global trends.
Second, continue to strengthen and sharpen appropriate and feasible policies and strategies, especially in response to the priorities of climate change, biodiversity conservation and low-carbon and sustainable development.
Third, continue to strengthen environmental protection to ensure a good environment and a clean village, which is the basis for supporting better life and public health for all people and all generations.
Fourth, continue to strengthen the management of protected areas to maintain the richness of natural resources and biodiversity, services, ecosystem services and sustainable local economic development.
Fifth, continue to develop local communities to become belts to protect natural resources and support the local economy
Sixth, continue to promote environmental education to raise people's awareness and responsibility for the environment, the spirit of "Cambodia, my motherland" and strengthen the close ties between people and nature.
Seventh, continue to promote cooperation in international relations and environmental diplomacy in the interests of Cambodia.
And 8th: Continue to promote the work of gender, youth, women and children to ensure environmental prosperity and social harmony.
