Mr. Van Him, a veteran in Treal commune, Tang Kork district, Kampong Thom province, received a new house from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit and vowed to support Samdech Techo after his death.
Mr. Van Him confirmed that he was 61 years old and joined the police force at Kampong Thom Provincial Police in 1993 and was retired by the Ministry of Interior in 2018. He is survived by his wife and five children, who raise livestock and grow crops to supplement their daily living, combined with the state's monthly salary.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun stated that seeing that his life was difficult and he could not afford to build a suitable house on his own, the committee of the Kampong Thom Cambodian Veterans Association asked for a decision to build a house for him now. The back of the 220th house, built high above the ground, concrete pillars, steel bones, planks, boards, smart walls, corrugated iron roofs and corrugated stairs.
During the handover ceremony, Lt. Gen. Som Sun brought the gifts of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet and Ms. Pech Chanmony to give him more, including: 50 kg of rice, 2 boxes of noodles, 2 cans of fish sauce, 2 cans of fish sauce. Two cans and some kitchen utensils, as well as money for him to deal with daily life.
Mr. Van Him and his family would like to express their deepest gratitude and best wishes to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as Mr. Hun Manet and Mrs. Hun Sen and the Committee of the Kampong Thom Cambodian Veterans Association. Meet only the five blessings of the Buddha, do not be lazy and determined to continue to support Samdech Techo Hun Sen until the end of life.
