(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 1, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the graduation ceremony for more than 6,000 students of the Royal University of Law and Economics (RULE). Successful graduation.
According to the university, more than 97% of the graduates are employed, of which more than 96% are undergraduates and almost 100% are undergraduates.
Please note that the Royal University of Law and Economics is a university that has been playing an important role in training human resources in law, economics, and other areas to serve the economic and social development in Cambodia.
From 1993 to the present, the university has sent 1,759 students to study abroad for master's and doctoral degrees through partner universities. In the academic year 2021-2022, the university sent 46 students (31 females) to study abroad and sent 10 students to participate in 10 exchange programs (5 females) in France, Japan and Indonesia.
In addition, 24 students participated in eight online international remote fiction competitions related to international law. At the beginning of 2023, the university is ready to send 30 students to participate in 10 more international fiction competitions.
