Together, give a smile to the students! Students of the Royal School of Administration provide study materials to students and food to the people in Chhouk district
(Kampot): In order to cultivate humanitarian activities and contribute to help people in poor communities, the 2022 Senior Officials Training Course at Nokor Phnom level of the Royal School of Administration has been active in rural areas.
On Sunday, October 31, the trainees of the 2022 Senior Officials Training Course at Nokor Phnom level continued their activities in Taken Commune, Chhouk District, Kampot Province to provide study materials to students and some food items to the people.
Social work activities under the theme: "Promoting the environment and rural education" were organized by the training staff of 2022 senior officials of Nokor Phnom level of the Royal School of Administration, 72 people from various institutions. Each.
This humanitarian program is led by Mr. Youk Bunna, Permanent Secretary of State and Director of the Royal School of Administration of the Ministry of Public Works. The event was also attended by the management team of civil servants of the Royal School of Administration and the internship of senior officials in 2022 Nokor Phnom level of the Royal School of Administration, local authorities, citizens and many students.
This humanitarian activity brought some study materials including bags, books, pens, pencils and some funds to distribute to a total of 453 students from 3 primary schools, including: Trapeang Run Primary School, Phnom Treal Primary School and Teuk Thla Primary School. At the same time, the 72 trainees of Nokor Phnom class also donated 300 saplings to the above 3 primary schools to improve the environment.
In addition to helping to improve the environment and educate the trainees of the Nokor Phnom class, they also brought food, rice, fish sauce, soy sauce and medicine to 120 needy families living in the area.
Mr. Un Savorn, Representative of the 2022 Senior Officials Training Course at Nokor Phnom Level, expressed his interest that all past humanitarian activities and acts and social work through the social work activities of the Royal School of Administration have cultivated the spirit of unity, patriotism and patriotism. Motherland loves the people and loves learning.
The Royal School of Administration has not only trained the capital, intellectuals and trainees to train their trainees, but also to help the needy people and students in remote rural areas. This activity is to contribute to the improvement of livelihoods and the development and training of human resources with the Royal Government.
All trainees of the 2022 Senior Officials Training Course at Nokor Phnom level of the Royal School of Administration expressed their happiness for contributing to social work and philanthropy to help local people in need and contributing to the promotion of education. In the countryside, especially young children, who are the nation's bamboo shoots.
It should be noted that the internship of senior officials in 2022 Nokor Phnom level of the Royal School of Administration has already participated in many social activities. He has already participated in social work with the leaders of the Royal School of Administration four times in Kirirom, Kampong Speu, Siem Reap and Changkrang commune, Chit Borey district, Kratie province.
The Phnom Penh Senior Civil Servants 2022 Vocational Training Internship has donated $ 15,000 to the Royal School of Administration to participate in the construction of Trapeang Treang Primary School in Trapeang Treang Village, Changkrang Commune, Chit Borei District, Kratie Province.
