(Phnom Penh): Colonel Toch Kimsong, Chief of Police of Russey Keo Sangkat Administration Post, on behalf of Sangkat Chief Moul Vireak and Colonel Heang Tharet, District Inspector, led a team to visit and support food and money to alleviate the burden of living. Some to Cambodian veterans living in Po Sen Chey district (former residents of Sangkat Russey Keo) on the morning of October 31, 2022.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association on June 17, 2022, issued a statement in seven messages on the 15th anniversary of the 21st Cambodian Veterans Day. June 2022.
In the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the 15th anniversary of the Cambodian Veterans Day, he called for the following:
First, Cambodian Veterans, please continue to maintain the spirit of great heroism and dignity as the outstanding citizens of the motherland to continue to be a good example in the society. The Royal Government and the people of Cambodia throughout the country will always remember the great sacrifices and merits of all veterans for our beloved homeland.
Second: All Ministries, Institutions, Units and Local Authorities at All Levels Must Organize Delegates to Visit Local Veterans and Veterans, Especially Veterans in the Armed Forces, Sisters, Veterans, and Veterans Hospitals and people with disabilities at military centers for the disabled to encourage and connect emotionally with veterans and female veterans.
Third, the Ministry of Information must introduce the public and private media to help disseminate the Royal Government's circular and message on the occasion of the 15th anniversary of the Cambodian Veterans Day, as well as achievements related to the field of veterans to the national and international public. Infiltrate more broadly.
Fourth, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation must continue to implement well and effectively provide social security services for veterans and veterans' families through the National Veterans Fund throughout the country. On the other hand, the Ministry must strive to promote the implementation of housing projects for veterans and their families, as included in the Royal Government's public investment plan.
Fifth, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation shall cooperate with the relevant ministries and institutions to continue to promote the implementation of the policy on the provision of social land concessions to the former Armed Forces and their families more effectively.
Sixth, relevant ministries, institutions, local authorities and the armed forces of all kinds must be involved in supporting veterans, especially to pay attention to supporting the families of veterans who are experiencing difficulties.
Seventh, the Cambodian Veterans Association at all levels must continue to strengthen and expand the activities of the Association in the spirit of the decision of the Second General Assembly of the Cambodian Veterans Association.
The Cambodian Veterans Association must continue to play a central role in promoting the role of veterans in society and encourage veterans to adhere to the spirit of solidarity and mutual support, and to actively participate in the race movement. 3 Excellent for the benefit of the brothers and the nation.
Please be informed that June 21, 2022 is the proudest historical day that veterans and people all over Cambodia celebrate the 15th anniversary of Cambodian Veterans Day to commemorate the heroic heroism and great merits. Of heroes, warriors of the armed forces and people of all walks of life who have bravely sacrificed their lives for the cause of our beloved motherland.
