(Siem Reap): The National Bank of Cambodia, in collaboration with the Banking Association of Cambodia and the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, on October 31, 2022, organized a dissemination workshop on ASEAN Savings Day, with the theme this year saving less than not saving at In Siem Reap. This ASEAN Savings Day is held annually on October 31.
Mr. Yun Linne, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, encouraged people to increase the practice of saving, especially saving with official financial institutions to get benefits as well as avoid risks. Mr. Yun Linne also called on people to start cultivating microfinance savings habits to achieve more effective financial management.
This program will further promote the culture of saving, which will help improve savings mobilization and better financial management among Cambodians. Saving is really important to take care of and participate effectively, because saving can help alleviate the urgent needs in the future, and in particular contribute to better daily financial management. .
According to Mr. Sok Voeun, by the end of 2021, the number of customer deposit accounts will increase to 12.1 million, with a deposit balance of approximately 157 trillion riels, equivalent to 38.5 billion US dollars, an increase of 15 , 4% The increase in the number of accounts and the balance of deposits reflects the financial awareness of the people, especially the understanding of the importance of savings.
