The Financial Technology Forum will be held at the Cambodia Technology Fair 2022 from November 11-13.
(Phnom Penh): Accompanying the ASEAN Summit, the Royal Government of Cambodia has authorized the Ministry of Industry, Science and Innovation to organize the Cambodia Technology Fair 2022 from 11 to 13 November 2022 at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center, which includes a number of forums. 4, which includes the Financial Technology Forum (Building B). This is according to the announcement received by Fresh News.
At the same time, another important purpose of this forum is to continue to collect good and specific inputs in the process of drafting a policy for the development of Cambodia's financial technology sector that is sharp and flexible.
The forum will be attended by the leaders of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Committee on Economy and Digital Business, National Bank of Cambodia, the new business training center "Techo", the Association of the Federation of Finance and Technology of Cambodia, banking institutions, microfinance institutions, educational institutions, research institutions, development partners. As well as other relevant associations and institutions in the private sector.
(Phnom Penh): On Tuesday morning, November 1, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will preside over the graduation ceremony for more than 6,000 students of the Royal University of Law and Economics (RULE) after They graduated successfully.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister always gives value and honor to the students who have successfully graduated and always gives the honor of presiding over the graduation ceremony for them. For the Royal University of Law and Economics, Samdech Techo has already presided over about 18 times.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, said that a total of 6,307 students (3,088 females) will be graduating tomorrow. There are 4,664 undergraduate students, 2,528 females and 1,643 undergraduate students, 560 females.
General Soeng Samnang awarded medals to 13 Air Force members to retirement age in return for national merits
(Phnom Penh): Thirteen Air Force officers have reached retirement age. With the retirement of the 13 Air Force members, General Soeng Samnang, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Air Force, organized a get-together program and presented medals to honor them for their merits. They have filled the nation.
The ceremony was held on the morning of October 31, 2022 at the Air Force Base under the presidency of General Soeng Samnang. The event was also attended by 225 Deputy Commanders, Deputy Commissioners, Air Force Base Commanders, officers of the Air Force Command, and 13 retired soldiers.
The retired soldiers include two lieutenant generals, three brigadier generals, two colonels, four lieutenants colonels, one brigadier general and one lieutenant colonel.
General Soeng Samnang, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Air Force, clarified the law on the implementation of pensions and disability pensions for both types of soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
General Soeng Samnang continued that despite the retirement age of military officers, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces still maintains the main military force with military resources to share good experiences with officers in accordance with the Royal Government's policy. Keep the old, create the new as an effective policy.
The Air Force Commander also did not forget to recall the values and merits of retired soldiers who contributed to the overthrow and prevent the return of the genocidal regime. In particular, join the end of the civil war and the successful implementation of the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
General Soeng Samnang recommended to remind retired soldiers to believe in the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the wise leader of Cambodia in finding peace, freedom and sustainable development. On the other hand, have a good relationship with the local authorities and take care of health care, prevent the spread of various diseases and hurry to complete the pension application.
The Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX) officially listed the Royal Company's corporate bonds for tycoon Kith Meng
(Phnom Penh): As of October 31, 2022, the Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX) has 17 listed companies, of which 9 companies are listed as shares and 8 are listed as corporate bonds. This was confirmed by Mr. Hong Sohour, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the General Director of the Cambodia Securities Exchange during the official registration ceremony of the Royal Railway Securities Company Limited on October 31, 2022.
In addition, the number of listed companies selling corporate bonds has steadily increased as the company has acquired low-cost, long-term sources of capital and even received tax incentives from the Royal Government to increase its reputation. Its presence in national and international markets has attracted the attention of potential business partners and gained the trust of customers, investors and the general public.
Mr. Hong Sohour praised the participation of Duke Kith Meng who has participated in the development of the securities market in Cambodia in the past and also hoped that under the leadership of Duke Kith Meng could bring other subsidiaries to work. Raise capital through the securities market by issuing and listing as equity securities or bonds.
He also encouraged business owners to consider the possibility of issuing shares that not only capitalize on the company but also create value for the business and attractiveness of the business among investors.
Ministry of Education sends 92 senior officials to study essential subjects at Royal School of Administration
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has sent a total of 92 senior civil servants under its supervision from the Deputy Director of the Department to the Director General to attend training courses at the Royal School of Administration, focusing on general administration, public administration reform program. Reforms and other necessary subjects are an important part of good governance and the backbone of deep state reform.
The opening ceremony of this training course was held on the morning of October 31, 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Youk Bunna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Director of the Royal School of Administration (represented by Mr. Prum Sokha) and Mr. Nath Bunroeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. Representative of Mr. Hang Chuon Naron) at the co-educational hall of the Royal School of Administration.
Deputy Director Ngey Thoeun continued that this training course lasts for 120 hours and lasts from November 1, 2022 to January 20, 2023 in order to strengthen the capacity of officials to suit the management needs. General Administration of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
At the same time, Mr. Nath Bunroeun said that the sending of senior civil servants of the Ministry of Education to receive additional training is to meet the requirements of human resource capacity to be in line with the policy "Cambodia is a middle-income country. High by 2030 and a developed country by 2050 "as well as to enhance human resource capacity in response to the Industrial Revolution 4.0, the development of information technology, society, economy, education revolution.
The Permanent Secretary of State said that the training program of civil servants of the Ministry of Education at the Royal School of Administration is focused on the necessary skills that are an important part of good governance and the backbone of deep state reform based on the Rectangular Strategic Plan. Fourth, the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He added that this training course will play an important role in supporting the implementation of the Rectangular Strategic Plan on the education sector, contributing to strengthening the capacity of officials, updating knowledge and changing the mindset, discipline, quality and virtue. And innovation for leaders and education officials to serve the people and improve the quality of education.
