Deposits in banking and financial institutions reached $ 41.5 billion as of August this year, officials encourage people to save more or less!
(Siem Reap): Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Assistant Governor and Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that as of August 2022, deposits in banking and financial institutions increased by 41.5 billion US dollars.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak's remarks were made during the ASEAN Savings Day 2022 under the theme "Saving less is better than not saving" held in Siem Reap on October 31, 2022.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak said, "As of August 2022, banking and financial institutions have continued to improve the financial environment, especially deposits, increased to 160.6 percent of GDP. 70.6 trillion riel or 41.5 billion US dollars, while the number of customer deposit accounts also increased by 14.3 million accounts, including 11.7 million accounts in commercial banks and 2.6 million accounts in institutions. "Microfinance accepts deposits."
He added that the banking and financial institution has expanded its operating system to a total of 2,593 branches and 4,219 ATMs in all capitals and provinces across the country, as well as diversified its financial products and services. Lots of stuff according to current needs and trends.
Mr. Sok Voeun, President of the Financial Association of Cambodia, confirmed that five microfinance institutions as of the third quarter of 2022 received a total of 4.7 billion US dollars from 2.6 million customers, of which is expected to deposit This will continue to grow through innovative services that are easy for people to use.
He said that saving is important to pay attention and participate effectively, because savings can facilitate the needs in emergencies in the future, especially to strengthen daily financial management. Improved.
"I encourage the public to continue and increase their savings habits, especially with official financial institutions, to benefit and avoid risks, and to start cultivating savings habits for children or young children as soon as possible," he said. It is possible for him to have this important life skill. ”
Dr. In Channy, Board Member of the Banking Association of Cambodia, said that the significant increase in customer deposits reflects the public's trust in the banking system in Cambodia.
Dr. encourages all citizens to use the savings service of the official banking institution, no matter how much or how little, it is better to save less than not save and save to get benefits such as interest rates, competition, security and protection from various risks. .
