Preah Vihear Governor Promotes Sustainable Blood Supply through "Club of Love"
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Vice President of the Central Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, and on the afternoon of October 29, 2022, donated blood to promote a sustainable blood supply by establishing a "Club of Justice". Sratbanh, Preah Vihear Province ”with the participation of the Deputy Governor, Departments and Units around the province, the three forces and the CPPCC from the eight districts of Preah Vihear province.
Mr. Kim Rithy said that blood donation saves many lives around the world, including hospitals in Preah Vihear need about 500 units of blood per year.
He said that blood from volunteers is not a sustainable source of blood supply because when patients need blood, sometimes no family donates blood or can not provide blood.
The provincial governor confirmed that voluntary blood donors are the only source of blood that can provide sustainable blood.
He also thanked the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in Preah Vihear for co-organizing this program and urged the provincial CPPCC to continue to organize this program every month, especially in the districts and departments. Volunteer Blood Donation Club of Love and can find about 500 units of blood per month to supply to the hospital in Preah Vihear province.
Mr. Kim Rithy also suggested that people in Preah Vihear province if they are interested in donating blood can go to donate blood at the Referral Hospital on 16 January. "Give blood, give love." Day 10 of the 2022 Voter List and Voter Registration: 138,492 Newly Registered Citizens
