(Phnom Penh): Cambodia will negotiate to open the Chinese market to export more Cambodian agricultural products such as pepper, fragrant coconut, turmeric, pineapple, pineapple, jackfruit and lotus seeds after officially exporting fresh Cambodian longan to Chinese market.
Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, at the inauguration ceremony of the official export of Cambodian fresh lentils to the Chinese market, stated that "in the future, Cambodia will open negotiations to open the Chinese market for "Exports other Cambodian agricultural products such as pepper, coconut, turmeric, durian products, pineapple, jackfruit and lotus seeds."
However, Dit Tina said that the Chinese market is still a potential market for Cambodia's agricultural exports, but Chinese investment in agriculture in Cambodia is still very low.
He pointed out that in 2021, Cambodia received only 70 million US dollars in Chinese investment, and for the first half of 2022, this figure has dropped to only 4 million US dollars, which requires more efforts to promote. To attract Chinese investors to invest in agriculture.
"The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries is warmly welcoming and ready to promote new cooperation and investment from China in agriculture for the mutual benefit of both countries," he said. "Two."
Speaking to Fresh News, Oknha Hun Lak, Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Rice Federation and exporter of bananas and mangoes to the Chinese market, confirmed that the agricultural products that Cambodia will negotiate with the Chinese market have all the potential. For the Chinese market.
Duke Hun Lak said that allowing the import of fresh produce into China, not only Cambodia, but other countries in the world is not easy, there are many conditions, especially with regard to technical barriers. So-called hygiene and phytosanitary.
According to the tycoon, the technical barrier requires time to study each other and to inspect for many years, but due to the positive development of Cambodian production, the Minister of Commerce and Agriculture of Cambodia. Enter a package requesting the head of government to negotiate in China.
He said that this is understandable and unique in allowing Cambodian products to be exported to China, but what Cambodia needs to do is to strengthen the quality, safety and compliance with Chinese hygiene and phytosanitary compliance standards.
In the first nine months of 2022, agricultural exports to China reached more than 580,000 tons, valued at more than 491 million US dollars.
According to agricultural export data recorded by the General Department of Agriculture in 2021, Cambodia exported more than 830,000 tons of agricultural products to China worth nearly 700 million US dollars.
Please be informed that so far, Cambodia's agricultural products that can be exported to China include: rice, dried cassava, cashew nuts, bananas, mangoes, lentils and trout. The longan fruit may be exported during the harvest season in November, while the trout is preparing export processing techniques. A fire broke out at a grocery store in Kambol district, destroying nearly $ 30,000 worth of equipment.
