Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Distributes Rice Seed and Food to More Than 6,000 Families in Prey Veng Province
(Prey Veng): On Sunday morning, October 30, 2022, tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will distribute rice seeds and food to 6,112 families in Prey Veng province.
Prey Veng is a province with high potential for rice cultivation and an area of nearly 340,000 hectares for farming. In that, the area of wet rice is up to 250,000 hectares. This province used to be the number one province in terms of rice yield.
During this year's rainy season, Prey Veng province was also affected by floods and the Mekong River.
Chea Somethy, Prey Veng provincial governor, said the floods affected 11 districts, 49 communes and 245 villages. Affects nearly 7,000 hectares of rice fields, equivalent to more than 7,000 families. The total damaged area is nearly 6,000 hectares, equivalent to more than 6,000 families. There are 9 districts that can be rehabilitated on an area of more than 5,000 hectares, equivalent to more than 6,000 families.
Please note that Prey Veng is the sixth province that Samdech Techo Prime Minister has invited to distribute rice seeds and food. The five provinces that Samdech Techo has already divided are Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Pursat, Kampong Chhnang and Kampong Thom.
The six provinces where Samdech Techo distributed rice seeds and food to farmers are the provinces most affected by the floods. The six provinces have a population of nearly 40,000 families, which Samdech Techo provided rice seeds to restore rice crops and provide food to solve difficulties in life.
