Last week, the ministry said it had asked the Central Bank of Vietnam to assist local fuel traders in obtaining foreign currency to pay for fuel imports.
He added that the central bank sold about $ 10 billion in foreign currency to oil importers, including two Vietnamese refineries, in the first nine months of this year. According to Reuters.
