For more details, please read the following announcement: Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin returns home after attending the 30th three-day APPF meeting in Thailand
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, this morning, Saturday, October 29, 2022, led a high-level delegation of the National Assembly to return home after attending the 30th meeting. Of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum (APPF) hosted by the Thai Parliament in Bangkok from October 26 to 28, 2022.
The 28-member Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum was initiated with the aim of convening an annual meeting of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Assembly to address common issues and promote regional and global peace and sustainable development.
At its 30th meeting, the APPF adopted 11 draft resolutions for legalizing the role of parliament and multilateralism in addressing emerging social, economic, security, and regional and global violence issues.
Please be informed that in this meeting, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin addressed the meeting, praising the Thai Parliament for organizing this important meeting at a time when the world needs economic recovery and Society is recovering after the Kovid 19 crisis and at a time when the world is facing many challenges, such as rising geopolitical tensions and security threats.
He urged the APPF family and countries around the world to abide by international law, especially the UN Charter, to promote democracy and respect for human rights.
In particular, during his participation in the 30th APPF Meeting, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, met with HE Chhuon Likphay, President of the National Assembly of Thailand and Chairman of the 30th APPF, and Mr. Say Samphoun Phum Vihan, President of the National Assembly. Laos. Nguyen Tuan Van, Secretary-General of the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA), based in Jakarta, Indonesia, was also allowed to pay a courtesy call.
