(Kampong Thom): On the morning of Saturday, October 29, 2022, after distributing rice seeds and food to farmers, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, continued to meet with provincial, district and commune councils. Sangkat Sangkat civil servants and the armed forces in Kampong Thom province.
A total of 1,523 provincial, municipal, district, commune and sangkat councilors, civil servants and members of the armed forces attended the event.
On behalf of the civil servants and the Armed Forces, Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, expressed his great pleasure to receive the opportunity to welcome the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who took the opportunity to meet with civil servants of the Armed Forces. Armed in Kampong Thom province.
The provincial governor emphasized that the presence of Samdech Techo really gave a great honor and testified to the high attention of the head of the Royal Government to civil servants and the armed forces in Kampong Thom province as a whole.
On that occasion, Mr. Nguon Rattanak informed Samdech Techo and the whole ceremony about the situation and some important achievements related to civil servants, security, order, land clearing, Tonle Sap Lake and the provision of services of civil servants.
According to the provincial governor, Kampong Thom province is 168 km away from Phnom Penh and has a total area of 15,061 square kilometers divided into 01 city, 08 districts, 73 communes, 8 communes and 765 villages with a population of 180,837 families equal to 839,991 people, population density is 56 people per square kilometer.
Across the province, there are a total of 7,937 civil servants working, 25 provincial councilors, 169 municipal councils and 585 commune councilors.
The provincial administration has requested to clear 60,886 hectares of land used by people in Prey Lang, Prey Lang Antenna, Boeung Per Wildlife Sanctuary and Natural Resource Protection Communities, equivalent to 15,378 hectares. Family.
In addition, in accordance with the high order of Samdech Techo on May 27, 2022, the provincial administration continued to request the demarcation of land from 3 areas to 2 areas to 4 people in 17 cities and districts. 577.42 hectares, 4,682 families, the remaining 2 districts are studying to apply for more pruning.
In connection with the work of cracking down on fisheries crimes, the provincial administration has set up a problem and set up a working group in cooperation with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to crack down on fisheries crimes on the Tonle Sap Lake in Phat Sanday commune, Kampong Svay district and Peam Bang commune, Stong district. .
On the other hand, in order to promote the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats, the provincial administration has set up a working group to take measures to crack down on all kinds of gambling crimes at the local level with good results.
At the same time, the provincial administration also received 51 complaints from citizens, of which 29 cases were resolved and 22 cases were sent to departments, units and districts. In addition, the provincial administration also responded to the Ministry of Interior for various opinions of the people written on the Facebook page of the head of the Royal Government and through various media.
In addition, the provincial administration has paid great attention to promoting vaccination against Kovid 19 to people throughout the province. Various levels of the people at the local level.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak also described the impact of some infrastructure in the province due to the floods. The provincial governor requested the relevant ministries, institutions and authorities to assist in the restoration of damaged infrastructure.
