Today marks the 18th anniversary of the accession to the throne of the King of Cambodia, His Majesty Norodom Sihamoni, the King pays high attention to the people
His election as the new monarch took place after his father, King Norodom Sihanouk, announced his coronation on October 7, 2004.
The inauguration ceremony of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni was held with great pomp and ceremony according to the Royal Ceremony for two days, October 28 and 29, 2004. With the visit and invitation of relatives, leaders of the top institutions of the nation, government officials and international guests in large numbers.
During the inauguration ceremony, the King of Cambodia swore, "I swear to abide by the Constitution and the laws of the Kingdom and to benefit the state and its people." " He made such an oath three times.
On that occasion, he also announced his commitment to serve the fields of religion, humanity, education, social affairs, welfare and livelihood of people throughout the country. Especially in rural areas. "I will do my best to serve all the monks, serve the people and serve my beloved homeland with patience and sincerity."
During the 18 years of his reign, the King upheld his duties and responsibilities as stipulated in the Constitution in the service of religion, humanity, education, social affairs, welfare and livelihood of the people. Across the country and bring happiness for the nation and the people of Cambodia.
In 2020 and 2021, at a time when Cambodia was facing the Kovid 19 crisis, the Khmer king was willing to give up many of his personal treasures and join the government in tackling difficulties as well as purchasing vaccines. And buy Luang Mae Hospital. In addition, he also donated food and money to the victims.
His Majesty the King, Prince Norodom Sahamoni, attaches great importance to relations with friendly countries. Meet politely and discuss other work to expand relations and cooperation with friendly countries.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum highlighted that the King of Cambodia has lived in the coldest shade with the Cambodian people in all circumstances, especially in the current phase of the fight against the devastating Kovid 19 pandemic.
Please be informed that His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni was born on May 14, 1953. He was the eldest son of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King and His Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia. He had only one younger brother, Samdech Norodom Norinpong (1954-2003).
He studied at Norodom Primary School and later went on to study at Descartes High School, both of which are located in Phnom Penh. At the age of nine, he was sent by his father to Prague, former Czechoslovakia, in 1962 as part of a neutral foreign policy and friendship with all countries that respected Cambodia's sovereignty.
There he exhibited unparalleled prominence in the pedagogical system, civil affairs, and excellent manners. After that he studied elementary, high school and music school, where he studied music and classical dance until 1975. King Norodom Sihamoni was fluent in linguistics, fluent in French and Czech. He is also fluent in English and Russian.
