(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has continued to encourage the private sector to invest more in rice production to achieve the Royal Government's plan to export 1 million tons of rice.
Such an encouraging statement to investors was made during the opening of the plenary session of the Council of Ministers on the morning of October 28, 2022.
"The Royal Government continues to encourage the private sector to invest more in rice production in Cambodia to achieve its vision," the statement said in a statement issued by the Council of Ministers. Of Cambodia's one million tons of rice exports in line with the policy on boosting rice production and rice exports.
Mr. Lon Yeng, Secretary General of the Rice Federation of Cambodia, welcomed and thanked the Prime Minister for calling for more investment in the rice sector.
At present, there are 195 medium- and large-scale rice mills that are members of the Cambodian Rice Federation, of which 80 mills can meet international standards. The 195 mills have the capacity to grind 30,000 tons of rice and dry 50,000 tons of rice per day.
Meanwhile, rice exports amounted to 2,357,674 tons, valued at an estimated value of 563.54 million US dollars, exported to Vietnam in the first nine months of 2022.
