Agriculture Minister wants to see more new investment from China in agriculture, with $ 70 million invested in 2021 and $ 4 million in the first half of this year
(Phnom Penh): Agriculture is one of the potential sectors of Cambodia that has contributed to economic growth, but investment in this sector seems to be limited, especially investment from China, although Cambodia has Free trade agreement with China will be allowed to export agricultural products to the Chinese market in the future.
Speaking at the inauguration ceremony of the export of Cambodian fresh lentils to the Chinese market on October 27, 2022, Mr. Dit Tina, Minister of Agriculture, said that the Chinese market is still a potential market for the export of products. Cambodia's agriculture, but Chinese investment in agriculture in Cambodia is still very low.
Dr. Ky Sereywat, President of the Institute of Chinese Studies and Economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, says Chinese investment in Cambodia's agricultural sector is still small because Cambodia's agricultural sector is not very profitable. The agricultural sector seems to be less attractive to Chinese investors, unlike industry, construction and real estate.
He added that if the government continues to promote the development of the real estate sector, the agricultural sector will not have much investment.
"The government must support the agricultural sector, especially land concessions, the establishment of insurance and electricity systems, and encourage the processing of agricultural products so that we can export agricultural products to China," he explained. "At the same time, in China there is a lot of agricultural production, because in China there is no vacant land, wherever there is agriculture."
Dr. Tan Monivann, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Deputy General Director of the Mong Reththy Group, told Fresh News that Cambodia has a large area of land that should be used to attract Chinese investors. It seems that the use of vacant land is not yet possible, while some farmers have given up farming and most traders are only interested in buying and selling real estate.
Dr. Tan Monivann wants the relevant institutions to strengthen the agricultural community better because the Chinese companies that come in also need to rely on the community, but the agricultural community in Cambodia is not yet strong.
He said that investment from this small amount, while the export of agricultural products to China is still small, while the free trade agreement between the two countries, which entered into force earlier this year has not made Cambodia. Exports are immediate, and investment in agriculture takes a long time to prepare for yields.
According to the data of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, in the first nine months of 2022, there were 7 investment projects in agriculture and agro-industry with a total investment of more than 104 million USD, a decrease of 5 projects compared to the same period last year. 2021 with 12 projects with an investment capital of more than 117 million dollars.
According to a report by the Ministry of Agriculture in 2021, Cambodia exported more than 830,000 tons of agricultural products to China, valued at nearly $ 700 million. For the first nine months of this year, agricultural exports to China reached more than 580,000 tons, valued at more than 491 million US dollars.
