Our Friends Association Continues Campaign to Provide Free Haircut Services to the Poor
Mr. La Vibol said that this is the second time that our Friends Association has organized the "Hair and Beauty of Our Friends" program, which aims to disseminate the professional knowledge of hair and beauty to those who want to catch Take this professionalism as well as provide hair and beauty services to the needy and workers of all informal sectors who do not have the opportunity or difficulty to access this service.
He said that this program is in response to the long-term vision of our Friends Association to help improve the living standards and increase the income of the people, which is in line with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He stated that today he led a group of well-known salons and barbershops in Phnom Penh to join our Friends Association to provide services to the informal business people and the needy in order to provide them with services. Beautiful hair to attend the upcoming National Independence Day as well as the upcoming Water Festival.
Please be informed that after providing the haircut service, our Friends Association also has a distribution of "Our Friend Support Package" to the needy and workers of the informal economy who participated now, each person will receive One package to help our friends to make life easier.
National Job and Productivity Fair 2022 expects 30,000 job applicants and live interviews
(Phnom Penh): The National Job and Productivity Fair 2022 is an easy gathering place for employers, education and training providers, job seekers and workers to get job opportunities, recruit staff and share labor market information.
Mr. Pich Sophoan said that the job fair is an intermediary to help employers select the workforce according to the needs, on time and meet the needs of stakeholders. Combining the main agendas, including:
1. Job opportunities and job applications, access to updates on job market skills requirements, career counseling and job market readiness
2. Workshop on Skills Development, Digitalization and Productivity as part of the National Productivity Campaign to share ideas, knowledge, know-how and good experiences by national and international experts to cultivate a positive mindset, change attitudes and Get rid of bad habits, increase awareness of productivity and business competitiveness in the context of the fourth generation industry.
3. Recruitment program for successful implementation of Occupational Health and Safety (OSH) measures, especially on the prevention and control of the spread of Kovid disease by 2022.
4. Human resource networking program among employers and stakeholders participating in the National Job and Productivity Fair to better link the flow of information on job opportunities, recruitment, human resource policy, skills training and Expansion of entrepreneurial potential.
Cambodian National Assembly President calls on Thai National Assembly President to continue to support and encourage people along the two countries' borders to help each other
(Bangkok): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, requested Mr. Chuon Lik Phay, President of the National Assembly of Thailand, to continue to support and encourage the people along the two countries' borders to continue to preserve the good heritage of their ancestors to help. Helping each other in emergencies, alleviating the need for urgent health services, as well as exchanging goods for daily life, make it easier for both parties.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin made this request during a meeting with Mr. Chhuon Likphay, President of the National Assembly of Thailand and Chairman of the 30th APPF on the morning of October 28, 2022 at the National Assembly of Thailand. Leading the delegation to the annual meeting of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum hosted by the Thai Parliament.
The President of the National Assembly of Cambodia thanked the Thai leadership and people for always taking care of the well-being of Cambodian migrants living and working in Thailand and getting the opportunity to learn.
The President of the Thai National Assembly expressed his deep gratitude to the President of the National Assembly of Cambodia for leading the delegation to attend the 30th APPF Annual Meeting on this occasion.
He supported the remarks made by Samdech Heng Samrin and emphasized that on behalf of the President of the Thai National Assembly, he always paid attention to the relations between the two countries, especially during the period of Kovid 19, the Thai National Assembly requested the administration to pay attention. To all foreign workers working in the country, including Cambodian workers.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin and Mr. Chhuon Likphay expressed their happiness for the achievements of the good cooperation between the governments of the two countries as well as between the two parliaments, which provided mutual benefits. For the progress and prosperity for both nations and to contribute to the maintenance of peace, stability and development both regionally and globally.
The demonstration came after RFA conducted an interview with Venerable Hok Savann, a monk in Ghana, about Dr. Hun Manet's character in the past.
Regarding the analysis of character by Venerable Hok Sovann, Dr. Hun Manet did not respond, stating that he respected his right to freedom of expression and respect as an educated monk. Dr. Hun Manet concluded that the purpose of this interview was for the interviewer to confront him with the monks.
The energetic prime ministerial candidate, who is well versed in the military, economic and political spheres, added: "It does not matter what you want me to see, because it is your right. For me, I am still me. "I will believe what I think is right and I will continue to do what I think is right, taking responsibility for my actions."
With the statement of non-response to Venerable Hok Savann, Dr. Hun Manet also taught how to report well to "Free Asia" journalists. Dr. taught that if you want to get accurate and clear information related to his character, you should ask people who know you, such as teachers who used to teach him or the school he used to go to.
Dr. Hun Manet demonstrated such good reporting techniques: "I would like to advise and advise or some journalists who want to analyze the topic of my personality if you want to research, publish information accurately. To be thorough, without bias, please do your professional research. "They never ask someone they have never met to evaluate someone."
With the response to the interview about his personality, Dr. Hun Manet also noted that since he was elected by the CPP as the next prime ministerial candidate, he has become the backbone of Opposition groups hit hard. Dr. made a comparison that the taller the tree, the stronger the wind. Dr. considers the blow is not bad because it makes the wood stronger.
Dr. concluded that the fabrication of many of the attacks on him had two goals: a for-profit political strategy. Dr. emphasizes that if you do not respond, they will continue to talk until the listener misunderstands or thinks that what they are saying is true. But if you answer, they will accuse you of being angry, they will not be able to talk a little bit.
Dr. also highlighted that those who try to attack him are all those who want a response from him to be popular. But he does not have time to respond, because he is very busy and busy with national service, even his birthday does not have time to meet with his wife and children.
Senior official of the Ministry of Environment: The Natural Resources Conservation Community Network is a good dialogue partner of the government in boosting the local economy and conserving natural resources.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khvay Atiya, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Environment, stated that the Community Resource Conservation Network is a good dialogue partner between the communities in the protected areas and the Royal Government in working together to increase the local economy and participate in protection. And better conservation of natural resources.
This statement was made by Mr. Khvay Atiya at the National Natural Resources Conservation Community Network Review Forum at the Ministry of Environment on October 27, 2022.
At the same time, Mr. Khvay Atiya said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been launching activities to increase the community's income and create new options for livelihoods by providing new knowledge, skills and occupations such as animal husbandry, planting. Other mixed crops for both daily use and for sale on the market, as well as helping to create ecotourism in the community.
Mr. Khieu Borin, Director General of Local Communities and Chairman of the National Network for Natural Resource Conservation Communities, added that the protected area communities have signed an agreement with the Ministry of Environment to participate in the protection and conservation of natural resources and biodiversity, depending on the conservation work.
Mr. Khieu Borin said that the community network for natural resource conservation is a dialogue and better cooperation between the community, local authorities, professional institutions, development partners and the private sector. At the same time, community networks share information, experiences, increase knowledge and skills between communities and stakeholders related to livelihoods and natural resource management of local communities.
He added that the Natural Resources Conservation Community Network has established internal solidarity, which has made conservation work more successful, as well as higher access to education, leading to changes in Cambodia's natural resource management. A legacy for Cambodians of all generations.
It should be noted that as of October 2022, the protected area community has been established and recognized by the Ministry of Environment, a total of 190 people with a total of 71,732 families around and in the protected area in Cambodia.
The National Natural Resource Conservation Community Network Meeting was organized with the participation of the leaders of the Ministry of Environment, representatives of provincial environment departments, regional natural resource conservation community networks at the local level and relevant development partners for the following purposes:
First, review the work progress and challenges in 2022. Second: Determine the strategic action plan for implementation in 2023. Third: Consult and approve the statute of the Community Network for Natural Resource Conservation. Is happening in the community.
According to the draft budget of 2023, "Based on the mid-year assessment, the Cambodian economy in 2022 is assessed to continue the growth trend compared to the growth in 2021, achieving a growth rate of about 5.4%. "Despite the effects of the Russia-Ukraine war crisis."
The increase is due to the continued improvement in external demand and as domestic economic activity returns to normal after the reopening of the country in November 2021.
According to the draft law on finance for management 2023, Cambodia's economic growth in 2023 will be supported by key economic sectors, including:
(1) The industrial sector is projected to continue to grow at a rate of 9.2% in 2023, similar to the 2022 growth rate of 9.0% due to the expectation of strong growth in the garment sub-sector and Manufacturing is not a garment.
The garment sub-sector is expected to continue to grow due to expectations of better external demand, especially in the US market, in line with expectations of diversion orders from countries in the region such as Myanmar.
(2) The service sector is projected to continue to grow at a rate of 6.6% in 2023 from 4.3% in 2022 due to the continued recovery of domestic economic activity, especially the hotel and restaurant sub-sector. Other tourism support sectors.
The hotel and restaurant sub-sector is expected to continue the recovery trend due to the expected recovery of international tourists, while domestic tourists are also expected to continue to grow at a faster pace than international tourists. Due to the removal of various travel barriers and the return to socio-economic normalization.
(Third): The agricultural sector is expected to continue the upward trend of 1.1% in 2023 compared to 0.7% in 2022 due to the expectation of maintaining the good growth of the crop and livestock sub-sector. Animals, meanwhile, the fishing sub-sector is expected to recover.
The crop sub-sector is expected to continue to grow due to the expectation of better growth in exports of agricultural products, especially mixed crops and industry, which will continue to be driven by free trade agreements coupled with increased government investment. In particular, financing to boost domestic production.
The livestock sub-sector is expected to maintain high growth due to expectations of continued growth in pig production, coupled with government intervention measures and the implementation of development partners' projects.
Kong Vibol, Deputy Prime Minister and Chief of Staff of the General Department of Taxation, stated that despite the uncertain economic situation, the Cambodian economy in 2023 is projected to grow by 6.6%. Taxes on the preferential sector continue to be high, but the General Department of Taxation will continue to do its best to fulfill this mission to support the implementation of government policies.
The Minister said that in order to achieve the implementation of tax revenue collection in accordance with the plan, the General Department of Taxation will continue to carry out further reforms, which will result in tax revenue exceeding the plan from 2012 to the present. In total, more than 10 years.
