7 Makara District Governor Leads Civil Servants to Clean the Streets on the Occasion of World Tourism Day 2022
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of celebrating the World Tourism Day 2022 under the theme "Rethinking Tourism" this morning, October 28, 2022, Mr. Theng Sothol, Governor of Khan 7 Makara, led the officials of Khan Youth Sangkat Cambodian Red Cross youth scouts and staff of a garbage collection company clean up the local streets.
On that occasion, Mr. Theng Sothol also read the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that this year's theme really responds to the global tourism situation, the region and Cambodia, which has been facing many complex obstacles. These include the prolongation of Kovid 19, the war in Ukraine, the escalation of the bloc and the polar system, trade and technology wars, and climate change.
These factors have led to a sharp rise in inflation, disrupting global value chains and productivity, and, in particular, a marked slowdown in global and regional economic recovery, which has had a negative impact on momentum. International tourism growth as well.
The message goes on to say that the development of tourism to become one of the main destinations for Cambodia requires careful thinking, which the Royal Government has always paid great attention to ensuring the sustainable growth of this important sector. .
This requires continued consideration of promoting the diversification of innovative ideas to ensure the competitiveness of Cambodia's tourism sector at the regional and global levels. In this regard, the Royal Government calls for more active participation to restore Cambodia's tourism sector, both in terms of quality and quantity, sustainable environment, so that development can be fruitful to all stakeholders.
At the same time, through these challenges, the Royal Government of Cambodia can also draw lessons and experiences to be an opportunity to rehabilitate and promote a better crisis-resilient tourism sector and an important input to think about. Develop and deepen the reform of the future of tourism for all. General Department of Taxation issues guidelines on the use of official exchange rates for taxpayers under the self-declaration regime
