The Royal Government of Cambodia claims that the debt situation of Cambodia is still at low risk despite the increase in loans (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Next year, the Royal Government of Cambodia plans to borrow more than 2 billion US dollars in foreign debt to meet expenses Of the Royal Government for 2023, while the Royal Government claims that although this loan increase, but does not create a debt burden to Cambodia, the debt situation is still low risk.
The draft Financial Law for 2023 stipulates that by 2023, the Royal Government of Cambodia plans to borrow 1,700 million SDR, or more than $ 2 billion, from SDs, an increase of 100 million SDR. Equivalent to more than 100 million US dollars compared to the 2022 budget.
These funds will be used for the following major projects: 7 energy projects, 5 irrigation projects, 6 physical infrastructure projects, 1 health project, 1 education and vocational training project, and agriculture sector. 3 projects and 5 other priority sectors.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has claimed that the issuance of the second issue of the securities and the borrowing of the above amount will not create a debt burden on Cambodia, that is, technically, the situation of public debt in Cambodia is still assessed as " Sustainability ”and“ low risk ”remain the same, with all of Cambodia's key debt indicators below the benchmark ratio.
