The intervention of Samdech Techo Prime Minister has two goals, the first is to rehabilitate rice fields that have been damaged by floods and the second is to solve the food shortage of the people. Therefore, in addition to providing rice seeds, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also provided food items such as rice, fish and noodles.
Thousands of tons of rice, fish and tens of thousands of cases of noodles were distributed to the people. In the face of the burden of the Royal Government in solving the difficulties of the people, they have seen the active participation of the private sector.
Tycoon Try Pheap's company is a private sector that always participates in activities with the Royal Government to solve the difficulties of the nation as well as the people whenever there are difficulties.
Tycoon Try Pheap, CEO of Try Pheap Group, who accompanied Samdech Techo Hun Sen on flood-hit provinces, provided a series of rice donations to address people's difficulties.
The company said that more than 1,000 tons of rice had arrived and had been transported from the warehouse to the provinces under the auspices of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
According to the company report, the provinces to which the company sent rice include: Preah Vihear province 100 tons, Pursat province 150 tons, Kampong Thom province 300 tons, Pailin province 50 tons, Battambang province 200 tons, Kandal Steung district, Kandal province 25 tons, Kampong Chhnang province 100 tons and Svay Rieng province 100 tons.
Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, expressed his deep gratitude to all the benefactors who shared the difficulties of the Royal Government to help the affected people. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered this gesture as a shared culture in Cambodian society, which is a good culture.
According to the report of the National Committee for Disaster Management, the floods in 2022 will affect 23 provinces, equivalent to 125 cities, districts and 513 communes. The affected provinces include Pursat, Banteay Meanchey, Pailin, Battambang, Preah Vihear, Kampong Thom, Tbong Khmum, Siem Reap, Takeo, Kampong Speu, Kampong Cham, Mondulkiri, Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Kampot, Kampong Chhnang, Stung Treng, Oddar Meanchey, Ratanakkiri, Kratie, Kep, Prey Veng and Kandal.
The floods affected 148,739 families, equivalent to 669,326 people. Affects more than 210,000 hectares of rice and more than 70,000 hectares of mixed crops. More than 110,000 hectares of rice were damaged and more than 30,000 hectares of mixed crops were damaged. Samdech Kittipritthbandit Sends a Message to His Majesty the King on the Occasion of the 18th Anniversary of His Majesty the King's Ascension
