The Cambodian economy in 2022 is expected to continue its growth trend compared to the growth in 2021, achieving a growth rate of about 5.4%, despite the impact of the Russia-Ukraine war crisis due to external and consistent demand. When the domestic economy returns to normal, especially for 2023, the Cambodian economy is projected to achieve a growth rate of around 6.6%.
Overall, Cambodia's economic growth in 2023 will be supported by key economic sectors, including:
* The industrial sector is projected to continue to grow at a rate of 9.2% in 2023, similar to the 2022 growth rate of 9.0% due to strong resumption of growth in the garment and non-garment sub-sectors. The construction sub-sector is projected to continue to recover at a slower-than-normal growth rate (before the Kovid-19 crisis).
The services sector is projected to grow at a rate of 6.6% in 2023, up from 4.3% in 2022 due to the continued recovery of domestic economic activity, especially the hotel and restaurant sub-sector and other tourism support sectors. More.
* The agricultural sector is expected to continue to grow at a rate of 1.1% in 2023 compared to 0.7% in 2022 due to the expectation of maintaining good growth in the crop and livestock sub-sectors while The fisheries sub-sector is expected to recover.
