Cambodia, China sign memorandum of understanding to boost earwax exports to China
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Trade Promotion of the Ministry of Commerce and the Cambodian Business Center in Xiamen, China have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on promoting the export of Cambodian earwax to China.
The Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was signed on October 27, 2022 with the participation of Mr. Chuon Dara, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, Mr. Kao Kosal, Director General of the Ministry of Commerce. Department of Trade Promotion, Ministry of Commerce and Mr. ZENG Yomin, President of the Cambodian Private Business Center in Xiamen.
Mr. Chuon Dara said that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding was the first step in paving the way for the export of Cambodia's earwax nests to China. He commended the leadership of the Ministry and all relevant officials for their efforts to promote the export of agricultural products from Cambodia to China.
He said that the more nests exported, the better as long as the quality is maintained, so it is necessary to bring the techniques used in the countries in the region that used to be imported to China, so that Chinese customs can have confidence in Cambodian products can only be successful in exporting to China.
Mr. Kao Kosal stated that the Memorandum of Understanding focused on key cooperation activities, including:
1: Finding a partner to produce and supply earwax products. 2: Protecting the establishment of a factory to process earwax saliva products. Strengthening the business network by organizing various business events such as business forums, business matching and attending trade fairs.
"The General Department of Trade Promotion will continue to work with the Center to launch a specific work program leading to the successful implementation of this Memorandum of Understanding," he added.
Mr. ZENG Yomin said that Cambodia has not yet officially exported the ear nests to China, so it will be detrimental to both countries, especially the farmers in Cambodia, so the signing of the MoU will be beneficial. Much to both countries.
He stated that the Cambodian Private Trade Center in Xiamen is very happy to sign a memorandum of understanding with the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia now through the Cambodian Private Trade Center in Xiamen will help promote Cambodian nests imported to China. Successfully. General knowledge: In our solar system, which planet is the highest mountain?
