A 3-year-old child can develop up to 80% of the adult brain and up to 90% by the age of 5, which is a determining factor for the development of intelligence and other skills such as social skills, courage, endurance, communication skills, etc. . Other research has also shown that skills developed in the first year of life for infants and preschoolers are determinants of success or failure in school and at school. Subsequent levels.
She also expressed her sincere appreciation to the Director of the World Organization for Children and Development, the representative of the World Bank, the Representative of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia and the Deputy Governor of Kampong Speu Province for their efforts to co-operate with all stakeholders. Coordinate the establishment of this community nursery, the first professional child care center in Cambodia.
Dr. HUN Manet Inaugurates Samdech Preah Vanroth Noy Chrek Chan Borey Vong Secondary School and Achievements at Wat Chan Borey Vong, Prek Pnov District
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hun Manet, Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, presided over the inauguration ceremony of Samdech Preah Vanroth Noy Secondary Buddhist School on the morning of October 27, 2022. Chrek Chan Borey Vong and achievements in Wat Chan Borey Vong, Sangkat Samrong, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh.
Speaking on that occasion, Dr. HUN Manet joined in congratulating on the continuous occurrence of new achievements in Wat Chan Borey Vong, which is more than 500 years old, and is also a testament to the great and powerful generosity of unity. Of Buddhists near and far, together with His Majesty the King Theranut Thera: All of them in building and developing temples to serve the actual needs and be a legacy for future generations to come.
Under the favorable environment of peace throughout the country and the support of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the field of religion has been promoted through all conditions for the implementation of the full freedom of religion. Significant contribution to the maintenance of religious harmony throughout Cambodia.
He claimed that these also reflected the people's trust in Samdech Techo, especially as manifested by the voluntary and unconditional acceptance of Kovid-19 vaccination. From the beginning, the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo has always taken care of and near the people and has also made unremitting efforts to serve the people by constantly improving the shortcomings.
According to Dr. Hun Manet, the CPP is not perfect, it is like the life of an individual who can suffer from criticism and sometimes fictional attacks on us. . The important thing is to have the patience to allow time to continue doing what we think is right and do it responsibly. Indeed, the growth of an individual is like a tree planted in a greenhouse and a tree planted in an outdoor environment.
Trees planted in greenhouses can have a high level of safety because there is no wind and can receive intensive care, and the glass roots of this tree can grow easily, but not sure to have a strong long life, especially In situations where big problems come to harass. As for the trees planted in the outdoor environment, of course, there are always obstacles, rainstorms, thunderstorms, which make the glass roots work hard to withstand the obstacles.
In this sense, the difficulties that arise in life can help as life skills for everyone to build and develop themselves based on maturity and experience.
EU High Commissioner for Energy Kadri Simson says Norway has become a major supplier of gas to the European Union after Russian supplies fell due to sanctions and technical problems. This summer, Oslo has approved gas extraction at seven new sites to increase gas production by 2022 by 20% compared to 2021.
According to the Russian Embassy in Oslo, Norway has been noted to have increased its profits through rising gas prices, and Oslo has no plans to participate in EU gas pricing. Its European partners work together on a long-term contract. Norway was once the EU's second-largest gas supplier, accounting for about 20 percent of EU demand.
