(Banteay Meanchey): The Serei Sophorn Municipal Gendarmerie Force, led by Brigadier General Yan Sovann, the Municipal Gendarmerie Local Commander, arrested a pagoda boy in the case of stealing a monk's phone on October 25, 2022 in Wat Sovan Bopta (called Wat Khla Kon Chas) is located in Khla Kon Chas Village, Sangkat Kampong Svay, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
According to Col. Yan Sovann, the suspect, Chhot Chhong, 28, was born in Kampong Speu province and currently resides in a pagoda in Khla Kon Chas village, Kampong Svay commune, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province.
Colonel Yan Sovann continued that at 00:30 on October 25, 2022, there was a case of theft (phone) at Wat Sovan Bopota (called Wat Khla Kon Chas) in the village of Khla Kon Chas, Sangkat Kampong Svay Krong. Serey Sophorn, Banteay Meanchey Province, by a suspect named Chhot Chhong, stole four mobile phones of a monk at the pagoda above.
After being arrested and interrogated, the suspect admitted that he had indeed stolen the monk's phone. The suspect was then sent to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command for further action by the local specialized force of the Municipal Gendarmerie.
Colonel Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, said that before cracking down on the above cases, he had received permission from Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie. Coordinated the procedure from Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
The suspect is currently being sent to the Provincial Court by the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Bureau and on the morning of Thursday, October 27, 2022, following legal procedures. The phone exhibits have been returned to the monks by the municipal military.
