(Kampong Chhnang): The use of seeds, fertilizers and pesticides is an essential element in determining the fate of farmers for profit or loss on farming. On October 25, 2022, Mr. Ngin Chhay, Director General of the Ministry of Agriculture, together with Mr. Pheng Kim Srun, an official of the National Committee for Disaster Management, met with the people in Melum commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province to exchange views. Some suggestions on farming.
Farmers in Melum commune, Boribo district, have a lot of knowledge on the techniques of using rice, seeds, pesticides and agricultural fertilizers, and also lead them to get more yields on farming and also profit.
The meeting was held directly in the field, Mr. Ngin Chhay and the people discussed the use of rice seeds, use of fertilizers and pesticides. Mr. Ngin Chhay provided the opportunity for farmers to have more knowledge related to the techniques of using rice, seeds, fertilizers and pesticides to share his experience.
Mr. Mao Sarim, a resident of Tuol Roka village, Mem Lum commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, said that in his experiment, he used about 200 kilograms of seed rice for wet rice and about 150 kilograms of dry rice for rumdoul rice on an area of about one hectare.
Another farmer shared the use of cassava rice. The farmer stated that for cassava rice, he used about 220 to 250 kilograms for one hectare of land.
After listening to the experience of farmers, Mr. Ngin Chhay confirmed that it is a technique for pure rice varieties such as Phkar Romduol, using between 80 kg and 100 kg for one hectare of land, for fragrant rice using between 150 kg. Grams to 160 kilograms. OM rice, like cassava, uses between 180 kg and 200 kg.
In this meeting, Mr. Ngin Chhay also discussed with farmers on fertilizers and pesticides.
