Vietnam's largest refinery to operate at full capacity to meet fuel demand
The plant, which has a capacity of 200,000 barrels per day, will supply 2.4 million to 2.5 million cubic meters of fuel during the period, Reuters reported, citing a statement issued by NSRP. From October to December, as the company has promised.
The statement came just days after several gas stations in southern Vietnam closed or restricted their sales, citing financial difficulties. State media.
NSRP said: "Recently, the supply of fuel from abroad to Vietnam has faced many difficulties, which could lead to shortages of petroleum products at some fuel agencies and retail stations."
Last Thursday, another Vietnamese refinery, Binh Son, said it had increased production to meet domestic demand and was operating at 109 percent of its capacity.
The two refineries together meet about 70% of Vietnam's refined demand.
Last Wednesday, the Vietnamese Ministry of Industry and Trade asked the State Bank of Vietnam to help local oil traders have better access to foreign currency to pay for imports as they face a sharp rise in prices. .
