MADRID (Reuters) - Three people were killed and two others were injured when armed police intervened in a shooting sparked by an altercation between a man and his father in central Madrid, police said. Spain this Wednesday. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, October 26, 2022.
The incident stemmed from a family dispute between the 50-year-old gunman and his 81-year-old father. When a neighbor, a policeman, tried to intervene, the gunman opened fire.
A special operations team from Ciudad Real was called in to intervene and shoot the gunman. A police officer was shot in the leg while another officer was also wounded by a bullet and was taken to hospital. Police said the father escaped with gunshot wounds.
