China to increase investment in rural infrastructure
BEIJING: China will accelerate investment in rural infrastructure to improve its ability to secure food supplies while maintaining economic stability. According to a report by Reuters.
Reuters reports, citing a plan issued by the Chinese Ministry of Agriculture on Tuesday, that the plan to accelerate investment in rural infrastructure, backed by eight ministries and government agencies, came at a time of decline. The growth of the world's second-largest economy is due to tightening measures to prevent Kovid-19 and a prolonged real estate slump.
Beijing has already issued a measure to try to boost the economy in the last few months of this year, but ongoing measures to curb the spread of Kovid-19 are hampering economic activity.
The rural infrastructure plan will target irrigation repairs, strengthening reservoirs, building modern greenhouses and fisheries, as well as freezing products for long-term storage.
The plan prompted the start of construction as soon as possible, and local governments were encouraged to support the project.
"Strengthening agricultural and rural infrastructure is an important task for expanding investment effectively and stabilizing the economy as a whole," the plan said.
