Cambodia presents the outcome of the 4th ASEAN-EU Dialogue on Human Rights Policy
The dialogue focused on human rights issues, including: improving guarantees for the protection of children's rights, labor rights, migration and human trafficking, freedom of expression and thought, freedom of religion and belief, and the rights of people with environmental disabilities. And climate change, women's rights and gender equality, the social environment, as well as the protection of human rights during the fight against extremist violence.
While acknowledging that challenges remain, the dialogue also provided an opportunity to review key developments in ASEAN, such as business and human rights, women's rights and children's rights. In addition, this is an opportunity to discuss the situation of the crisis in some countries in the world, which has led to a serious impact on the human rights sector.
The fourth dialogue was also attended by representatives of civil society organizations and representatives of national human rights institutions (NHRIs) in the ASEAN region and from the European Union, sharing their priorities in ensuring justice and expectations. For human rights cooperation between regional and national human rights mechanisms.
In addition to the above-mentioned consultations, there were also separate bilateral meetings between the EU Delegation and representatives of a number of countries, representatives of the ASEAN Commission on the Promotion and Protection of the Rights of Women and Children (ACWC). The ASEAN Committee is responsible for implementing the ASEAN Declaration on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Migrant Workers (ACMW) and the ASEAN Committee on Women (ACW).
