Residents of Kampong Chhnang province are angry with Sam Rainsy for insulting the King and declaring opposition to any movement that causes social unrest (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Insulting the power of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom Cambodia, highly revered by three generations of traitors, Sam Rainsy has ignited the anger of the Cambodian people.
The bitter insults of the convicts who betrayed the nation from the time of their grandfathers made the Cambodian people unacceptable. According to the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the King is the head of state and cannot be abused or despised by anyone. In addition, the people of Cambodia have maintained the deepest respect and love for the King.
For His Majesty, the Prince of Life has been on the gems since he ascended the throne in 2004, he has fulfilled his royal duties and duties in accordance with the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia. He was a cool shade for the Cambodian people. Especially under the shadow of his hand, Cambodia has been in peace and progress. Khmer people live in harmony and happiness.
Khem Channoeun, an official at Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hall, said he could not accept Sam Rainsy's ignorant remarks. Mr. Chan Noeun considered the remarks of Sam Rainsy as the most serious insult to the King's power that can not be forgiven.
The official of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hall stated, "We are very dissatisfied and cannot accept what Sam Rainsy has said to the King, who is the highest deity." He has always provided peace and harmony since coming to the throne. "He played an important role as the king in the center, without regard to any political party."
Mr. Chan Noeun saw that what Sam Rainsy was saying was because he was angry with the King for not supporting their political activities, which were political activities that led to national destruction.
Mr. Chan Noeun also saw the words and deeds of Sam Rainsy as an expression of the ungratefulness of three generations of Sam Rainsy convicts, both himself and his father, who had been blessed by God. The royal family, especially the former King Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, the King.
Mr. I Sary, a resident of Baribo District, Kampong Chhnang Province, was also very angry at the insult to the power of the Khmer King, whom he deeply loved. The citizen of Boribo district has condemned the prisoner's actions and announced that the law will punish him severely.
Hing Phop Meena, Governor of Kampong Chhnang City, considered the words of Sam Rainsy to be a serious violation of the Cambodian Constitution, which states that no one can touch or violate the King. The mayor strongly condemned Sam Rainsy's remarks.
In a rice distribution ceremony for farmers in Kampong Chhnang province on the morning of October 26, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, called on the words of Sam Rainsy as an intention to overthrow the monarchy. Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on the Cambodian people to stand up and condemn the actions of Sam Rainsy and to jointly protect the peace that is covering Cambodian territory.
Mr. Khem Channoeun fully announced his support for Samdech Techo's message by defending peace in Cambodia. For Mr. Chan Noeun, peace is very important in the process of national development, especially to ensure the peace of the people.
Mr. Chan Noeun expressed his strong opposition to the extremist policies of Sam Rainsy. The Kampong Chhnang provincial official sees that extremist politics that leads to social unrest will lead to national destruction and can not provide well-being for the people.
