(Phnom Penh): Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, stated that the General Department of Taxation is committed to strengthening the implementation of tax laws, tax collection and the elimination of tax evasion to provide justice to taxpayers. All will push for Cambodia to remove its name from the gray list to attract foreign investment flows.
Mr. Kong Vibol said this at the Tax Forum 2022 organized by the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia on October 26, 2022 at the Sofitel Hotel.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that the strengthening of tax collection is to create fair competition among business people in Cambodia, and this case will also push Cambodia out of the gray list.
Kong Vibol's remarks come after the Paris-based Financial Working Group (FATF) in March 2022 decided to continue to put Cambodia on a "gray list" that the world needs to increase. Follow up.
"Cambodia has anti-money laundering agents, because Cambodia is on the gray list, we have various mechanisms that we hope Cambodia will leave the gray list and return to the list again to attract investment flows," he said. From abroad to invest in Cambodia.
Mr. Kong Vibol said that in the past few years, the Director General of Taxation has caught many cases of tax evasion, which some companies commit. At the same time, some business associations have also proposed tax incentives. However, he can no longer allow tax evasion because Cambodia needs to build its reputation and get back on the list.
According to the General Department of Taxation, from January to October this year, taxes collected more than 104% of the national budget law, and it is expected that by the end of this year, tax collection will exceed the plan by 15% to 25%. Tomorrow, the Government Spokesperson Unit will hold a press conference to present the achievements of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport for 5 years.
