Through this digital nursery, the public can find the latest information related to the digital revolution in Cambodia and be able to participate in various initiatives to promote the economic development and digital society in Cambodia.
To support the launch of "Cambodia Towards Digital" and promote the production of more useful video content for viewers, especially to encourage creative video content producers, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has organized an educational video content competition. On two topics: (1) a day in the digital world and (2) how to keep your Facebook account secure.
For the first topic, candidates are required to prepare video content to share experiences on the use of digital tools / applications that are useful for their studies or daily work. For the second topic, candidates are required to prepare video content on various ways to secure their Facebook account.
The top three video content for each topic will be awarded from 1 million to 4 million riels from the program. All winners will have the opportunity to become educational content producers for the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and will be invited to a talk show with a representative of Facebook in Cambodia. Drugs ruin your future, stay away! Nationwide drug crackdown on October 26: 13 cases cracked, 33 arrested
