Mr. Chan Sokhon also expressed his full support for the campaign announced by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to eradicate the ideology of extremist politics of three generations of traitors from Cambodia to maintain peace, social stability and peace of the people. Khmer citizens.
Notably, the statement condemning Sam Rainsy by the second deputy head of the Candlelight Party in Anlong Veng commune came after the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on the commune council to condemn Sam Rainsy's actions. Rainsy.
During the rice seed distribution ceremony for farmers in Kampong Chhnang province on the morning of October 26, 2022, Samdech Techo called on commune / sangkat councils to come out and condemn Sam Rainsy's actions without fear of the party's removal. .
Samdech Techo stated that the Candlelight Party could not remove the Commune / Sangkat Council from the Candlelight Party without the approval of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior.
In this morning's ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also waited to see the statement of the leaders of the Candlelight Party to the remarks of Sam Rainsy. For Samdech Techo, if the Candlelight Party does not condemn Sam Rainsy, it is as if this party is supporting the insulting act of the traitorous King, the founder of the Candlelight Party.
Fifth Senate Commission Meets with Information Minister on Information and Audiovisual Progress in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information Committee of the Senate, chaired by Mr. Chhit Kim Yat, Acting Chairman of the Fifth Committee of the Senate, met with Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, this morning, October 26, 2022. Answer some questions related to the development process of the information and audio-visual sector in Cambodia, along with the challenges that the Ministry of Information must address and fulfill well.
He further clarified the function of the Senate is to legislate, inspect and represent and mentioned the number of questionnaires that the Fifth Commission sent to the Ministry of Information to review and report.
On that occasion, Minister Khieu Kanharith informed about the progress of the Ministry of Information regarding the implementation of roles and responsibilities in line with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy and the National Development Strategic Plan.
Along with this, there are also FM radio programs in the provinces, in which the National Radio of Ratanakiri Province also broadcasts in the languages of Prev, Pnong, Tampuon, Kreung and Jarai. With this, the Ministry is also preparing to set up a radio station on Bokor Mountain, which can be broadcasted at high altitudes, especially useful for fishermen, seafarers and the army stationed on the islands can listen to the news broadcast. Recent events.
The Ministry is preparing a draft law on access to information and a draft law on amendments to the press law to strengthen the management of journalists and the right of information of the general public. He also pointed out that the challenges facing the Ministry are financial and human resources, which are still limited and can not respond in time and adequately on information and dissemination.
Regarding questions related to the transition from analog to digital broadcasting, the Minister of Information stressed the importance of changing in line with the rapid development of the media in Cambodia and the world, and in the past, some local public and private television Switching to this digital system is already gradual.
Mr. Chhit Kim Yat summed up the discussion and confirmed that the Fifth Commission and the report of the discussion on this occasion were respected by the President of the Senate and all the committees were informed. Ratanakkiri Provincial Administration Holds a Meeting of Provincial Unity Command to Strengthen Security, Law and Order Enforcement
