Gendarmerie Arrests Siem Reap Provincial Finance Director in Public Insult, Violence and Murder Case
(Phnom Penh): The National Gendarmerie Force, in cooperation with the Kampong Cham Provincial Gendarmerie and the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, arrested Mr. Som Samsak, Director of Finance Office of Siem Reap Provincial Hall and accused in a public insult case. Intentional use of violence and attempted murder. This was confirmed by Brigadier General So Savoeun, Commander of the Kampong Cham Provincial Gendarmerie, to Fresh News on October 26.
Brigadier General So Savoeun said that the arrest of the director of the Siem Reap Provincial Hall of Finance was made on a warrant issued by the Investigating Judge of the Kampong Cham Provincial Court, Mr. Sous La, on charges of “public insult, intentional violence and attempt. Murder "took place at Neak Meas Restaurant in Mondul 2 Village, Sangkat Svay Dangkum, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province on June 14, 2022.
Please be informed that the accused was arrested by professional forces at 11:30 on October 26, 2022 at the point of Street 118, Village 9, Sangkat Phsar Thmei I, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh.
The operation was led by Brigadier General So Savoeun, Commander of the Kampong Cham Provincial Gendarmerie, in collaboration with the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie and Brigadier General So Sarin, Deputy Commissioner for National Police Investigation and Suppression under the coordination of Mr. Vong Bunvisoth, Prosecutor of Kampong Cham Provincial Court and Phnom Penh Prosecutor.
Currently, the Phnom Penh Royal Gendarmerie has handed over to the Kampong Cham Provincial Gendarmerie for processing.
1,191 young people receive Hoka hospitality training by the third quarter of 2022
(Phnom Penh): The results of Hoka Hospitality Training for the third quarter of 2022 by the Hoka Project Management Committee trained a total of 1,191 tourism professionals and trainers (783 females) in office food and beverage service skills. Front row of professional chefs in Preah Vihear, Kratie, Stung Treng, Ratanakiri, Mondulkiri, Siem Reap, Battambang, Pursat and Kampong Chhnang.
On that occasion, Secretary of State Pak Sokhom said that the meeting will highlight the efforts and achievements of the Secretariat and the Provincial Department of Tourism in the past in the target provinces, projects and challenges in Hoka hospitality training. As well as the direction of the Department of Tourism to continue the work in the fourth quarter of 2022.
The meeting was also a forum to exchange and share hospitality training experiences with the Tourism Industry Association and the private sector to explore the possibility of incorporating the Hoka Hospitality training program into its plans, he said.
Mr. Chuob Ratana said that the Hoka Hospitality Training focuses on the knowledge and skills of the trainees, who are currently working professionals, poor youth and professionals who have retired from the Kovi-19 crisis.
He said that through this good cooperation, Swiss Consult will expand Hoka Hospitality Training to Battambang, Pailin, Pursat, Banteay Meanchey and Oddar Meanchey, which are priority destinations and potential for tourism.
According to Chuob Ratana, the Ministry of Tourism and Swiss Confederation have been expanding Hoka hospitality training to Battambang, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey and Pursat provinces. 884 young people (596 females) received Hoka hospitality training in the first half of 2022.
He said the training focused on forms of cooperation, including:
1. Promote cooperation with the Hoka Project Management Committee to facilitate better project implementation with high quality and productivity.
2. Strengthen the capacity of the Department of Tourism of Target B on the organization of hospitality training programs, the capacity of trainers and cooperation with tourism operations for the sustainability of hospitality training in the future.
3. Promote tourism professionalism with a focus on front office skills training, food and beverage services, housekeeping, community chefs, tourism / ecotourism and coffee making skills.
