(Phnom Penh): Don Christine Rosana is in very good health after receiving the most intensive treatment by Calmette Hospital doctors for almost a week. Christine Rosana is now being treated at Calmette Hospital for further treatment at Kantha Bopha Hospital in Siem Reap near her home.
On the morning of Wednesday, October 26, 2022, Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, visited Calmette Hospital to arrange for Christine Rosana to be sent to Kantha Bopha Hospital in Siem Reap. Ms. Youk Sambath bought a wheelchair for Christine Rosana to learn to sit and donated an additional 3 million Riels for Christine Rosana's mother to solve various difficulties.
"Sana is relieved and clear of her face after nearly a week of treatment at Calmette Hospital," she said. "There are painkillers, anticonvulsants and more. There is a pusum serum. He is refreshed and the contractions are relieved and the pain is reduced."
Ms. Youk Sambath, who was directly instructed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to monitor Sana's treatment, said that after her condition improved, Calmette doctors arranged to send Sana to Kantha Bopha Hospital for further treatment. In Siem Reap. According to Ms. Youk Sambath, she was sent to Kantha Bopha for treatment in Siem Reap because this doctor is a pediatrician and is located near Sana's guardian's house, which is convenient for care.
Ms. Youk Sambath also confirmed that she will continue to monitor the treatment and the doctors of Kantha Bopha Department in Siem Reap will continue to pay close attention to Sana's condition.
According to Ms. Youk Sambath, Sana was diagnosed with meningitis and encephalitis when she was one and a half years old, which has caused complications and serious condition to this day.
Because of the above conditions, Don Christine Rosana has been living in a plant-like condition for many years. Parents have to live in despair, full of grief and sadness, pity their daughters.
Unable to bear the pain of her daughter, Nuon Niratey, a mother, lost her three children in search of mercy and relief from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on October 22, 2022. One in the development area of Siem Reap.
Thanks to a week of medical and rescue efforts, Christine Rosana has finally regained the hope of breathing life on this beautiful planet.
Hope and excitement are not just for Christy Rosana, but Nuon Niratey, a mother who has great love for her child, is even happier and happier.
Through Ms. Youk Sambath, Ms. Nuon Niratay said goodbye to Samdech Techo and wished Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, as well as sons, daughters, grandsons and granddaughters, happiness and prosperity.
