This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Distributes Seed Rice to More Than 3,000 Families in Kampong Chhnang Province
(Kampong Chhnang): The mission of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to distribute rice seeds to flood-affected farmers in the provinces around Tonle Sap Lake has reached Kampong Chhnang province after about 4 days. In the morning of Wednesday, October 26, 2022, Samdech Techo Prime Minister distributed rice seeds and food to 3,460 farmers affected by the flood. Each family received 100 kg of rice, as well as some food and money.
Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, said that the floods from the river affected people's rice crops in five districts, including Boribo, Choulkiri, Kampong Leng, Kampong Tralach and Rolea Bier districts. Affected 3,460 families, damaged rice crops on a total area of 2,610 hectares, equivalent to 1.80% of the total rice cultivation area in the province. However, all those damaged areas can be restored.
The floods affected a total of 11,479 families in 6 cities / districts, 29 communes / sangkats, of which 794 families were evacuated to their relatives' homes and safe places. People's lives.
Despite the flooding, the authorities have not been indifferent, have been active in helping to evacuate to safety and provide food to solve the problem.
According to the Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, in response to the floods, the provincial administration has immediately deployed operational forces and local authorities to address the challenges of the affected people, especially providing food, shelter, clean water, medicine and permanent staff. Provide security and be ready to continue to help and evacuate people to the prepared safety.
The provincial governor said that the measures that the province has taken care of in the past include intervening to save lives, evacuate people to safety, provide food, equipment, pay attention to welfare, water, sanitation, security, etc. .
In that, the provincial administration has donated food, royal gifts to the King and gifts from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as philanthropists to 4,584 affected families.
Please note that Samdech Techo Hun Sen spent about a week to solve the problems of the people in five provinces. Samdech Techo Hun Sen starts the process of solving the problems of the people in the provinces on October 21, 2022 in Siem Reap to organize the village for people to volunteer to leave the Angkor resort and the area controlled by the Apsara Authority.
On October 22, Samdech Techo continued to Banteay Meanchey and continued to Battambang, Pursat and Kampong Chhnang on the following days. The missions in the four provinces include meeting with government officials and the armed forces, as well as distributing rice seeds, food and money to flood victims.
In about 4 days, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with farmers in Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Pursat and Kampong Chhnang provinces, a total of more than 20,000 families distributed more than 2,000 tons of rice.
The mission to distribute rice seeds to farmers will not end in Kampong Chhnang province, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will continue to distribute rice seeds to farmers in Kampong Thom province on October 29 and in Prey Veng province on October 30 this weekend. Check out the gallery of important pictures on international events on October 25, 2022!
