Report: More than 29,000 people have died in migration to Europe since 2014 (Video inside) (Barcelona): More than 29,000 people have died in migration to Europe since 2014 In 2014, 5,000 people died in the last two years. This is according to the International Organization for Migration in a report released on Tuesday.
The UN agency warns of "rising death tolls on the Mediterranean crossing on the mainland to Europe and on the continent."
According to its report, the deadliest migration route continues in the central Mediterranean, where 2,836 migrants and refugees have died since January 2021 trying to reach Italy. Malta, passing through mostly from Libya and Tunisia.
The second deadliest route is the Atlantic route from West Africa to the Spanish island of Canary, where more than 1,500 deaths have been recorded since 2021.
