In order to help the farmers to resume farming quickly and timely, Samdech Techo Hun Sen launched a special intervention by releasing rice seeds of the Royal Government, and Samdech personally invited to distribute. In the past few days, Samdech Techo has already distributed more than 2,000 tons of rice seeds to farmers in Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Pursat provinces.
On October 26, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will continue to distribute about 346 tons of rice seeds to 3,460 farmers in Kampong Chhnang province affected by the floods.
Rice seeds are very valuable for farmers to replant their fields and also help reduce their costs. The farmers who will receive rice seeds from Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed their happiness and expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo.
Mr. Mao Sarim, a resident of Tuol Roka village, Mem Lum commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, said that rice seeds are very important for them to replant when they run out of rice.
Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, as well as other farmers, expressed his happiness and joy for the donation of rice seeds for farmers to replant rice. The provincial governor expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who is always present when farmers have difficulties.
It should be noted that the floods in Kampong Chhnang province, in addition to damaging rice, also affected a total of 11,479 families. Of those, 794 families were evacuated to relatives' homes and safe havens, and no casualties were reported.
In order to solve the flood problem, the provincial administration has assigned operational forces and local authorities to immediately intervene to solve the challenges of the affected people, especially to provide food, shelter, clean water, medicine, security forces and regular preparations. To continue to help and evacuate people to a safe place prepared.
