According to Plan International Cambodia, more than one million people in Prey Veng province, from 1,139 villages, 116 communes and 12 districts and 1 city, are benefiting from the change of provinces to end open defecation (ODF) in Cambodia. Which means every household has a toilet.
According to Mr. Lok Vuthy, Director of the Prey Veng Provincial Department of Rural Development, in recent years, Prey Veng Rural Water Supply, Sanitation and Sanitation has made significant progress. There are 197,273 wells, 2 community water distribution stations and 31 community drinking water production stations supported by partner organizations.
At the same time, Dr. Chrun Therawat set out 9 important points for the Provincial Governor, Deputy Provincial Governor and Chairman of the Technical Working Group on Rural Water Supply and Sanitation (PWG), partner organizations and 25 rural development departments - Provinces for implementation are as follows:
* Second: Chairman of the Technical Working Group on Rural Water Supply and Sanitation (PWG) at the provincial level, with the Capital-Provincial Departments of Rural Development as the Permanent Secretaries (PWGs) and the administration of all districts, municipalities, communes and sangkats in each province. Educate, disseminate and inspire rural communities to build toilets and use latrines, as well as clean the environment.
* Third: Chairman of the Provincial Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Technical Working Group (PWG), with the 25 provincial-capital Department of Rural Development as Permanent Secretary (PWG's) and all district, municipal, commune and sangkat administrations in each province. Educate and encourage rural communities to wash their hands with soap before eating and after defecation with safe drinking water and storage.
* Fourth: Please call on all private sector development partners and non-governmental organizations, especially the organizations present here, to continue to support and actively participate in the implementation of the plan to expand basic sanitation coverage in Cambodia. Both material, financial and technical.
* Sixth, all provinces with environmental challenges must consider discussing with relevant parties to provide technology and resources to poor households to have access to latrines, avoiding cooperation, which is an obstacle to the growth of sanitation in Its basis.
* Eighth: The Commune / Sangkat Administration should prepare additional action plans related to the 6th qualification on "Sanitation, Aesthetics and Environment" to request additional funding for the following year or part of the budget allocation from the Commune / Sangkat Development Fund to serve the water sector. Rural and sanitation.
Ninth: Carefully organize services and guidelines for the proper management of manure in a technical manner to avoid the discharge of manure into the environment, causing serious impact on people's health.
