The following is the announcement of the General Department of Taxation: The National Museum received a set of furniture and a painting from the Constitutional Council to preserve the National Heritage
(Phnom Penh): The National Museum of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts handed over a set of furniture, including 6 wooden chairs, 1 small armchair, 1 long armchair, 1 marble table and 1 painting from the group. Constitutional Advisor to the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts for the purpose of registering as a national heritage property.
The ceremony took place on October 24, 2022 at the National Museum, presided over by Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, and Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts.
This set of furniture has been used by high-ranking Cambodian dignitaries since the 1950s in the "White" building of the Chamkar Mon State Palace, which is now the headquarters of the Constitutional Council. The paintings are a rare remnant of Nhek Dim.
Taking this opportunity, the Minister of Culture and Fine Arts delivered a welcome message to the public wishing to donate artefacts to preserve the National Heritage.
He added that this is the second time that the Constitutional Council has handed over to the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts art objects that should be preserved as heritage. In 2018, the Constitutional Council has already handed over once. A large number of rare paintings by Nhek Dim to be preserved at the National Museum.
