BEIJING: The 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC) has called for a modernization of the Chinese style to promote the great prosperity of the Chinese nation. China's vision of modernization is widely recognized by the world's youth who give interviews.
A survey in 30 countries surveyed 4,700 young people under the age of 30, showing that 84.7% of respondents agreed that development paths should be based on national circumstances. Note that no modernization form can be applied in all countries.
More than 80% of the young people interviewed agreed with the Chinese Communist Party's view on keeping the people as the core, and generally praised that modernizing the Chinese style is a way to improve the lives of all people.
Global interviewers praised China's development over the past 10 years, with 83.1% noting that China has made great strides in science and technology. 74.1% said that China's position in the international arena is steadily increasing, while 79.1% said that the Chinese Communist Party is a party that the Chinese people can trust.
