(Pursat): On Tuesday morning, October 25, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, handed over 514,500 kg of rice seeds to 5,145 farmers affected by floods in Pursat province.
Pursat is also a province that has been severely flooded due to flooding and runoff from other areas. Mr. Cheng Lay, Acting Governor of Pursat Provincial Board of Governors, said that the floods affected 7 cities / districts, affecting a total of 13,775 families, equivalent to 6,709 houses. Short-term evacuation of 174 families to safety. Four people drowned.
The floods also affected 25 schools, 2 health centers, affected 16 pagodas and temples, affected 3,050 meters of rubber roads, affected 92,115 meters of red gravel roads, and affected a number of water wells. 96 places, 66 ponds, 2,311 toilets.
Along with the floods, the authorities and the provincial armed forces have paid close attention to rescuing the people and solving the difficulties of the people during the floods.
According to the Acting Provincial Governor, the Provincial Disaster Management Committee and the Cambodian Red Cross have provided emergency food to 1,032 flood-affected families, including 205 families in Kandeang district and 827 families in Krakor district. .
