(UAE): On the occasion of accompanying Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, attended the official opening ceremony of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates on the morning of October 24, 2022. Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, leads a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to attend the United Arab Emirates-Cambodia Business Forum in Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates.
Speaking at the business forum, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, expressed his deep gratitude to the Ministers of the two countries for presiding over the United Arab Emirates-Cambodia Business Forum and congratulated the opening ceremony. Official form of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates.
He spoke about business opportunities, investment, economic situation, potential sectors of Cambodia and the growth of each sector, urging UAE investors to visit Cambodia and explore the possibility of cooperating on joint projects.
Despite the effects of Kovid-19, Cambodia is one of the fastest growing economies in the region. Economic growth in 2022 is projected at around 5%, supported by the recovery of key sectors.
The Royal Government has launched a plan for economic recovery after the Kovid-19 crisis 2021-2023, which will help restore the economy to an annual growth rate of 7%.
As the Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, the President invited the UAE investors to attend the ASEAN Business and Investment Summit to be held on 9 and 10 November 2022 in Phnom Penh, Cambodia.
The summit is the largest forum in Southeast Asia and will be attended by the President and Prime Minister, as well as business leaders and researchers in the ASEAN region and dialogue partners.
