Samdech Techo Hun Sen Holds a Get-Together with Pursat Civil Servants and Armed Forces
(Pursat): On the morning of Monday, October 24, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen arrived in Pursat after completing his mission in Battambang.
On his way to Pursat province, Grandfather Khleang Moeung, the great commander of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen started his work with a meeting with provincial councils, municipalities / districts, communes / sangkats, government officials and the Armed Forces, and tomorrow Samdech Techo Will distribute rice seeds to flood farmers.
According to the report of Mr. Cheng Lay, Acting Governor of Pursat Provincial Board of Governors, the provincial / municipal / district / commune / sangkat councils, civil servants and the armed forces who had the honor of having a face-to-face meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen this afternoon Approximately 2,022 people.
Representing Mr. Cheav Tay, Governor of Pursat Province, as well as government officials and the Armed Forces in the whole province, Mr. Cheng Lay expressed his immense excitement at the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who was busy providing meetings.
Mr. Cheng Lay said that the presence of Samdech Techo at this time shows the highest concern of Samdech Techo to civil servants and the armed forces in Pursat province.
After welcoming with warmth and pleasure, Mr. Cheng Lay also informed Samdech Techo and the whole ceremony about the information related to the civil servants, the Armed Forces in the province, the security situation, order and other work in the province.
According to the acting provincial governor, there are 5,976 civil servants in Pursat province, 2,581 of whom are female. Mr. Cheng Lay also said that in order to better serve the public at the sub-national level, civil servants at all levels have strictly implemented in accordance with the reform policies of the Royal Government, especially the performance of duties in Provide administrative services to the people through mechanisms to solve challenges and participate in local development.
In addition, to increase confidence in the leadership of the Royal Government, especially the recommendation of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the provincial administration has created an atmosphere for monks, people, government officials, the Armed Forces to enjoy through the event of the boat race. The three-day event, which recently ended, was attended by more than 170,000 national and international guests.
On the task of maintaining security, safety and public order, the Acting Provincial Governor affirmed that the Administrative Unity Command at all levels, civil servants, and the Armed Forces have made efforts to unite and cooperate to prevent and suppress all kinds of crimes that occur within their jurisdiction in order to Make people warm in living and doing business.
After listening to the reports of the provincial governor, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure to return to meet with provincial councils, municipalities / districts, communes / sangkats, government officials and the armed forces in Pursat province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen congratulated all Commune / Sangkat Councils in Banteay Meanchey Province for their support through the recent election.
The Prime Minister praised and appreciated the civil servants and the armed forces in the province for their joint efforts to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and help solve the problems of the people during the recent floods. Recently. In particular, joint efforts to maintain security, order and order in society to prevent acts of social unrest.
However, in this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded all civil servants, especially commune / sangkat councils to continue to pay attention to fulfill their duties and responsibilities to serve the nation and the people, especially to continue to pay attention. Provide necessary services to the people quickly. Absolutely avoid creating problems that lead to resentment to the morale of the people.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister reminded to continue to pay attention to maintaining security and social order by implementing the policy of safe villages and communes, including the suppression of various crimes such as theft, robbery, drug trafficking, etc. to provide warmth and ensure safety Of living and working of various people.
Samdech Techo also instructed the authorities to take care to resolve land disputes for the people quickly and effectively, especially to resolve a lot outside the court without bias, must stand in the middle to serve. Mutual benefit.
Samdech Techo also instructed the Armed Forces Authority to have good cooperation with neighboring countries such as Thailand to strengthen cooperation relations, especially to strengthen economic and trade relations between neighboring countries. Better.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also praised officials at all levels who have worked together to develop Pursat to grow more and more. Senior official of the Ministry of Education: Good young people should be a solution and a messenger to help society to the problems facing society
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kim Sethany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, stated that a good young person should be a solution and a messenger to help society, no matter how small, to the problems that are facing. In society, especially helping young people to stay away from drugs and alcohol.
Ms. Kim Sethany added that today's students and youth are qualified and fit enough to be a messenger to work not only for the competition, but also to contribute to promoting the impact of Use of alcohol and drugs is an important contribution to the ban on the use of alcohol in sports venues.
Ms. Kim Sethany added that being a youth messenger to help other young people stay away from alcohol and drugs is a good virtue to fulfill their role as a citizen. One to use what one has in order to be a solution to help others.
Ms. Kim Sethany also claimed that in order to be a role model and a good messenger to help others, young people must strive to understand more about what is the current problem and a good solution, including what is The Royal Government's efforts to control the media, such as the effects of drug and alcohol abuse, are even better to have a clear testimony to help others as well.
