Officials and experts encourage real estate developers to enter the stock market to raise capital from the public
(Phnom Penh): Senior officials of the securities and real estate sector support real estate developers to enter the stock market to raise capital from this market for real estate development, as for more than two years, the real estate sector in Cambodia has been affected by The Kovit Crisis 19 and the effects of the Russian-Ukrainian war.
Mr. Sou Socheat, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, encouraged other real estate companies that need capital for their real estate development to list on the stock exchange. Listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange to raise capital from the public.
"Encourage him to get more on the stock exchange, and now is the time for greater competition, making him better prepared to list on the stock exchange for his name," she said. "He is more recognizable to customers."
He said that the new product will start to study at the end of 2022 and can reach the start of trading on the stock exchange in 2023.
Regarding the development of new products that link the real estate sector and the securities sector, Mr. Chou Vannak, Director General of Real Estate and Mortgage Regulators, said that he would provide cooperation and seek advice from management to promote the growth of both sectors. But now the real estate sector has seen modest growth following the effects of the 19-Kovid crisis and the Russian-Ukrainian war.
He added: "When we have a better relationship between cash flow and cash flow from real estate investors, because the growth of the real estate sector today is that we get from the capital of investors from buyers from the bank, but in the future. "The source of capital is that we can get it from the stock market."
He added that if the war between Russia and Ukraine was brought under control, the real estate sector would revive in 2023 and 2024.
JS Land is the first real estate developer to list on the Cambodia Securities Exchange in February 2022, listing nearly 26 million shares at a price of 1,900 riels. The Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX) expects the company's entry into the stock market to attract more real estate companies to the stock market.
