This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Distributes Seed Rice to More Than 10,000 Families in Battambang Province
(Battambang): On Monday morning, October 24, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, distributed rice seeds and had a talk with about 11,528 farmers affected by floods in Battambang province.
Meeting with farmers today, in addition to providing rice seeds, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also prepared food packages and budgets for farmers to solve difficulties in life.
Battambang is a province in the northwest of the country that has also been severely flooded due to flooding and downpours from various areas.
The floods also affected a total of 29,384 homes, damaged 32, affected 76 schools, six health centers, 19 pagodas and four public administration buildings. In addition, 45,812 hectares of people's rice crops were affected and 27,233 hectares were damaged.
In addition, Samdech Krala Hom, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, provided a series of donations to flood victims, including the Provincial Disaster Management Committee and the provincial branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, bringing donations from philanthropists and material donations of Samdech Techo. The Prime Minister, through the Food Reserve System Management Committee of Cambodia, has already distributed a total of 6,472 families.
