Samdech Techo Hun Sen Instructs the Minister of Agriculture to Study Rice Seed Production for High Yield Farmers (Video inside) (Battambang): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on October 24, 2022 To Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Hunting and Fisheries, to consider producing rice seeds for farmers so that they can grow high yields.
Samdech Techo advised the Ministry of Agriculture to study the production of rice seeds in the area to suit the soil conditions in that area, and the state can cooperate with farmers by contracting them to produce seeds that the state. Needed and sold back to the state at harvest. This does not require the state to have its own production area.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the yield of farmers also started from the use of the right variety, which he spent almost half of his life to change the attitude of the people about the use of this variety.
Speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of distributing rice seeds and meeting with 11,528 farmers affected by floods in Battambang province on the morning of October 24, 2022.
Samdech added, "We do not need to go to the land to produce our own seeds, our people already produce rice, we just choose an area that has enough water source, we put good seeds for him to produce that seed for us." "And we buy from him to stock up, so that in the future we can afford to supply rice varieties that are suitable for each area."
Samdech Techo Prime Minister also stated that when the state has good rice varieties, people can exchange their rice with the state's rice seeds and the state must exchange seeds for him.
Samdech Techo reiterated that in the government led by Samdech will not be ridiculed as "seedless," which is not seed here, it means no seed, not seed. The Royal Government of Cambodia guarantees enough rice seeds to be distributed to farmers in case of natural disasters such as floods in 2022.
Samdech stated that this year's flood, the Royal Government has confirmed rice seeds to intervene to more than 7,000 tons of farmers so that farmers can recover as soon as possible.
