(Kiev): Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has said that his military will continue to develop Russia's missile launch capabilities with the help of allies and allies, while the Ukrainian military is now capable of launching a large part of its missiles. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, October 23, 2022.
The Ukrainian military claimed that about 33 missiles were fired at Ukraine earlier this morning (Kiev time) and that 18 of them had been shot down. Since October 10, Russia has launched a series of missile and drone strikes on Ukraine's energy infrastructure. According to Kiev, about 40 percent of Ukraine's energy infrastructure has been damaged so far.
Authorities in some parts of Ukraine have reported attacks on power plant sites, as well as power outages, while engineers have been working to restore the damaged network. Meanwhile, power supply restrictions are being implemented in a total of 10 areas, including Kiev. More than 100 families request the relevant local authorities to expedite the issuance of land titles in Tumnup Rolok commune, Stung Hav district
(Preah Sihanouk): More than 100 families living and doing various activities in Village 1, Tumnup Rolok Commune, Stung Hav District, Preah Sihanouk Province, on the morning of October 22, 2022, gathered to apply to the authorities and district officials. Stung Hav aims to visit the realities of life and enjoyment in their area so that they can get the same legal title as other citizens.
Regarding the above request, the people agreed that every time they asked about the process of issuing the title, the relevant authorities seemed to respond indifferently to them, with some saying that the land was in This company domain, that company, which is a factor that makes them very worried.
In response to Mr. Sun Pisey, Deputy Governor of Stung Hav District, in response to the request from the people that the location of the land requested by the people, it is still unclear with the private land of others. Therefore, he also asked the people to wait for a clear examination.
Separately, according to a source from Stung Hav District Hall, who asked not to be named, he revealed to the media that the people who applied for the title of the above title are not related to the private land of others or any company. A small percentage can only be associated with forage land, as the land has clear boundaries and roads as evidence.
Please note that according to the people, this location was originally in the territory of Cheung Ko commune, managed by the Prey Nob district administration. However, between 1996 and 2012, they were recognized by the Cheung Ko commune authorities as legal residents.
Later, during the end of 2012, the land where they lived was cut from Cheung Ko commune, Prey Nup district, into Village 1, Tumnup Rolok commune, Stung Hav district. After 2014, every time there was an election, they came to register to vote in Tumnup commune, Stung Hav district, never missing a moment until now.
