Understand the business: Officials urge investors to look at investing in the stock market because there are profit opportunities like real estate
(Phnom Penh): Experts say that while the real estate market in Cambodia is stagnant, it is an opportunity for the public to look back to investing in the stock market, because investing in stocks is profitable, not inferior to investing in real estate. .
Mr. Hong Sohour, the Royal Government Representative in charge of the Director General of the Stock Exchange of Cambodia, said that in the last 2-3 years, the real estate sector has grown slightly, which is an opportunity for those who have money to start considering investing. Investing in the stock market At the same time, some stock prices are now cheaper, which is an opportunity for the public to invest in the stock market to enter the market.
He said that in the same 10 years, investing in the stock market will be as profitable as investing in real estate, as investors increase every day.
At the same time, he showed good growth in stock trading, which increased from year to year, despite the crisis, but trading is still active.
He said that for those who are interested in investing in the stock market, and if there is not enough time to monitor the stock market can invest in a monthly savings of $ 50 to $ 100.
Chou Vannak, director general of real estate and mortgage regulators, said that for the real estate sector over the last two years, due to the effects of the spread of Kovid 19 and the effects of the Russia-Ukraine war, it has led to buying activity. Sales have slowed significantly, but low-cost real estate is still growing well due to the government's preferential treatment of stamp duty.
He added, however, that investors can have different investment options according to their preferences.
Please be informed that currently the Cambodia Securities Exchange has 16 listed companies, of which 9 companies are listed as shares and 7 are listed as bonds.
Farmers in Banteay Meanchey Province: Blocking the flow of water into the Tonle Sap Lake, leading to chronic flooding in various geographical areas in Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): For the last three years, Banteay Meanchey has become a province in the northwest of the country, often flooded by rain and runoff from other areas. The sinking lasted longer and the receding was slower. The reason for the slow decline is that the farmers suspect that it is due to the obstruction of the water that flows into the Tonle Sap Lake.
Banteay Meanchey is a province that is rarely flooded, but in the last three years, one of Cambodia's rice barns has always experienced more severe flooding than other provinces, and also affected the rice crop of farmers. In 2022, Banteay Meanchey province was also severely flooded and until now the water has not receded.
Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, said that this year's floods affected eight cities / districts, including Serei Sophorn, Poipet, Mongkul Borei, Phnom Srok, Preah Net Preah, O'Chrov, Thmor Puok and Malai districts.
Mr. Hay Soeun, 59, and Mr. Ma Vanna, 60, farmers in Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province, also expressed surprise at the flooding in their district. Both farmers pointed out that there could be two reasons for the flooding. The first reason is the amount of rainfall and runoff from other areas and the second reason is due to the obstruction of the water flow to the Tonle Sap Lake due to various infrastructures.
Mr. Hay Soeun and Mr. Ma Vanna want to study and restore the drainage system to the Tonle Sap Lake as soon as possible to relieve the chronic flooding in the villages and farms of the people in Banteay Meanchey province.
During the distribution of rice seeds to farmers under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, Sunday, October 23, 2022, Mr. Oum Rath also asked Samdech Techo Hun Sen to restore two streams to help speed up the flow of water. Also in Banteay Meanchey province.
The two streams that the provincial governor requested to be rehabilitated are: O'Nhor, which borders Banteay Meanchey and Battambang with a length of 27 km and O'Rumduol, 22 km long, located in Preah Net Preah district.
Water resources experts claim that if there is no study to restore the water flow from Banteay Meanchey to the Tonle Sap Lake to wide and fast flow, Banteay Meanchey will face annual flooding from rainfall and Water flows from other areas.
