The Paris Agreement was internationally recognized as an agreement to end the civil war in Cambodia, which took place on October 23, 1991.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled the negotiations that began with the Sihanouk-Hun Sen negotiations in Indonesia. He reminded that in 1989, the five permanent members of the UN Security Council did not participate in helping to solve Cambodia's internal problems until 1990.
"This negotiation paves the way for the Cambodian side to do nothing if it does not talk to each other. Like the framework for the establishment of the High National Council, it is an important part of the process," he said. The Paris Agreement itself is not the organizer, the Khmer organizers.
The agreement has become the subject of opposition groups attacking the Royal Government of Cambodia, accusing it of violating the spirit of the Paris Agreement. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered that both people and people were expressing their opinions incorrectly and were not in the same situation as Samdech.
The prince asserted, "I myself have attended every meeting, but I am afraid that those who do not attend the meeting will interpret it better than I do. "Just being right is wrong."
The Paris Agreement established a provisional authority called UNTAC. King Techo stated that UNTAC did not resolve all issues until after UNTAC's departure left Cambodia with two territories and two governments, one government. Help is an elected government, while the other belongs to the Khmer Rouge in the western part of the country where the Khmer Rouge later seceded in 1996.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded that in the Khmer Rouge area, even President UNTAC could not enter the area, but Samdech Techo entered the Khmer Rouge area and worked to unite the Khmer and Khmer until complete peace. Today.
Samdech Techo further stated that Samdech always told the Minister of Agriculture, both previous and current generations, to be careful not to be called "seedless", which means not to eat even the seeds for cultivation.
Samdech Techo stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set up a food reserve committee, which includes rice, rice and other crops to protect and ensure food and seed security in the event of a disaster.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this statement on the occasion of Samdech distributing more than 500 tons of rice seeds to more than 5,000 families in Banteay Meanchey province this morning, October 23, 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that according to the Minister of Agriculture, Mr. Dith Tina, until now, the Royal Government has released 7,000 tons of rice seeds to intervene and to distribute to people affected by the floods. So that they can recover quickly.
Samdech Techo stated that through the distribution of rice seeds, the new Minister of Agriculture, who inspected these days, found that rice seeds have grown well, but what is found is that some farmers because the rice seeds are too thick. Which requires guidance related to cultivation techniques to additional farmers.
Samdech Techo instructed the new Minister of Agriculture to appoint agricultural experts to explain and guide farmers about sowing rice and using fertilizers to reduce costs and get high yields.
The reiteration of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the founder of the Paris Peace Accords, marks the 31st anniversary of the establishment of the Paris Peace Accords (October 23, 1991 - October 23, 2022), an agreement concluding Darkness on the tragic land of Cambodia brings the pages of a new era: peace and the end of the war, the end of the conflict between Cambodians and Cambodians that occurred for nearly three decades.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, during a meeting to distribute more than 500 tons of rice seeds to more than 5,000 families in Banteay Meanchey province, said that after the Paris Peace Agreement, the war in Cambodia was not completely closed at that time. UNTAC has spent more than $ 2 billion, leaving Cambodia with two jurisdictions and two governments, the elected government and the Khmer Rouge government.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "What the Paris Agreement wants, but UNTAC can not achieve is that when UNTAC has spent $ 2 billion and withdrawn, leaving Cambodia with control. 2 and 2 governments in Cambodia. "One government came out of the election and the other was the Khmer Rouge government."
Samdech Techo Prime Minister also reminded that the location where Samdech is here is in Malai, Kamrieng, Phnom Proek, Sampov Loun, Pailin, Samlot, Koh Kong, etc., in the past under the control of the Khmer Rouge.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, what made Cambodia successfully end the chronic war was the win-win policy set out by the prince, along with loyal operators, to end the war without the use of ammunition. Samdech continued that it was not until the beginning of 1998 that Cambodia fully integrated between the Khmer Rouge army and the army of the Royal Government.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that without the role of Prince Norodom Sihanouk and without the procession of political parties participating in the election, it is clear that so far the United Nations has not withdrawn. Already out of Cambodia. He said that after the election, there were many incidents, including the rejection of many elections, but under the auspices of His Majesty the King, a compromise was reached.
This historic agreement has three main objectives: First, to restore peace in Cambodia through the implementation of a ceasefire and disarmament of the four Cambodian conflicting parties. The foundation of democracy in Cambodia through the holding of elections to the Constituent Assembly; and third, to protect the sovereignty, independence, integrity and inviolability of the territory, neutrality and national unity of Cambodia.
