Young people are starting to use the riel as the riel plays an important and comprehensive role in their lives
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia has continued to promote the riel for the fourth time in Kampong Cham province, with the support and participation of the masses, especially the youth, because they understand that the riel is the identity of the nation. The National Bank of Cambodia continues to disseminate the riel in many provinces to spread the knowledge and benefits of using the riel to the Cambodian people.
In fact, on October 22, 2022, the National Bank of Cambodia continued to promote the riel in Kampong Cham province with the participation of Dr. Chea Serey, Deputy Governor and Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia and Mr. Ly Sararith, Deputy Governor. Kampong Cham province, as well as many government officials, bank owners and students.
On the day of the riel promotion, it was observed that some young people who participated in the riel promotion program were happy when there was a Khmer Riel exhibition and benefited from the importance of the riel. They are determined to continue to support the riel.
Dr. Chea Serey said that this program was held to show the contribution to promote the use of the riel of the nation, which allows people, traders to take old banknotes or tear new banknotes, organize exhibitions on History of Riel, answer quizzes to win prizes and watch concerts at night.
Dr. Chea Serey added that in the last two decades, the riel in circulation has increased by 16%, deposits in riel have increased by 29% and loans in riel have increased by an average of 38% per year.
According to a survey conducted by the National Bank of Cambodia in collaboration with the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in 2017, the riel has gained more trust and use, especially for daily expenses, especially in rural areas. . The riel plays an important and comprehensive role in life, whether it is income, expenses or savings.
Separately, for Kampong Cham province, according to the survey data, 79% of people use most of the riel (more than 80%) in their daily expenses. Check out the main gallery of international events on October 22, 2022!
