(Phnom Penh): Due to the pressure of heavy rain, causing the water to not flow on October 22, 2022, with the guidance of Mr. Cheng Monira, Governor of Chbar Ampov district to solve the difficulties of the people affected. During the flood, Mr. HOT Kimny, Deputy District Governor, led a team to install machinery to open the waterway from Koh Nora village in Niroth and Prek Pra communes, Chbar Ampov district, Phnom Penh.
Mr. HOT Kimny said that in recent days, he led a team to install drainage equipment from the flooded area in Sangkat Niroth and Sangkat Prek Pra, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh, which suffered from flooding.
Mr. HOT Kimny confirmed that in the past, the Boeung Prolit market area used to be flooded every time it rained because the flood water from the lake to the Boeung Prolit market area caused the water to flow into the sewer too slowly and caused the flood until the district governor Chbar Ampov installs machinery with the authority of the authorities, with the volunteer of the villagers together to build a dam to prevent water from flowing into the house.
Regarding the installation of drainage canals from Sangkat Niroth and Sangkat Prek Pra, the people living in this market area thanked the Khan and Sangkat Prek Pra authorities for using force to lift the dam day and night. Until the dam is successfully lifted.
It should be noted that the Chbar Ampov district authority has already built a 600-meter-long drainage system with a diameter of 6 meters to help prevent flooding of houses in O'Andong 1 village, Prek Pra commune.
