Minister Thong Khon and Mrs. and officials of the Ministry of Tourism marched to Svay Chi Ok pagoda, Baray district
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, and Ms. Nhek Sim Thong Khon, together with leaders and government officials under the Ministry and their families, on October 22, 2022, celebrated the Kathen Donation Ceremony at Ampavannaream Pagoda. Called Wat Svay Chi Ok, located in Baray District, Kampong Thom Province.
The Kathen Donation Ceremony started on the afternoon of October 21, 2022 with the participation of leaders, government officials, relatives and close Buddhists gathered at the residence of the Minister and Mrs. in Tuol Kork, Phnom Penh to celebrate. Krong Pali performed the song of Preah Rattanatray and invited the monks to give a sermon under the presidency of Bhikkhu Chirpanho Kou Sopheap.
On the morning of October 22, 2022, Minister Thong Khon and Mrs. Nhek Sim Thong Khon, together with government officials, families and Buddhists, marched in a car from the Minister and Mrs. to Svay Chi pagoda. Ok Na, Baray district, Kampong Thom province, to give to the monks who have been waiting for the rain for three quarters.
Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Distributes More Than 500 Tons of Rice to More Than 5,000 Families in Banteay Meanchey
(Banteay Meanchey): In the morning of Sunday, October 23, 2022, tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, donated more than 500 tons of rice seeds to more than 5,000 families affected by floods.
Meeting with farmers on the 31st anniversary of the Paris Peace Agreement (October 23, 1991-October 23, 2022) tomorrow, in addition to providing rice seeds, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also prepared food packages and budgets for farmers to Solve difficulties in life as well.
Banteay Meanchey is a province in the northwest of the country that has been severely flooded by floods this rainy season.
Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, said that the floods and rains from Thailand also affected 8 cities / districts, including: Serei Sophorn, Poipet, Mongkul Borei, Phnom Srok, Preah Net Preah, O'Chrov, Thmar Puok and Malai district.
With this disaster, the authorities and the armed forces in the province have been active to help evacuate people from the flood and help solve various problems.
At the same time, Mr. Oum Rath and Mr. Kheng Sum, Chairman of the Provincial Council, visited and distributed gifts from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to the people affected by the floods.
Please note that in addition to providing rice seeds to farmers in Banteay Meanchey, the next day, Samdech Techo will travel to Battambang, Pursat and Kampong Chhnang to distribute rice seeds and food to the victims.
Mrs. Khuon Khundy and Oknha Kuy Leang Ky Initiated 136 Million Riels in Charity Donation to Wat Angkor Touch South in Siem Reap Province
(Kampong Thom): Ms. Khuon Khundy, Senator and Mr. Oknha Kuy Leang Ky, as well as leaders and Buddhists from near and far, marched in a procession to pay their last respects to the monks at Wat Angkor Touch South in Siem Reap province on October 22, 2022, collecting more than 136 million riels.
She added that after the victory on January 7, 1979, the field of Buddhism has been revived to this day, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, leading the country towards peace and development in all fields, both Buddhist and imperial. By ensuring political stability, completely extinguishing the chronic war in Cambodia.
Minister Thong Khon leads a group of Vietnamese volunteer doctors to treat 1,000 people
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Kampong Thom province on October 22, 2022, led a group of Vietnamese volunteer doctors to treat 1,000 people in the district. Baray and Taing Kork district.
He said that the types of diseases to be examined and treated include diseases related to the digestive system, respiratory system, heart, blood vessels, muscles and skeleton, health effects caused by Kovid-19 disease, ultrasound examination, ultrasound and midwifery.
Mr. Thong Khon added that Vietnamese doctors brought 1,000 packages of medicine and medicine to the people at a cost of about $ 40,000. At the same time, the Vietnamese team also prepared food for people old and young, such as chicken porridge, popcorn, fried meatballs, fried chicken and other cakes.
It should be noted that a group of Vietnamese volunteer doctors have examined and treated the Cambodian people eight times, and the total population is already more than 20,000, including two in Baray and Taing Kork districts. Lift (both this time).
Samdech Techo Youth Volunteer Doctors Provide Free Medical Treatment in Siem Pang District, Stung Treng Province
(Stung Treng): Samdech Techo Youth Volunteer Doctors (TYDA) on October 22, 2022, provided free medical check-ups and treatment to people, families, army, police, military police and retired soldiers in Siem Pang district. Stung Treng Province.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Phay Bunchhoeun, Chairman of the Stung Treng Provincial Assistance Team, and Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Stung Treng Province, and Dr. Sou Siphana, Executive Director of the Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association (TYDA), representing Dr. Hun. Manet and Mrs. Pech Chanmony, as well as members of the provincial council, deputy governors and provincial leaders, the youth of the CPPCC, the youth of the Cambodian Red Cross in Siem Pang district.
Dr. Su Siphana said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as Dr. Hun Manet and Mrs. Pech Chanmony always consider the health and well-being of the people and always make it easier to treat the people. Arrive and send people with serious cases to Phnom Penh for treatment under the full support of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
On that occasion, Mr. Svay Sam Eang and Mr. Phay Bunchhoeun expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for taking care of the well-being and well-being of the people through free medical examination and treatment. Citizens whose humanitarian activities have helped alleviate the cost of living.
He requested the volunteer doctors to continue to visit, consult and treat the people in the future in order to improve the well-being of the people and together reduce poverty while the country is at peace. The provincial governor considers this program as a good humanitarian activity of the Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association (TYDA), which provides free medical check-ups to the people today.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng will lead a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to attend the official opening ceremony of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates
On the occasion of this business visit, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce in collaboration with the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia, the Ministry of Economy of the United Arab Emirates and the United Arab Emirates Chamber of Commerce and Industry organized the Cambodia-United Arab Emirates Business Forum with the participation of leaders of the country's ministries and institutions. Both and more than 70 companies in total.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, will address the forum, highlighting business opportunities, investment, economic situation and potential sectors of Cambodia to promote trade, investment, economic cooperation, digital sector development, small and medium enterprises and examine the possibility of cooperation. On a joint project between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates.
This business forum will take place on October 24, 2022 after the official opening ceremony of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates under the chairmanship of Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce of Cambodia and Mr. Dr. Thani bin Ahmed Al Zeyoudi, Minister of Foreign Trade of the United Arab Emirates.
