For Lee Chan-soo and Han Cheng, they are both old enough to retire. Li Keqiang, on the other hand, will step down as prime minister in March 2023 during the opening session of the annual session of the National People's Congress, as he has already served two terms.
Tomorrow, the new Central Committee will hold its first meeting to elect a new 25-member bureaucracy, and most importantly, the bureaucrats' standing committee. It is the largest and most powerful body in the Chinese Communist Party and has seven members, led by General Secretary Xi Jinping.
On the same day, Xi Jinping is expected to be re-elected as party secretary general for a third term and head to the presidency for a third term in March next year. Of the seven members of the Politburo Standing Committee to be announced on Sunday, one will be Li Keqiang, the new Chinese prime minister.
All four are current members of the Standing Committee of the Politburo, the most influential body in the Chinese Communist Party. Lee Chan-soo and Han Cheng are expected to retire at the age of 68. In March 2023, Li Keqiang will also step down as prime minister after two terms.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration and Provincial Department of Culture Organize an Exhibition of More Than 50 Types of Khmer Cakes Showcasing the Preservation and Development of Intangible Cultural Heritage, the Soul of the Khmer Nation
(Preah Sihanouk): In order to preserve and develop the ancestral heritage left for the next generation of Khmer children, on the afternoon of October 21, 2022, Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration and Provincial Department of Culture and Fine Arts organized the first Khmer Cake Exhibition 2022 in The Cultural Center is located on Street 827, Village 1, Sangkat 1, Preah Sihanouk Province.
Mr. Kong Viphanak, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, said that the efforts to mobilize human resources who have knowledge in packaging, cooking and decorating many Khmer cakes have brought about 50 kinds of Khmer cakes to be displayed at the Cultural Center. Sihanoukville Province.
He added that there is another type of cake called Nom Krap in Svay Rieng and Prey Veng provinces. Cooked on the grill and set on fire, they are kept for a long time to receive guests, for gifts at weddings, or to visit friends and relatives.
He hopes that at the next exhibition we will definitely see other types of cakes. In addition, the provincial Department of Culture and Fine Arts has set up other cultural events, such as traditional costumes for weddings, religious ceremonies.
