(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, October 23, 2022, posted a message congratulating the 31st anniversary of the 23 October Paris Peace Accords.
The message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen is as follows:
Despite the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991, the civil war in Cambodia continued, sparked by Democratic Kampuchea (Pol Pot). Under Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy, the civil war was completely ended in 1998, in which Cambodia throughout the country has known complete peace and prosperity to this day. This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen distributed more than 500 tons of rice seeds. To more than 5,000 families in Banteay Meanchey
Meeting with farmers on the 31st anniversary of the Paris Peace Agreement (October 23, 1991 - October 23, 2022) Today, in addition to providing rice seeds, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also prepared food packages and budgets for farmers to solve Difficulties in life, too.
At the same time, Mr. Oum Rath and Mr. Kheng Sum, Chairman of the Provincial Council, visited and distributed gifts from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to the people affected by the floods.
In the case of the police stopping a car without a license plate on National Road 41, Kampong Speu Province, the police returned the car to the owner without any fine, just education and guidance
(Phnom Penh): The Department of Traffic Police and Public Order of the General Commission of the National Police stationed on National Road 41 in Kong Pisey District, Kampong Speu Province stopped a gray Prius without license plate and identification card. The authorities did not impose fines, only education and guidance.
It was not until October 12, 2022 that the traffic police contacted them to come and solve the problem by attaching the car documents with them. There are no fines and no fees.
(Pursat): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, presided over the organization of the 5th Khmer Literature Festival "Living Legacy of Literature" on the night of October 22, 2022 at Pursat High School. This festival is held every year to promote the value of Khmer literature to be stronger going forward.
The 5th Khmer Literature Festival will be held from October 21-23, 2022, with the aim of commemorating and reflecting the values of writers who survived the Pol Pot regime. The 5th Khmer Literature Festival also features performances of cardamom and peacock dance in Pursat province, a drama about a thief.
On that occasion, Mr. Khieu Kanharith said that these veteran writers have contributed tremendously to help spread knowledge, entertain the people in the society and connect the literature of the previous generation and the next generation, especially as a motivator. To the next generation of writers to develop the field of Khmer literature to grow more.
"These values should be upheld, respected and remembered by the people, the same authors, readers and relevant institutions," he said.
He added that the Khmer Literature Festival was established in 2017 with the aim of cultivating the spirit of national literature, promoting the honor and values of writers and increasing communication opportunities and expanding the market scope for writers.
Every year, the Khmer Literature Festival changes from one province to another, bringing new topics and major events to the participants to explore and entertain, such as discussion forums, seminars, cultural visits, literary heritage exhibitions, competitions related to literature and the performing arts.
Minister Khieu Kanharith expressed his support for the 5th Khmer Literature Festival and hoped that the festival would be held every year to further strengthen the value of Khmer literature.
At the same time, Minister Khieu Kanharith and she contributed an additional $ 500 to the festival.
It should be informed that the organizing committee of the 5th Khmer Literature Festival expressed its deep gratitude to the ministries, institutions, organizations and philanthropists, especially the support of the Minister and Mrs. is a good gesture and a good example and a driving force. It is important to encourage and motivate the team of the Khmer Literature Festival, especially the youth to continue to work with pride for the sustainability and progress of national literature.
