Dissemination meeting of "Cambodia-China-Laos Transport Cooperation and Vocational Education" aims to exchange views on transportation between the three countries
(Phnom Penh): The Outreach Meeting of "Cambodia-China-Laos Transport Cooperation and Vocational Education" was held on Zoom Video Online with the participation of the Cambodian Association of Transport and Supply Chains, Transport Institute Nanjing Logistics and Technology Co., Ltd., the representative office of the Lao Chamber of Commerce in China and a number of transport companies' enterprises attended the meeting.
The meeting was held on October 21, 2022 under the chairmanship of Ma Yaowen, Director of the Office of Modern Logistics Management Studies and Research from the Nanjing Institute of Transportation and Vocational Technology, China.
During the meeting, the participants exchanged views on the current situation of education and vocational training in logistics, multilateral trade, logistics and logistics services, and industrial and educational integration between institutes and enterprises in China, Cambodia and Laos.
With the frequent development of China, Cambodia and China, Laos, economic and trade activities, bilateral and multilateral cooperation projects are fully underway, bearing fruitful results in the fields of economy and trade, logistics services and even launching. High demand for multilateral integration of production and education and talent training.
In 2021, the China-Laos railway will be officially opened, opening a new transport corridor between China and Southeast Asia, and adding new impetus to the Lao economic recovery and economic flow to Cambodia. .
The Nanjing Institute of Transport and Vocational Technology of Cambodia, the Association of Cambodian Freight and Supply Chain Traders and the Lao Chamber of Commerce in China are cooperating in the field of logistics and education, which will set a precedent for international cooperation between China. Laos and Cambodia.
At the meeting, Yang Donglun from the Lao Chamber of Commerce in China introduced vocational education cooperation and education integration projects in the Lancang Mekong countries and set out strong expectations for the project. International cooperation of transport enterprises and cooperation for regional economic development and training of transport professionals.
Mr. Chea Chandara, President of the Association of Freight Forwarders and Supply Chains in Cambodia, shared the important achievements of economic and trade cooperation between Cambodia and China and expressed his sincere intention to work together. Business cooperation and education and training in transportation and economy and trade.
Ma Yaowen introduced the experience of logical vocational education, sharing the characteristics of vocational education by seizing the opportunities of human resource development, discipline competition and international cooperation of four-dimensional integrated teaching methods of the "Curriculum Certificate". Competition and Innovation ”of specializing in logistics and logistics management.
Please be informed that this outreach meeting opened a new situation of international cooperation among the three countries, with the expectation that the cooperation between the three institutions will be the new highlight of the Mekong-Lanchang Education Coalition, which relies on multidisciplinary interaction. Parties and cooperation between industry, trade and education. US, Russian defense chiefs discuss Ukraine war in rare telephone conversation
