Dr. Chea Serey: The riel has contributed significantly to the restoration and building of economic and social sovereignty
(Kampong Cham): In the dissemination workshop on the riel this morning, October 22, 2022, Dr. Chea Serey, Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, stated that in the past 42 years, the presence of the riel has contributed Important in restoring and building economic and social sovereignty.
She said that these proud achievements can be achieved under the roof of peace, political stability and development in all fields with the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, which makes the people and investors trust. Stronger on the riel and the future of the Cambodian economy.
"However, the practice of using the US dollar has deepened the economy and society, especially the mindset of the people, which will continue to require more participation in the promotion," she said. The use of the riel from all stakeholders, including ministries, public and private institutions, companies, enterprises and the general public.
She said that the greater use of the riel will enable the National Bank of Cambodia to implement more effective monetary and exchange rate policies aimed at stabilizing prices as well as protecting people's purchasing power.
Deputy Governor of Kampong Cham province, Mr. Ly Sararith, also said that the socio-economic development of the nation in general and the economy of the region or Kampong Cham province in particular could not go smoothly without the national currency acting as an oil. Smooth to facilitate investment activities, production and trade to be lively.
The Deputy Governor continued, "However, in the past, he has observed the spending of riel in Kampong Cham by a lot of people should be proud, especially daily expenses such as food, drinks, clothes and travel. Although Kampong Cham has been becoming an important economic pole and an attractive tourist destination for foreign tourists, it has brought a lot of foreign currency revenue to the people in the province.
The Deputy Governor took the opportunity to encourage people and companies-enterprises present in Kampong Cham to use the riel instead of foreign currency more because the riel is our national currency.
(Siem Reap): Achievements supporting the livelihood of the people in the Run Ta Ek Development Area are beginning to take shape. The presence of all those achievements made the people more confident in the development work in the Run Ta Ek development area and they started to build houses and come to live in the Run Ta Ek area as well.
Run Ta Ek Development Zone is a new village organized by the Royal Government for people to volunteer to leave the Angkor resort and other areas of the APSARA Authority. The Run Ta Ek development area covers a total area of more than 500 hectares and nearly 6,000 families have been relocated.
Currently, the construction of hospitals, schools, markets, roads, land preparation, housing, electricity and water supply are being done simultaneously.
The report shows that the clearing of plots reached 431 hectares, equivalent to 76.20% of the total area of 566 hectares. Construction of red gravel road using 220 people and 194 machines, the construction of red gravel road reached 57 km, equal to 40.71% of the total length of 140 km. Fill up 283 plots of land for the people.
The construction of two secondary and high schools with 24 two-storey high schools has completed about 20%. One office building and one library with 3 rooms achieved 20% results.
In particular, the construction of a health center, including a general ward, maternity ward and a doctor's dormitory, 2 floors, 20 rooms, achieved about 20%. The construction of a market with 8 houses, each measuring 20 meters x 40 meters, achieved about 15%.
Water System Rehabilitation The Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation has planned to build a 17-kilometer water transmission system to the Run Ta Ek Development Zone from Angkor Market along National Road 66 to the location of the Run Ta Ek Development Zone at a cost of About $ 3 million is being processed.
Through these achievements, the people who volunteered to live in the Run Ta Ek area have more confidence and trust in the development plan of the Royal Government.
Many people have moved in to build homes and some have even started trading on their land.
Residents who have moved in and arranged for the construction of houses in the Run Ta Ek area say they have high confidence in the government's development projects. They also expressed their pleasure at coming to live in the Run Ta Ek development area as there is a lot of support infrastructure such as roads, water, electricity, schools, hospitals and markets that will make their lives easier.
Residents also expect that their livelihoods will improve with the construction of new livelihoods in the Run Ta Ek development area, as more people live there, which can be more conducive to doing business.
