MOSCOW (Reuters) - The Indonesian ambassador to Moscow said on Friday that the contract for the purchase of Su-35 fighter jets from Russia would remain in force as Jakarta had no plans to abandon it. This is according to the release by the news agency RT on Saturday, October 22, 2022.
In March 2020, Bloomberg reported that the Indonesian government had decided to cancel its contract to buy the Su-35 fighter jets due to budget shortfalls caused by the Kovid 19 crisis and the threat of US sanctions.
