The following is the sub-decree of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Cambodia-East Timor held a joint business forum related to tourism and trade
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia-East Timor has organized the first business forum on tourism and trade for peace and sustainable development.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon said that the people are really satisfied with the remarkable progress of Cambodia-East Timor cooperation in all fields. The East Timorese President's state visit will push cooperation to the next level.
He said yesterday two documents had been signed between the two countries, an agreement on air transport services and a memorandum of understanding on rice trade. All this will open up more opportunities for boosting trade between the two countries, people-to-people connections, including tourism.
In addition, bilateral cooperation, exchanges and friendship will be further strengthened through multilateral cooperation, which Cambodia and East Timor have always supported each other. In this regard, the Royal Government of Cambodia reaffirms its full support for East Timor's ASEAN membership.
He added that today's forum is attended by the private sector and public institutions, which will be a prominent event focusing on exploring and exchanging views for business and investment opportunities between the two countries. The forum will cover many other areas of cooperation and joint project development under the theme: Tourism and Trade for Peace and Sustainable Development.
