General Department of Identification calls on citizens to check their ID cards in case they expire, at least 90 days to be replaced (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): General Department of Identification, Ministry of Interior calls on citizens to check their Khmer identity cards Lest it expire and be used in the upcoming 7th National Assembly Election 2023.
In a letter received by Fresh News on October 21, 2022, the General Department of Identification stated that the new model of Khmer identity card is valid for 10 years from the date of issuance. Therefore, the identity card issued to citizens since June 2012 has gradually expired from June 2022 onwards.
In order to ensure the right to receive various services, especially the political right to use the Khmer Nationality Identity Card for the upcoming 7th National Assembly Election 2023, the General Department of Identification calls on the people who have the Khmer Nationality Identity Card. New model expired or less than 90 days left, please come and fill out the form to exchange your new Khmer identity card at the following locations:
* First: at the administrative police station, commune, sangkat or police inspectorate of municipalities, districts, Khans or one-stop shops of municipalities, districts, Khans or the Capital / Provincial Police Commission of their residence.
* Second: Khmer Nationality Identity Card Department (Sangkat Niroth, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh)
Please attach a new model of Khmer Nationality ID card that has expired or has less than 90 days left (and documentation in case of data change).
