(Kratie): On the evening of October 20, 2022, joint police forces cracked down on fishery crimes in Boeung Prang, Boeung Krou, Chai Eng and the floodplain of Chroy Veng in Kanhchor commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province.
The operation was led by Mr. Thim Seang Leng, Deputy Governor of Chhlong District, with the participation of Kratie Fisheries Administration District Officers and Prek Prasop Fisheries Administration Division in collaboration with Chhlong District Unity Command, Kanhchor Commune Council, Kanhchor Administrative Police Force and relevant fishing communities.
Mr. Mok Ponlok, Director of Kratie Fisheries Administration District, said that during the crackdown operation, the joint force dismantled and destroyed illegal fishing gear on the spot, including: 29 nets, 850 meters long, 32 nets. Drainage mouth, 3 barracks, 450 meters long, 3 barracks, 250 meters long, 80 bamboo poles and release 25 kg of mixed fish back into natural waters.
He added that on behalf of the competent authorities, he called on all fishermen not to use illegal fishing gear, such as fishing nets, which seriously destroy fishery resources, and asked the fishermen to fish as a family in order to maintain sustainable resources. Present to future.
