2: To the teachers at Hun Sen Prey Luong High School 7,500,000 Riels, 269 students each received 10,000 Riels and support for the program 2,600,000 Riels. France will stand by Cambodia and continue to provide assistance in international peacekeeping and security operations
The First Secretary of the French Embassy in Cambodia stated that peacekeeping is a noble task that requires more military forces and skills. The military is volunteering to work for peace, sacrificing his physical strength and even his life, they live within the framework of established laws and regulations. This requirement implies strong credibility and requires a high level of commitment, but not absolute.
He said that over the years, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the National Center have made significant contributions to Cambodia's overwhelming peacekeeping operations, with more than 800 alert forces present in the war zone. Karma At the same time, the quality of training is also enhanced.
He said that France has provided assistance to the NPMEC and the National Gendarmerie. The Gendarmerie course meets the requirements and norms of the United Nations and focuses on legal, technical, intervention and judicial skills. Security in accordance with the tactics and work of UN police officers.
He said that 2022 is the 30th anniversary of Cambodia being the host country of the United Nations Blue Hat soldiers, including the French peacekeepers, to contribute to the search for peace in the poor land. Full of conflict and torn apart by war. During the mission, four brave French soldiers sacrificed their lives for the cause of peace in Cambodia.
Mr. Ouch Borith recalled that after benefiting from the UN peacekeeping force, Cambodia's participation in the UN operation, which began in 2006, continues to be active in some countries. The most dangerous in the world. This success is inseparable from French support through training, as we have seen so far.
This training course is very appropriate and important in the direction of building and strengthening the capacity of the army to have professional skills, knowledge, practical skills, aimed at participating as law enforcement, crime prevention, refugee protection, delegation and Senior dignitaries of A. UN and countries with a mission in South Sudan.
He stressed that the recently completed training course is invaluable for both the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and for the Cambodian people: firstly, to provide additional knowledge and skills in the military and secondly: to build solidarity and friendship. Cooperation between our two countries, Cambodia-France.
"This year and in the future, Cambodia remains highly committed to continuing humanitarian activities by continuing to participate in the United Nations peacekeeping mission in the world," Ouch Borith said.
For the past 16 years, Cambodia has sent Blue Hat forces to join peacekeeping missions under the United Nations umbrella with 121 countries around the world. It is a matter of pride that so far Cambodia has sent a total of 8,302 troops to nine countries, including the Republic of Sudan, South Sudan, Lebanon, Cyprus, Syria, Chad, Mali and Central Africa, including 580 women. People.
Currently, 801 troops are on peacekeeping missions in four countries: Mali, Central Africa, Lebanon and Sudan, specializing in mine clearance, demining and unexploded ordnance, civil engineering, airport engineering, observation officers and officers.
