Timor-Leste President pays courtesy call on National Assembly President
Dr. Jose Manuel Ramos Orta, 72, led a delegation to Cambodia on October 19, 2022 for a three-day state visit from October 19 to 21, 2022. The visit was made at the invitation of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia.
During the state visit, Dr. Jose Manuel Ramos Orta paid a courtesy call on His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, and Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia. Royal Palace.
He also had separate meetings with Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The Prime Minister and the President of East Timor will preside over the signing ceremony of two important bilateral documents, including the Aviation Services Agreement and the Memorandum of Understanding on Rice Trade between the two countries.
Dr. Jose Manuel Ramos Orta also laid a wreath at the Independence Monument and laid a wreath at the statue of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the former King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
During his stay in Phnom Penh on the evening of October 19, Dr. Jose Manuel Ramos Orta also received a courtesy call from Dr. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army.
The President also has other programs such as public lectures at renowned universities in Phnom Penh, interviews with local media, as well as speeches at the first Cambodia-East Timor Forum on Tourism and Business. Sustainable development and peace.
José Ramos Orta visited Cambodia in 2003 as foreign minister and for a second time in 2011 as president.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs expects that the state visit of Dr. Jose Manuel Ramos Orta to Cambodia will further strengthen and deepen relations and cooperation in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks for the benefit of Mutual of the two countries. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Meets East Timorese President at Peace Palace (Photo inside)
