The Minister of Health announces the launch of the second phase of the Health Quality and Equity Improvement Project
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, on October 20, 2022, announced the launch of the second phase of the Quality and Equity Improvement Project, which took place at the Sofitel Phnom Penh Phokitra Hotel.
Minister Mam Bunheng stated that the implementation of the second phase of the Health Quality Improvement and Equity Project, which is the largest health project ever covered. On behalf of the Ministry of Health, "I am very proud to see this project emerge to support the implementation of the Health Strategic Plan leading to the achievement of global health coverage by 2030."
The first phase of the Health Quality and Equity Improvement Project was implemented from November 2016 to May 2023, focusing on sustainable financing and the implementation of key health system initiatives to improve accessibility. Quality health services for the target population. This project has made a significant contribution to improving the health of the Cambodian people in the last six years.
The Minister of Health said that significant improvements include equipment management, knowledge and staff capacity, prevention and control of infections, waste management, sanitation and support to expand the network of health centers with the construction of 45 additional health centers. Obstetrics and gynecology in 15 referral hospitals and construction of 2 more provincial hospitals.
He added that the Prime Minister also provided cash directly to pregnant women, workers and civil servants in poor families as an incentive to increase the nutritional status of both mothers and newborns up to 2 years old. Which has received great support and gratitude from the Cambodian people.
The second phase of the project to improve the quality and equity of health should draw lessons from successful experiences in the first phase by adding innovative interventions to avoid the challenges encountered in the implementation of the first phase and align with the priorities of the Royal Government to achieve coverage. Global Health through its Five-Year Action Plan (2022-2027).
The project has prepared four main components for implementation as follows:
*  Component 1: Promoting the use of equity funds and financial protection This component will support the government's vision of achieving universal health coverage (UHC) in Cambodia by 2030.
* Component 2: Strengthen the quality and capacity of health services, which will implement national quality health monitoring tools, as well as expand non-communicable disease services and community participation.
