Announcing the inauguration of the President of the Bar Association of the 14th mandate, Mr. Ly Chantola set 13 priority directions
(Phnom Penh): The Bar Association of Cambodia this morning, October 20, 2022, held a ceremony to announce the inauguration of Mr. Ly Chantola, President of the Bar Association of the 14th mandate in the office of the Bar Association after he was newly elected. Take this position again.
The event was attended by members of the Bar Council, the Secretary General, the Deputy Secretary General, the Director of the Department, the Director of the Bar Professional Training Center, all the staff and staff of the Bar Association, as well as the first generation of law students. 18 Many too.
Mr. Ly Chantola considered that the results of the referendum showed that the Union had given confidence and trust in the leadership of the Bar Association in his first term. The President of the Bar Association has a two-year term, and Mr. Ly Chantola became the President of the Bar Association in 2021, while 2022 is the second year of his first term.
For the second mandate of Mr. Ly Chantola, in order to continue the progress of the work of the Bar Association and continue to promote the excellence and prestige of the legal profession, he requested the active support of the members of the Bar Council on the direction of work. Some 13 priorities are as follows:
* 1: Continue to follow the policy and mission of the Bar Association set out to achieve the vision "Together for the excellence and prestige of the legal profession."
* 2: Continue to contribute to the Royal Government in judicial and judicial reform.
* 3: Continue to strengthen the effective implementation of the law on lawyers' statutes, ethics, internal regulations and decisions of the Bar Association.
* 4: Continue to review and discuss the law on the statute of lawyers to be amended in accordance with the current society and the interests of the legal profession.
* 5: Continue to examine and protect lawyers in their profession in accordance with the law in force.
* 6: Continue to monitor and take strict measures against lawyers in practicing the profession that does not comply with the laws and rules of the Bar Association and re-study the disciplinary mechanism of the Bar Association.
* 7: Continue to discuss and solve the problem of exercising the rights of lawyers at the judicial police stage.
* 8: Continue to take legal action against people who practice the legal profession illegally.
* 9: Continue to review, decide and prepare a mechanism to implement the decision on the honor of the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia for providing outstanding lawyers in assisting the Bar Association, the legal profession and social justice affairs.
* 10: Continue to strengthen the protection of the poor and the work of the Bar Delegation throughout the country and implement the policy No. 098 / SOC / 21 dated 5 February 2021 on free consultation and defense of the poor Fees.
* 11: Continue to disseminate and mainstream awareness and recognition of the role of lawyers in society, both nationally and internationally, including the implementation of the Lawyer Project at the grassroots level.
* 12: Continue to strengthen the quality, ability and skills of lawyers through regular training, workshops, study visits both inside and outside the country to respond to the social, economic and current developments of globalization.
