However, the request to make the village safe, the provision of various public services and environmental issues was not raised by the people to intervene. The forum was held in the presence of Mr. Mop Sarin, President of the Phnom Penh Municipal Council and Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
During the forum, residents said that the construction of a large building in Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkar Morn has severely disrupted their lives, made it impossible for them to sleep and cracked the walls and ceilings of their houses. .
They confirmed that the construction work started from 7 am until 5 am, and most of the night the construction company hit the foundation, making it impossible for them to sleep. In addition, residents also requested the construction of roads, sewers, and public lighting.
Regarding the request to build roads, sewers and public lighting, Mr. Keut Chhe said that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration requested the relevant district authorities and departments to study the impact, if there is no problem, we will solve it for them.
Chairman of the Phnom Penh Capital Council, Mr. Mop Sarin, said that the outreach and consultation forum of the Phnom Penh Capital Council focused on the direct concerns of the people, including security, order, environmental issues and local development issues. Authorities have heard and found a solution.
The Phnom Penh Capital Council Dissemination and Consultation Forum is held once a year to address all concerns, suggestions and requests of the people. But for the second year in a row, it was missed by the Kovid epidemic. The Kovid epidemic was taken seriously by the Royal Government, which vaccinated the people until the fourth and fifth rounds, which re-launched Cambodia as well as Phnom Penh.
New ideas in ancient Chinese sentences: benefiting the people as the basis of the law governing national governance
On October 16, 2022, the 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China opened in Beijing. Xi Jinping, on behalf of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, presented the work report to more than 2,200 delegates, saying: "Land is the people, people are the land. "The Chinese Communist Party is leading the Chinese people in the war of national liberation, defending the nation, to protect the dreams and aspirations of the people."
Improving people's lives is the goal of the Chinese Communist Party. China has built the world's largest population insurance network. Chinese people receive mechanical insurance when faced with risks such as old age, illness, unemployment, injuries while working, disability and poverty.
In 2021, the per capita income in China was 35,128 yuan, the total value of the Chinese currency for the past 10 years increased by 78%. The government has implemented a number of policies to enable the elderly to enjoy their old age, with the average life expectancy per capita reaching 78.2 years. Despite the 19 epidemics of Kovid, in 2020 and 2021, the average life expectancy of the Chinese population will continue to rise.
Keeping the people primarily for the benefit of the people is a clear symbol of the Chinese Communist Party. China has now built the world's largest education system, social security system and health system, one of the world's most secure countries, and the common aspirations for common prosperity are emerging. Of course.
Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, NEC, Press Release, Commencement of 2022 Voter List Registration and Registration at Commune / Sangkat Halls
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued a press release on the examination of the 2022 voter list and voter registration at Commune / Sangkat Halls starting on October 20, 2022. . This year's voter list and voter registration review lasts only 50 days, from October 20 to December 8, 2022, both Saturday and Sunday.
During the period of review of voter list and voter registration in communes / sangkats, Commune / Sangkat councils must close their voter registration offices for 3 days: on November 3, November 18 and December 2, 2022. To hold meetings with the voter registration team to monitor the implementation of voter registration and voter registration.
According to the report from the Capital / Provincial Election Secretariat, voter registration offices in commune / sangkat halls across the country were opened at 7:00 am on October 20, 2022 and went well without any challenges. Any obstruction. Based on the work calendar, the voter list review and voter registration in the commune is divided into three stages as follows:
* For the first 15 days, from October 20 to November 3, 2022, the voter registration office shall be open at the Commune / Sangkat Hall * For the next 25 days, from the 4th to the 3rd November 28, 2022 Voter registration offices are mobile in some villages in each commune * For the last 10 days, from November 29 to December 8, 2022, polling stations will be open. Returning to the commune hall.
The period of mobility of polling stations in villages, communes, sangkats, commune councils and voter registration teams can be adjusted according to the geographical situation and the actual situation to ensure that all eligible voters in the commune / sangkat have access. Come and register to vote safely.
Please be informed that only Cambodian citizens whose names are on the official voter list in 2022 will have the right to vote for the upcoming 7th National Assembly Election 2023. Therefore, all Cambodians who have not yet registered to vote or have just reached voting age should go and register to vote.
