He added that in addition, this agreement will bring benefits to both countries, such as:
* Establish closer ties in the field of civil aviation
* Cooperate to strengthen the safety and security of international air passengers
* Establish air transport links for both passengers and cargo
* Establish air transport services, connect people, culture and business between the two countries, as well as support the sustainable growth of aviation.
* Passengers will get new experiences, new destinations and new travel options with diversity.
It should be noted that up to now, the Kingdom of Cambodia has signed Air Transport Services Agreements (ASAs) and Memoranda of Understanding (MOUs) with 47 countries around the world.
