Dr. Hun Manet Meets and Discusses with East Timorese President
It should be noted that Dr. Jose Manuel Ramos Orta, 72 years old, led a delegation to Cambodia this morning for a three-day state visit from October 19 to 21, 2022. The visit was made at the invitation of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during the state visit, Dr. Jose Manuel Ramos Orta will pay homage to His Majesty the King of Life at the Royal Palace.
The President will also have separate meetings with Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
During his stay in Phnom Penh, Dr. Jose Manuel Ramos Orta will receive a courtesy call from Dr. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, giving a public lecture at a well-known university in the capital. Phnom Penh, giving interviews to local media as well as giving speeches at the first Cambodia-East Timor Forum on Tourism and Business for Sustainable Development and Peace.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs expressed the hope that the state visit of Dr. Jose Manuel Ramos Orta to Cambodia will further strengthen and deepen relations and cooperation in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks for the benefit of Mutual benefit of both countries.
