Senior officials of the Ministry of Rural Development inspect the flood situation in Banteay Meanchey province and put in place measures to solve
(Banteay Meanchey): On October 19, 2022, after the floods receded, Dr. Ouk Rabun appointed Mr. In Chantha, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Disaster Management Secretariat of the Ministry of Rural Development, and Mr. Chuob Ratana, Under Secretary of State and Deputy Chief of the Disaster Management Secretariat, as well as professional officers, inspect and assess the impact of rural infrastructure in Banteay Meanchey province.
Chea Yuthearun, director of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Rural Development, said that the floodwaters had receded by about 80 percent, but that the floodwaters had inundated 60 rural roads in Banteay Meanchey province, 621,936 meters long, and cut off 38 roads. , 785 meters, 143,200 meters long foot drain and 4 round drains.
Mr. In Chantha said that Banteay Meanchey province has been affected by floods for three consecutive years, which has caused damage to rural infrastructure, and the Ministry and the Disaster Secretariat have inspected the actual situation and reported to the leadership of the Ministry. Renovation for people to travel and facilitate farmers to transport other agricultural products.
