President of the Cambodian Rice Federation hopes that rice prices will improve by the end of this year as floods severely affect rice crops (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Duke Song Saran, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, hopes that in the heavy rice season In November, rice prices will rise if Europe has high demand for rice due to drought and climate change in some countries in the region.
He said that at present, ordinary OM rice costs between 830 riel to 930 riel per kilogram. As for the fragrant rice that has been harvested almost from the field, the price is between 1,100 riel to 1,200 riel per kilogram for wet rice, the price varies depending on the area.
He said heavy rice or wet rice will start harvesting in November. However, he worries that prolonged flooding over last year, which has damaged farmers' rice, could hamper exports next year.
Kien Narin, a farmer in Battambang province's Thmei Koul district, said more than four hectares of his paddy fields were almost completely damaged by the floods, causing severe losses as fertilizer prices doubled.
The new Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Dith Tina, began a mission to the provinces of Cambodia on October 19 to distribute rice seeds to flood-affected farmers to ensure that Cambodian farmers receive Rice varieties for replanting in time when the water recedes.
Senior NEC official: The 2022 voter registration procedure is simple and clear, and the posting will take place on the same day, January 13, 2023.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mean Sati, a member of the National Election Committee (NEC), said that the 2022 voter registration procedure is simple and clear and that the NEC can create the first voter list. Same time for communes across the country and posting on the same day, January 13, 2023, including the voter list, which will be removed from the voter list.
He said that during the review of the voter list and voter registration, the commune council must close the registration office every 15 days to meet with the voter registration team to discuss the work that has been done in the past and organize the work. To be continued.
Regarding the registration procedure, Mr. Mean Sati added that Cambodians living in communes who are at least 18 years old at the time of the National Assembly election (July 23, 2023) are born first or last. On July 24, 2005, those who are not yet on the voter list of the commune where they live can apply to register to vote.
He confirmed that the documents to be used for voter registration are that Cambodian citizens must meet directly with the voter registration team and present their Cambodian identity card to the head of the voter registration team. If the address on the Khmer Nationality Identity Card is in the commune where the resident is living, the voter registration team will arrange for registration in accordance with the NEC procedures.
If the address in the Khmer Nationality Identity Card is different from the Commune / Sangkat where the citizen is applying for registration, the citizen must bring a family book or residence book or a certificate of residence in the commune / sangkat that applies for registration.
NEC members also briefed on the procedures for obtaining residency certificates and the procedures for obtaining identification documents for voter registration.
Regarding the transmission of data, Mr. Mean Sati stated that during the examination of the voter list and voter registration, the voter registration team had to send the computerized data to the Department of Voter Data and Voter Registration every day for the Department to monitor the work. Regular.
He added that the registration procedure was simple and clear, and the NEC was able to create the first voter list simultaneously for communes across the country, and the posting would take place on the same day, January 13. 2023, including the list of voters who will be removed from the voter list.
For a Cambodian citizen living abroad to be able to register to vote, he or she must return to Cambodia to register to vote in the commune where he or she lives in accordance with the documents he or she has.
The NEC facilitates them to register first and return to work soon. The NEC will also appeal for his information on voter registration.
In response to the last question, the NEC informed that for those who do not have a Cambodian identity card used for voter registration, please go to the commune / sangkat where they live and vote. . Ministry of Mines and Energy Decides to Capital-Provincial Administration to Provide Administrative Services Related to Oil and Gas Sales and Distribution
