Senior officials of the Ministry of Cult urge students to respect teachers consistently
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Seng Somony, Secretary of State, Representative of Mr. Chhit Sokhom, Minister of Cult and Religion, urged students to respect their teachers consistently. He said that in ancient times, as long as the students met the teacher, the students worshiped, but now there is no such demand, that is, just show respect to the teacher enough.
The Secretary of State said this at the closing ceremony of the training course for primary school teachers for the 2022-2023 school year, organized by the National Inspectorate of Buddhist Studies of the Ministry of Cult and Religion for three days from 17 to 19 May. This October 2022.
"Teachers are our role models," the senior official said. In the Khmer language, all teachers and students must worship. From time immemorial, even when fighting, the students still worship the teacher. "But now we have changed our attitude and can not go to worship in the mud on the ground, just do it to show respect."
According to Chuon Nath's dictionary, "teacher" means one who is serious, one who should be respected, one who teaches students various arts. While instructing students to respect teachers, Mr. Seng Somony also instructed teachers to set a good example for students.
Taking that opportunity, Mr. Seng Somony spoke about the merits of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which made the realm of empire and Buddhism grow steadily. In particular, Samdech Techo has maintained peace, which gives everyone the opportunity to acquire knowledge to become good citizens in society.
Separately, the Secretary of State claimed that because of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the National Buddhist Studies continues to stand as an important educational institution, while the National Inspectorate of Buddhist Studies is the unit that governs the process of Buddhist education throughout the country, and this unit The incident happened a long time ago and continues to this day.
According to Mr. Seng Somony, the Royal Government has given us three important opportunities, including:
* First: Strive to protect our peace so that we have the opportunity to promote our Buddhist studies * Second: Give us the opportunity to maintain, concentrate and serve all aspects of Buddhism to support Buddhist studies * Third: The Royal Government helps Salary.
The training course for primary Buddhist teachers for the academic year 2022-2023, organized by the National Inspectorate of Buddhist Studies, was attended by 90 participants (39 priests, 47 males and 4 females). All 25 provincial capitals and all subordinates to the National Inspectorate of Buddhist Studies.
At the same time, Samdech Preah Pothivong also instructed all participants to use the knowledge gained from this training to better use to contribute to the promotion of education in Cambodia.
