45 Families Affected by Floods in Battambang Province Receive Donations from the Royal Government
(Battambang): Mr. Touch Channy, Director General of Social Services of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, this morning, October 19, 2022, distributed the donations of the Royal Government of Cambodia to 45 families living in safety on their backs. Ang Phas Dam is located in Doung village, Peam Ek commune, Ek Phnom district, Battambang province after flooding.
Each family received 25 kilograms of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 bag of fish sauce, 1 bag of fish sauce and some money. Nearly 3,000 families affected by the floods in Chi Kreng district received food. From the Royal Government
(Siem Reap): A total of 2,874 families affected by the floods in Siem Reap province's Chi Kreng district have received food, grain and rice seeds from the Cambodian Food System Management Committee.
The ceremony took place at Indras Ussa Pagoda (called Wat Chi Kreng) in Chi Kreng Commune, Chi Kreng District, Siem Reap Province this morning, October 19, 2022, under the presidency of Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, with the participation of relevant departments. Around the province and many people participate as well.
Mr. Tea Seiha said that the provision of food is the attention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Only the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo, has considered and continuously supported the affected people, families affected and vulnerable during the floods. Although this food is not much, but can facilitate the lives of the people for a while, this shows the attention of the Royal Government.
The provincial governor said that no party other than the Cambodian People's Party has helped the people in distress. In particular, the Cambodian Red Cross also always helps the poor.
Mr. Pov Bunthoeun, Governor of Chi Kreng District, said that the floods in Chi Kreng District from September 23, 2022 to October 17, 2022 affected 12 communes.
Among them, 2,720 families were affected, 2 children drowned, 172 families were submerged, 17 school houses were flooded, health centers were flooded, commune administration buildings were flooded, pagodas were flooded, and some road infrastructure was flooded. Damaged 2,316 meters, affected 2,779 hectares of rice and damaged 135 hectares, of which 52 hectares were rehabilitated, equivalent to 121 families.
He said that a total of 2,874 poor families affected by the floods received emergency food aid from the Royal Government and 121 families received rice seeds for them to plant rice during the rehabilitation period. When the water is gradually receding.
Siem Reap Provincial Administration confirmed that as of October 17, 2022, the distribution of food and food to the people affected by the disaster from the Food Management System of Cambodia more than 6,000 families. 10,450 families were affected by the floods in eight districts of Siem Reap province.
