Honorary Dr. Khuon Sodary Asks Mayor to Encourage Korean Investors to Invest in Cambodia
On that occasion, the Honorary Dr. Khuon Sodary also warmly welcomed the delegation from Kyungyu, Republic of Korea to visit Cambodia and especially to the National Assembly. She also recalled the invitation to attend the closing ceremony of the High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the closing ceremony of the Gyeongyu World Culture Expo 2019 in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do Province of the Republic of Korea.
It should also be noted that the first launch of the Gyeongyu World Culture Exhibition outside of Korea was held in Siem Reap, Kingdom of Cambodia in late 2006 under the auspices of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Republic of Korea. A total of 300,000 people watched with performances from 33 countries.
Taking this opportunity, HE Dr. Khuon Sodary also thanked the Republic of Korea for making it easier for Cambodian workers to work in Korea. She observed that due to various concerns, including health care, additional skills training with a decent wage, Cambodian workers were able to continue their work in Korea and help make a living. Their families are getting better.
At the same time, HE Dr. Khuon Sodary also mentioned the achievement of the new Cambodia-Korea Friendship Bridge across the Mekong River, which will start construction next year under the high initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, with a grant and Concessional loan from the Government of the Republic of Korea, which is a good bridge to serve the lives of the people in Cambodia.
In response, Mayor Kyung Yu agreed with Ms. Kittisangha Bandith that through the Korea-Cambodia bilateral relations, cooperation in many fields has really improved, including diplomacy, culture, tourism and industry. Trade and so on. In Korea, the birth rate is declining and the aging rate is rising, leaving Korea facing a labor shortage, including in Kyungyu.
Mr. Chou Nak-young also observed that many Korean companies came to invest in business in Cambodia, such as components, car parts, etc., and he also visited and gave a presentation at the Cambodian Polytechnic School, which is a training center for human resources before. Will go to work in Korea as well as meet politely and discuss with the Governor of Phnom Penh.
At the same time, Mr. Chou Nak-young also invited Ms. Kittisangbandit to lead the delegation to visit Kyung-U to learn more about the outstanding areas of Kyung-Yoo, such as cultural centers, history, tourism, agriculture, industry and engineering. The National Bank of Cambodia, the General Commission of the National Police and the Ministry of Justice show a joint position to take action to crack down on and eliminate illegal advertising and lending activities.
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia, the General Commission of the National Police and the Ministry of Justice have expressed their joint position on taking measures to crack down on and eliminate illegal advertising and lending activities to protect customers and improve financial literacy for local people. Getting timely on-demand banking is affordable.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak stated that the National Bank of Cambodia has been cooperating with the Ministry of Justice, the Provincial Courts, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Ministry of Interior, the National Police and the General Department of Taxation. Participation in supporting the collection of taxes for the government, the fight against money laundering and financing, terrorism and illicit trafficking.
The National Bank of Cambodia attaches great importance to mainstreaming financial awareness and consumer protection by organizing "workshops on microfinance in Cambodia" in provinces, cities and districts across the country.
He added that through the results of previous publications, the National Bank of Cambodia has become more aware of the challenges such as:
* Rural people do not fully understand the obligations and use of financial services, and do not have full access to financial information and find it difficult to seek clarification when there are problems or questions related to Use financial services.
* Local authorities find it difficult to distinguish between legal and illegal banking and financial institutions.
* A number of crooks have been conducting banking operations in the districts and communes, both lending and deposit collection services without proper and exploitative licenses.
Subsequently, the National Bank of Cambodia has issued a press release on the illegal promotion and provision of credit to provide additional information to the public about legal and official institutions that provide credit and other related services, as well as to increase vigilance. Especially for illegal and informal credit providers.
He stated that the National Bank of Cambodia has cooperated with the General Commission of the National Police and the Ministry of Justice to initiate today's workshop in order to:
1: Maintain more awareness to stakeholders about legal measures for illegal advertising and lending. 2: Introduce educational measures or guide people to understand the official banking services. 3. Take legal action against unlicensed banking providers.
"Not only that, it has affected the lives of the people as a whole, because advertising attracts people, business people in companies to borrow money and return it to demand high interest rates, as well as threats to security," he said. Of Cambodians and foreigners living in Cambodia.
He stressed that this is what requires joint institutions to prevent in this area.
The representative of the Ministry of Justice stated that the cooperation in organizing the workshop on "Measures and Suppression of Illegal Advertising and Credit Activities" of the National Bank of Cambodia, the General Commission of the National Police and the Ministry of Justice today showed the cooperation to stop all These illegal activities will protect the safety of the people.
The representative of the Ministry of Justice continued that the Ministry of Justice will continue to ensure justice and equality for all. The Ministry of Justice would like to express its position to cooperate with all competent ministries and institutions to take measures to prevent all illegal credit promotion activities in a timely and effective manner.
