Senior Minister Kun Kim and Mr. Dith Tina Distribute More Than 200 Tons of Rice Seed to Farmers in Kratie Province
(Kratie): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, and Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on Wednesday morning, October 19, 2022, went to distribute rice seeds. To farmers affected by floods in Kratie province.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Hoeur Siyem, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Vathorn, Provincial Governor, as well as many provincial officials.
205,350 kilograms of rice seeds distributed to farmers this morning. The rice was distributed to 2,702 families from Chhlong, Prek Prosop, Sambo, Chit Borei and Kratie districts.
During the ceremony, Senior Minister Kun Kim conveyed the cordial greetings and deep sympathy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all the people and expressed their regret for the impact. Of people born from floods.
The Senior Minister also briefed the people on Samdech Techo Hun Sen's consideration and attention on the work of rehabilitating farmers by assigning relevant officials to assess the immediate impact and transport rice seeds. Farmers as fast as possible.
The senior minister also informed the flood-affected farmers to consider releasing a budget to help solve the difficulties of the people who have been flooded for about three months.
"These are demonstrations of the care of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for the plight of our farmers. Even though Samdech is busy with national affairs and did not visit in person, the memories of Samdech Samdech are always with our farmers. ” This is what Senior Minister Kun Kim said during the rice seed distribution.
Senior Minister Kun Kim requested the provincial, district and commune authorities to cooperate with all relevant ministries and institutions to continuously implement Samdech Techo's regulations and assess the need to launch practical activities when the water recedes in accordance with Samdech Techo Hun Sen's priority strategic direction. In rehabilitating the lives of the affected people.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also encouraged people to pay attention to cooperating with the authorities to replant rice and crops to improve livelihoods after the flood.
In addition, the work of cleaning the environment in the community during the low tide and after the low tide is also a priority that the Senior Minister requested the relevant authorities and the community to participate in to prevent various diseases caused by unclean environment. Regarding the distribution of aid to the people, Senior Minister Kun Kim proposed to distribute it in small groups by distributing it directly to the locals.
