Mr. Sak Chankanharith, Governor of Por Senchey District, briefed on the progress report as well as the plan to implement the recommendations in the campaign to crack down on illegal gambling and illegal pawn shops in Cambodia this morning. October 19, 2022 at Por Sen Chey District Hall.
In fact, recently, the Po Sen Chey District Administrative Unity Command inspected all illegal gambling sites in 7 communes in the district from September 18, 2022 to the present and found illegal sites. A total of 32 people were arrested in 150 illegal gambling sites.
In that, 14 people were educated and handed over to their guardians, a total of 14 foreigners and 4 Cambodians (5 foreigners - 2 Cambodians handed over to the Khan Military Police to follow the procedure of 9 foreigners - Two Cambodians handed over to the district police inspector to follow the procedure) and all locations are closed. Currently, the Khan Administrative Unity Command will continue to regularly inspect other locations.
Separately, the Khan administration has invited local business owners of condominiums, hotels and guesthouses to educate, guide and contract to properly implement the measures of Phnom Penh and Khan administration without gambling, human trafficking, sex work. Production, distribution and use of drugs in 112 locations.
The report of Mr. Governor Sak Chankanharith confirmed that the inspection team of pawn shops in Po Sen Chey district has a total of 17 pawn shop business locations, including 2 in Sangkat Kakap I, 2 locations in Sangkat Choam Chao I, 2 locations in Sangkat Choam Chao II 2 locations and Sangkat Choam Chao 3 11 locations.
During the meeting and meeting with relevant authorities in Po Sen Chey district, Mr. Khleang Huot, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh also saw the efforts of the Board of Governors as well as subordinates to further improve the safety of the people. Citizens.
Mr. Khleang Huot also emphasized the recommendation of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, who received the high recommendation of the Head of the Royal Government on the prevention and suppression of illegal gambling as well as pawn shops in Phnom Penh. And the most serious.
Mr. Khleang Huot also urged the Board of Governors of Po Sen Chey district to take this issue as the main issue in implementation, especially to be responsible before the Royal Government, because the well-being of the people is the responsibility of all levels of authorities. Class. The deputy governor considers illegal gambling to lead to social instability and illegal pawnshops as a source of funding for illegal gambling, theft and drug use.
