Indonesia claims 74 children have died of severe kidney injuries this year
JAKARTA: At least 74 children in Indonesia have died of serious kidney injuries since January 2022, Indonesian health officials said on Wednesday. Increase. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, October 19, 2022.
The findings come after health officials in the Gambia said nearly 70 children had died of severe kidney injuries after using locally sold paracetamol to treat fever. Excess levels of pigments and sweeteners were found in four cough syrups manufactured by a New Delhi-based pharmaceutical company and marketed in The Gambia.
A team of health experts has been set up in Indonesia to investigate the spread of kidney injuries among children, with representatives from the Ministry of Health, the Indonesian Pediatric Association and the World Health Organization (WHO). .
