The Minister of Environment said that today's meeting will provide important input to disseminate information on the situation and risks caused by climate change in the world, in which Cambodia has also been negatively impacted. Socio-economic, livelihood and well-being of the people, although Cambodia is not a country that causes climate change.
Mr. Say Sam Al stated that this is an important forum for discussing the challenges and opportunities for the private sector and as a basis for decision-making for the banking sector and investors in financing and investing in projects. Environmentally friendly, resistant to climate change, contributes to reducing greenhouse gas emissions and access to new green technologies.
He said that Cambodia is the first of the 10 ASEAN countries and the second of the 46 least developed countries to adopt a carbon-neutral long-term development strategy set by 2050 and is committed to Support the "ASEAN Vision 2025" which focuses on the balance of economic development and environmental sustainability.
