(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, said that 20 years ago, Cambodia was a food insecure country, but now it has become a food exporter and the global hunger index has dropped. Down to 20.6% by 2020 and stunting for children under 5 has dropped from 50% in 2000 to 22% in 2022.
Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly made the remarks as he chaired a seminar on "Working together to fill the gaps in global action plans to address children's malnutrition" on the morning of the 18th. This October 2022 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Through this seminar, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly said that the purpose of raising funds to accelerate the progress of prevention, treatment of children with malnutrition and strengthen multi-sectoral cooperation to jointly promote food security and nutrition in Cambodia. .
The Deputy Prime Minister said that the food security and nutrition sector has played an important role in contributing to the development of human capital, increasing work efficiency, promoting economic growth and social progress. Urban development, migration, climate change, demographic change and economic and social progress have changed the way Cambodians live and eat.
