(Siem Reap): 3,454 flood-affected families in Kralanh and Srey Snom districts received donations from the Royal Government. Among them, 1,000 families from 10 communes in Kralanh district were affected by the recent floods and 1,454 families from 6 communes in Srey Snom district received rice seeds for Rehabilitation and 1,000 families in Tram Sor commune also received food.
In the program of visiting and distributing gifts to people from Kralanh and Srey Snom districts on October 17, 2022, there was also the participation of Senior Minister Kun Kim in charge of special missions and the first vice chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management. Disaster and Duke Seang Nam, Member of Parliament for Siem Reap Province, as well as relevant government officials around the province.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also highlighted the values of peace that are prevailing in Cambodia today, what the people get today is because Cambodia is peaceful. Therefore, we must work together to maintain peace and be grateful to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of peace.
It should be noted that a total of 1,000 flood-affected families from 10 communes of Kralanh district received emergency food aid from the Royal Government, including Sambour commune, Ta An commune, Kampong Thkov commune, Kralanh commune, Sranal commune, Rong Ko commune. Snoul, Krouchkor commune, Sen Sok commune, Chanlas Dai commune. Each family received 24 kg of rice, 1 can of Thai noodles, 1 can of fish sauce, 1 can of soy sauce, 1 can of fish and 1 can of Vital water.
In this program, there is also the distribution of rice seeds to the people in Kralanh district to restore the agricultural sector as the water has started to recede gradually. In addition, food was distributed to people in Srey Snom district who ran out of food during the floods, a total of 5,536 families. Battambang and Pailin provincial governors lead professional officers to inspect the geographical boundaries of the two provincial administrations to adjust the border
(Battambang): On the morning of October 18, 2022, the delegation of Battambang Provincial Administration led by Mr. Sok Lou, Provincial Governor and Pailin Provincial Administration led by Mrs. Ban Srey Mom, Provincial Governor led relevant officials from major departments in the province and stakeholders. Inspect the location in the administrative border between the two provinces.
