Japan decides to impose more sanctions on North Korea over missile test (Video inside) (Tokyo): Japan on Tuesday decided to impose additional sanctions on North Korea by freezing the assets of five entities. Involved in Pyongyang's missile and nuclear weapons development program. This is according to a Japanese government spokesman quoted by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, October 18, 2022.
Japanese government spokesman Hirokazu Matsuno said the additional sanctions were approved at a cabinet meeting on Tuesday morning after North Korea launched a series of missile tests. Into the Sea of Japan, including missiles fired over Japan.
Speaking to reporters, the spokesman added that North Korea's provocative actions are a serious and urgent threat to Japan's national security, as well as a threat to international peace and stability, which is absolutely intolerable. At the same time, Matsuno also urged North Korea to take concrete action to resolve a number of issues, including its nuclear and missile development programs, including the abduction of Japanese nationals.
