Tehran: Iranian Foreign Ministry spokesman Nasser Kanaani said on Monday that inconsistencies in the words and actions of US officials were a major obstacle to the revival of the nuclear deal. 2015. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Monday, October 17, 2022.
Speaking at a weekly news conference, Kanaani added that US officials had sent a message to express their views on the nuclear talks on the one hand, while expressing conflicting attitudes on the other.
He noted that Washington's approach failed to contribute to nuclear talks.
Al-Kanaani stressed that "there is reason to revive the nuclear deal and the return of all parties," but the current issue depends on the US government's political decision.
"We can return to the agreement" whenever the United States shows a necessary will, he added. However, Iran will not wait for an agreement.
Samdech Say Chhum and a High-Level Delegation of the Communist Party of Vietnam Discuss Continuation of Cambodia-Vietnam Cooperation
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP), on the afternoon of October 17, 2022, met with Mr. Vo Van Thuong, Member of the Politburo of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam at the 7 Makara Palace.
Both sides praised and welcomed the steady development of relations between the two parties and countries in the direction of "good neighborliness, traditional friendship, comprehensive cooperation, long-term stability".
The two sides exchanged information on the emerging situation of each party and country and exchanged views on the international and regional situation.
The two sides praised the bilateral cooperation in all fields in the past, including economic, security, health, education, tourism, culture and border issues. Which has grown significantly.
The two sides celebrated the 55th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries and the year of Cambodia-Vietnam friendship, in which the two parties and the two countries have been jointly organizing celebratory activities through the exchange of delegations. Visit of party, state and mass leaders of the two countries and congratulatory letters to each other.
The talks were held in a warm, friendly, understanding and trusting atmosphere to further deepen and deepen the traditional solidarity, friendship and cooperation in all fields between the two parties.
