SINGAPORE: Singapore and Vietnam have agreed to increase cooperation in areas such as digitalization and cyber security, a green economy and sustainable infrastructure, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MFA) said on Monday. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Monday, October 17, 2022.
During the talks, the two heads of state reaffirmed "comprehensive and strong economic cooperation" between the two countries, the Foreign Ministry said. They also agreed to increase cooperation in new and emerging areas such as digitalization and cyber security, green economy, including renewable energy and carbon credits, sustainable infrastructure, as well as vocational training.
