Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth urges new agriculture minister to prioritize flood relief
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on October 17, 2022, requested the new Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Dith Tina, to consider the work of addressing water impacts. Flooding is the first priority in the future.
The request was made on the occasion that Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, High Representative of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen, attended the inauguration ceremony of Mr. Dith Tina as the new Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries this afternoon. October 17, 2022 at the Ministry of Agriculture.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth stated, "I would like to ask Minister Dith Tina, leaders and civil servants at all levels of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to consider flood relief work as the first priority. In the future and better implementation of measures that have received high approval from Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
Speaking on this occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth highlighted the following:
First, continue to inspect and assess the impact and actual damage caused by floods on agricultural crops, livestock and aquaculture, especially to clearly identify the location of the damage, the size of the area and the number of affected farmers in collaboration with the Ministry. Institutions, especially relevant capital-provincial administrations, to be highly effective.
Second: Continue to campaign for the rehabilitation of flood-damaged farmland and bring rice, crop, fish and frog seeds to farmers in the affected provinces to respond. And the extent of damage to agricultural crops, livestock production and aquaculture that has occurred in the past.
Third: Introduce the leadership of the Ministry, specialized units under the supervision and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Capital-Province to cooperate in coordinating operations in response to this natural disaster and accelerate the rehabilitation of impacts in their target provinces. .
Fifth: Encourage professional units to pay attention to continue to monitor animal health, vaccination, prevention of various infectious diseases and prevent illegal movement of animals in the capital-province on a regular basis, including fisheries and forestry crimes. Well.
Sixth, to provide close cooperation with relevant institutions in collecting data on seed needs, rehabilitation area, victim identification and other information to put in place effective restoration measures and other social assistance.
