General knowledge: When did Cambodia first appear on the world map?
(Phnom Penh): Some ancient maps have been found to date from 16500 BC until the 6th century BC, when the ancient Greeks began to draw the first world map on paper. Later, the world map was also revised until now, but do you know when Cambodia was first included in the world map?
During the European colonial period, especially the older colonies such as Portugal, Spain, the Netherlands, etc., they first arrived in Southeast Asia, in 1498 AD, Portuguese troops invaded the Indian state of Goa and continued to arrive. Southeast Asia in 1511 to conquer Malacca.
During the late 15th and 16th centuries, Cambodia was between the late Chaktomuk and early Longvek periods, which were in turmoil due to both the war with each other and the war with the Siamese in Ayutthaya.
Historians record that in 1515, King Chan Reach (1515-1566) ordered 150 Canon cannons and 2,000 special artifacts, as well as some modern weapons to fight. Army of King Srey Chetha - King Kan. It was not until 1525 AD that King Chan Reach triumphed over King Srey Chetha and moved the capital to Longvek, now in Longvek commune, Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province.
At the beginning of the Longvek period, Cambodia began to strengthen close relations with the Portuguese and continued to have relations with other European colonies such as the Netherlands and France.
