Guest speakers: Representatives from the Ministry of National Defense. This afternoon, General Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth officially announced the inauguration of Mr. Dith Tina as the new Minister of Agriculture.
(Phnom Penh): The inauguration ceremony of Mr. Dith Tina as the new Minister of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries will be held on the afternoon of October 17, 2022 under the presidency of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Please be informed that His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, on the afternoon of October 14, 2022, issued a Royal Decree appointing Mr. Dith Tina as Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. The King issued a Royal Decree appointing Dith Tina as Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries at the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
On the morning of October 14, 2022, the National Assembly of Cambodia unanimously voted for Dit Tina to run for Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
The vote of confidence took place in a plenary session of the National Assembly chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, with the participation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and a total of 111 members of the National Assembly.
In this plenary session, Mr. Dith Tina, former Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, was unanimously elected by 111/111 members of the National Assembly to be the Minister of Agriculture.
Mr. Dith Tina was nominated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to be the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. This proposal was made after Mr. Veng Sakhon was terminated by the King of Cambodia on October 8.
This proposal is made in accordance with the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the Council of Ministers.
Mr. Dith Tina served as Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy from 2014 to the present, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce from 2013 to 2014 and Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce from 2009 to 2013.
Through the above roles and responsibilities, Mr. Dith Tina has been involved in leading the elimination of slum dredging business along the river, leading the working group to prepare the National Policy on Mineral Resources 2018-2028, leading the working group to draft the law on management. Petroleum and petroleum products and lead the drafting of laws on geographical indications.
Mr. Dith Tina was described by Samdech Techo Hun Sen as a good chess player.
