(Phnom Penh): This morning, Monday, October 17, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the graduation ceremony for 6,411 students of the National University of Management (NUM), 3,560 females. From them successfully graduated with overcoming many difficulties and obstacles.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen spoke for nearly 2 hours, the following are the main contents:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked all participants in the graduation ceremony to stand up and pay their respects to the boys and girls who died due to the sinking of the boat.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his condolences and shared the sad death with the family of the deceased.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expresses his deep gratitude to the King and Queen for donating the royal property and sharing his condolences with the family of the deceased.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the Armed Forces and the authorities for their joint efforts to rescue and search for the victims' bodies.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised Senior Minister Kun Kim for standing firm in the search operation for the victims.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the boat sinking incident showed the cooperation and solidarity in Cambodian society.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen congratulated the successful students and highly praised the leadership of the National University of Management for its efforts to develop and strengthen the quality of education.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after the day of liberation in 1979, Cambodia lacked human resources very much, but now Cambodia has trained many human resources.
* According to the study data of the National University of Management, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the current Cambodian society, parents no longer rely on state aid, but have paid for their children's education.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that the Minister of Education of Cambodia after the liberation in 1979 did not have higher education. This is a manifestation of the lack of human resources after the liberation era.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has warned all political parties involved in fugitives to file a lawsuit. This confirmation came after Samdech received a new statement and project to overthrow the Royal Government in 2023.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the success of Sam Rainsy in the defamation case was not paying a single euro, but this prisoner was exposed to hypocrisy and untruth.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen tells people in France to support three generations of traitors that on December 12, Samdech arrived in Brussels.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the history of Cambodia for about 500 years, no one is more corrupt than the three generations of traitors Sam Rainsy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that on October 20, Samdech will go to correct the identity card information in the voter list. Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on young people of voting age to register to vote.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the governors of Battambang and Pailin to expedite the demarcation process of the border between the two provinces.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen revealed that the inability to demarcate the border between the two provinces due to the large landowners in the area did not want to cut to Pailin and tried to cause obstruction.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he will definitely eliminate those who implement the plan of the three generations of traitors.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminds local Khmers not to get involved with three generations of traitors.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen tells stakeholders to speed up the impact assessment and provide rice seeds to farmers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen warns all agricultural officials not to ride students to see flowers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the philanthropists and the Cambodian Red Cross for bringing food aid to the flood victims.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends studying the statistics of flood victims and providing support for 3 months, which can cost more than 2 million dollars.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on all financial institutions to understand and favor the flood victims.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the opposition that the transfer of ministers is the right of the Prime Minister, without consulting the opposition.
