Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Graduation Ceremony for More Than 6,000 Students of the National University of Management
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, October 17, 2022, tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the graduation ceremony for 6,411 students of the National University of Management (NUM), 3,560 females. After they successfully graduate with overcoming many difficulties and obstacles.
Tomorrow's graduating class includes: undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral students. The report shows that the winning students are all employed and about 10 percent of the undergraduates are self-employed.
Please note that the National University of Management is an old state higher education institution and has been involved in education and training of human resources since 1983.
According to Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, a total of 56,326 students graduated from the National University of Management, 25,280 females, or 44.8 percent. These alumni have been working in public, private and international institutions with high professionalism, excellence, dignity and honor.
The minister also said that the university is currently training a total of 13,520 students, 8,479 of whom are female, or 62.7 percent in 23 majors, divided into three levels, including bachelor's, master's and doctoral degrees. .
At the same time, the University has adjusted the training program to fully meet national and international standards, as well as developed additional new curricula for bachelor's, master's and doctoral degrees to have dual programs with partner universities. Who studied in English.
In particular, the University has recently developed a training program and equipped with modern technology in the form of Digital Platform to serve the work of staff, research, teaching and learning of professors and students to respond. Socio-economic development in the context of Industry 4.0 and contribution to the fight against Kovid-19 with the Royal Government.
