Regarding his policy to lead the Bar Association, Mr. Ly Chantola recalled the following:
* 1: Restrict the application for professional experience according to Article 32 of the Law on the Statute of Lawyers and the entrance examination for the profession of lawyer under Article 31 of the Law on the Statute of Lawyers based on quality and ability.
* 2: Strengthen the capacity of lawyers by increasing training courses, seminars, quoting and exchanging experiences, study visits both inside and outside the country.
* 3: Strengthen cooperation, value and understanding with national and international institutions.
* 4: Increase the dissemination of the role of lawyers and the tasks that lawyers can provide clients.
* 5: Expand the scope of work that lawyers can provide to clients more and against illegal competition by individuals who do not have the right to be a lawyer.
* 6: Establish a mechanism to value and honor lawyers who have made outstanding contributions to the Bar Association, the legal profession, and social justice.
* 7: Continue to implement and expand the welfare mechanism of all lawyers, especially the mechanism related to the fund to help lawyers who are old and seriously ill.
* 8: Increase the interaction between the bar and the lawyer and provide better services to all lawyers.
According to Mr. Ly Chantola, in order to implement the policy of leading the Bar Association, the Bar Association has set out three missions:
* First: Expanding and strengthening participation in the justice sector
To carry out this mission, the Bar Association has identified five activities in order to contribute to the promotion of the right to justice by providing free, effective and timely legal assistance to the poor, especially women and minors.
* Second: Strengthening and promoting the professional value, ability and well-being of lawyers
* Third: Expanding and strengthening cooperation with national and international institutions
To carry out this mission, the Bar Association has identified three activities in order to broaden the legal profession and the role of lawyers in society, and to expand the scope of lawyers' work, as well as to exchange experiences and share legal knowledge in other fields. Lawyer.
