Senior Minister Kun Kim Distributes 100 Tons of Rice Seed to Farmers in Prasat Sambo District
(Kampong Thom): Follow the high order of Samdech Techo to help restore the lives of people affected by the flood this morning, October 16, 2022, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management. Delivered about 100 tons of non-seasonal light rice to 1,426 families from 5 communes: Chhouk commune, Koul commune, Sambo commune, Sreung commune, Tang Krasaing commune, Prasat Sambo district, Kampong Thom province.
This rice seed, a precious help from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprit Bun Rany Hun Sen, was immediately given to priority farmers with rehabilitated land among flood-affected families. Rain in the past.
Speaking at the ceremony, Senior Minister Kun Kim, Chief of Staff to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, brought greetings, attention, nostalgia and compassion to the people with deep affection and compassion from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittiprittbandit. Bun Rany Hun Sen to the flood victims.
The event was attended by representatives of senior officials from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, representatives of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to manage the food reserve system of Cambodia, as well as the authorities of Kampong Thom.
Mr. Ngin Chhay, Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, introduced the important cultivation techniques such as land preparation and proper use of rice seeds in order to be able to replant in time and yield. High.
The Senior Minister also praised the past activities of the provincial, district, commune and village authorities in helping people during the floods.
In addition, the Senior Minister also advised the commune chiefs who have gained the trust of the people during the last election to continue to serve the people regardless of the trend as long as they are affected by the floods and have real needs. He also stressed that this commune chief is the commune chief of the people, must serve the people in return for the trust that the people have provided.
Taking this opportunity, the Senior Minister also reminded and called on people from all walks of life not to get confused with Kovid-19 and to seek further vaccinations, because Kovid-19 has never forgotten us. Although the Royal Government has been successful in the fight against Kovid-19, the participation of all citizens is a key factor.
Chinese President Xi Jinping has vowed to oppose Taiwan's independence and will not give up the option of using force to reunite (Video inside) (Beijing) And will not give up the option of using absolute force to reunite with the archipelago. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, October 16, 2022.
The Chinese President made the remarks during his inaugural address to the 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China. During that time, on the subject of Taiwan, Xi Jinping said, "In the past, we have fought valiantly against separatist movements, as well as interference, which has demonstrated a strong commitment, including the ability to maintain sovereignty and integrity." "The territory of our country and against the independence of Taiwan."
"We will try to adhere to the position of seeking peaceful reconciliation under the most sincere efforts, but at the same time we will not commit to abandoning the use of force to do so and to keep the options," Xi said. "To take all necessary measures."
However, Xi stressed that the option of using force was primarily aimed at foreign interference, and that a small number of groups supported the Taiwan independence movement rather than the people of Taiwan as a whole, emphasizing that China has always respected Always care for and benefit the people of Taiwan.
Tensions between China and Taiwan escalated in August when Beijing held large-scale military exercises near the island after US House of Representatives Speaker Nancy Pelosi made a controversial visit. Come to Taipei, Taiwan, regardless of repeated Chinese warnings.
