On the morning of Saturday, October 15, 2022, Samdech Kittipritthbandit assigned Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, and her colleagues to distribute fruits and drinks to the forces after the search operation. Is closed.
In the search for the bodies of the victims of the sinking of the boat, many forces participated in the search operation and coordinated various activities. The forces involved in the operation and intervention include the 911 Special Forces of the CMAC, the police, the military police and the provincial military, a total of more than 300 people.
For about 2 nights a day, both the search and rescue operations force acted diligently and diligently, day and night, without complaining of fatigue. .
In front of all the forces, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak brought the words of thanks and praise of Samdech Kittipritthbandit to all the forces that have sacrificed their physical and mental strength in the operation to help the suffering of the people.
After chatting and bringing some remarks from the President of the Red Cross, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak also prepared to hand over fruits and drinks to all forces. Fruit and soft drinks were handed over to the force, including 50 cases of fruit (apple, grapefruit, grapefruit) and 50 cases of soft drinks.
Immediately after the distribution, all the forces came to eat the fruit with a big smile, showing their happiness, full of warmth, lost their tiredness because they received high attention from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany. Hun Sen.
After handing over fruits and drinks to the troops, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak and her colleagues continued the second mission of Samdech Kittiprittbandit to bring water, food and money to 6 students and people who survived the flood. The boat is at the back of the house on Koh Chamroeun.
Mrs. Men Neary Sopheak brought the generous gift of the Cambodian Red Cross, as instructed by Samdech Kittipritthbandit, to the six people in the backyard. She also brought the words of Samdech Kittipritthbandit to congratulate the grandchildren of 4 students and 2 other people.
According to Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, Samdech Kittipritthbandit considered the survivors of this tragedy to be highly fortunate. Samdech Kittipritthbandit also instructed all grandchildren to continue to take care of their health and study hard, especially to be careful when going to school by wearing a bag regularly when crossing the water so as not to continue such accidents.
In addition, when traveling by road, you must obey the traffic rules and travel carefully to avoid accidents on the road.
Donations donated by the Cambodian Red Cross to the six survivors include: 50 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish and 2 million riels. In addition, the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Kandal province donated an additional 1 million Riels per person.
It should be noted that Samdech Kittipritthbandit also shared the sad death with the families of 11 students who lost their lives in this tragic incident. With this condolence, Samdech Kittipritthbandit also received food and suffixes for the funeral of the 11 children, with each family receiving: 100 kg of rice, 5 boxes of noodles, 50 cans of fish, 5 orange juice Case and budget 5 million riels.
