(Preah Vihear): The Preah Vihear Provincial Administration and the National Authority of Preah Vihear on the morning of October 15, 2022, held a ceremony to pay homage to the late King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King Father, Father of National Independence, Territorial Integrity and National Unity. Khmer celebrates the 10th anniversary by counting the feet of 100 monks on the mountain of Preah Vihear temple.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Prak Sovann, Chairman of Preah Vihear Provincial Council, Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Mr. Kong Puthikar, Director General of Preah Vihear National Authority, with the participation of provincial leaders, government officials from departments around the three Armed Forces. Municipal and district authorities and many other citizens.
Mr. Kong Puthikar, Director General of the National Authority of Preah Vihear, said that today is a national event that the Royal Government sets October 15 every year to pay tribute to the late King Father Norodom Sihanouk. Reminiscent of his merits of leading the country from the independence claim in 1953 to the Kingdom of Cambodia 1-2.
Mr. Kong Puthikar said that the ceremony we are doing now is to show respect and gratitude. He said that the claim of the Temple of Preah Vihear in 1962 was the basis on which the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, could register the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site in 2008.
* Story and operation to search for the body of the victim
The tragic accident happened when 15 students, a boat driver, a boat worker and two villagers were traveling from a secondary school in Ampil Teuk village to Koh Chamroeun village. Their home was also in danger when a dilapidated wooden boat left the shore near the other shore.
As soon as this happened, the victims, who were students with some backpacks and slippers, swam to the shore, but unfortunately 11 of them could not escape death. Eight others drowned, including four schoolchildren, a boatman, a boat worker and two villagers who swam to shore and escaped death.
Immediately after receiving this information, the authorities and local authorities, including relevant officials, launched an operation to the scene to provide first aid, but on the night of the incident, the rescue force found six victims, but two died. Gone.
The search for the body took place day and night, with almost no rest from after the incident until the end of the mission at 6:10 am on October 15, after the body of a 14-year-old male student named Meas Sovannra was found. Found under the scorpion.
In an interview with Fresh News at the scene this morning, October 15, 2022, Senior Minister Kun Kim said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has been following this case closely, despite being busy. Big meetings, however. The prince instructed the joint operation team to do their best to rescue the dead if all the bodies were found.
After finding all the bodies, Samdech Techo also thanked the operation team, including the armed forces, government officials, authorities, as well as thanked the monks who worked together to rescue the victims and search. The bodies of the victims.
Senior Minister Kun Kim continued that after finding the last body, the team handed over the body to the family to prepare for the traditional ceremony, with the Senior Minister also attending the funeral. Senior Minister Kun Kim confirmed that at the end of the mission, the Kandal Provincial Police will continue to investigate the leak after conducting an autopsy on the 11 bodies to build a case file.
