Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum would like to express his deepest condolences to the families and relatives who lost their children, grandchildren and great-grandchildren in this tragic incident and pray for the souls of their children. Grandchildren and great-grandchildren go to death, not to be wasted.
At the same time, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum wished the victims' nieces and nephews, who are being treated at the hospital, a speedy recovery and return to normal studies.
On October 15, 2022, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, sent a message of condolences to the families and relatives of all the victims of the sinking of a student ferry in Kandal province.
In a message, Samdech Heng Samrin said, "My wife and I are very shocked and saddened by the incident of the sinking of a student boat from school to home in Kampong Phnom commune, Leuk Dek district, Kandal province on the night of October 13. 2022, which caused many deaths and some were hospitalized.
I would like to express my deepest condolences to the families of the bereaved children and all my relatives, and pray for the souls of all the lost grandchildren to go to hell. "I wish all the victims who are recovering from their injuries a speedy recovery so that they can return to their normal studies."
(Phnom Penh): The spokesman of the General Commission of the National Police, Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, called on the people to report to the Hotline 117 of the General Commission of the National Police in case the traffic police stopped their means of transportation for fines. For no reason across the country.
In the press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit on October 14, 2022, Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun emphasized that at all targets, in case any individual traffic police officer commits a mistake by stopping people's means of transportation to For no apparent reason, citizens can call Hotline 117 to take action.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun said, "We recognize that the individual police officer has a loophole in terms of moral discipline, and if there is a problem, we have a system of 117 up to date." "People just call and tell me that I am at this or that destination, giving the name of the officer and his number, he stopped the fine for no reason, we will work immediately."
In the past five years, 1,046 police officers have been fined for misconduct. Another 406 were fired for serious misconduct. This is according to Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police. General Department of Prisons continues to pay attention and put in place mechanisms to solve overcrowding in prisons (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Overcrowding in Cambodia's prisons remains an issue that the General Department of Prisons, Ministry of Interior, has been focusing on and taking forward measures to address.
Mr. Nuth Savana, Deputy Director General and Spokesperson of the General Department of Prisons, in the press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit on October 14, 2022, emphasized that the General Department of Prisons has set out a series of strategies in this phase. Short and long stages, while this issue is not something to be underestimated.
According to Nuth Savana, overcrowding in prisons is not unique to Cambodia. If we look at the prison situation in the region, the rate of prison overcrowding in Thailand is 339%, in the Philippines 362% and in Indonesia 209%.
A series of measures were taken to address overcrowding, Nuth Savana said, adding that the General Department of Prisons had expanded storage capacity by building additional commune buildings, renovating buildings, and transferring detainees from overcrowded prisons. High congestion to low-density prisons, strengthen cooperation with the judiciary to reduce case congestion.
In addition, the General Department of Prisons also strengthens the prisoner movement to increase pardons and commutation of prisoners to participate in the development of conditional release mechanisms.
The spokesman for the General Department of Prisons also noted that the campaign to reduce congestion, which was launched by Justice Minister Keut Rith in the past, also eased the congestion. More than 10,000 people have been released from pretrial detention.
