Senior Minister Osman Hassan pays a courtesy call on Singapore Minister for Social Development and Family
The meeting took place at the Peace Palace on the occasion of the Minister of Social Development and Family of Singapore attending the 28th ASEAN Socio-Cultural Community Council Meeting in Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Osman Hassan said that Cambodia, under the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister, has harmonized all religions in Cambodia, without religious conflicts, without discrimination, and especially the Islamic community. Has received a lot of attention and offers that have made progress in the field of education and socio-economic transformation of the general population.
The Senior Minister continued that the Royal Government has allowed community representatives to be leaders in the Senate, National Assembly, Royal Government, Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, senior diplomats, national and sub-national authorities, the Armed Forces of all kinds and civil servants. The Royal Government allows, in principle, full rights for all Cambodians, such as the right to life, education, the right to education, and the right to practice religion.
He added that the head of the Royal Government has allowed Muslim women to cover their heads for passports, ID cards or take photos for other administrative documents. Muslim students can wear traditional attire and wear a krama while studying at both public and private educational institutions. In addition, the Royal Government has included about 1,500 Khmer Muslim teachers in the framework of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and 180 contract officials.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan also called on Singapore to cooperate with Cambodia in providing free health care and medical services to Cambodians in general, both Muslims and non-Muslims, with the participation of Singaporean doctors. More new techniques and experiences. In addition, he asked Singapore to contribute to improving the lives of the poor in Cambodia through the provision of humanitarian assistance.
