The purpose of this workshop was to raise awareness of the National Social Protection Policy Framework and to disseminate the report on the implementation of the cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age, organized in collaboration with the General Secretariat of the Council. National Social Protection, Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and the United Nations Children's Fund (UNICEF) in Cambodia, with approximately 200 participants.
He said that through the above vision and commitment, the Royal Government has prepared and announced the implementation of the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025, which is an important national policy framework as a basic document and guide for the development of the protection system. Cambodian society today and in the future is based on a lifelong social protection approach and has two main pillars: the social assistance system and the social security system.
She said that a number of programs and regimes are being considered for implementation and continuous improvement, and that a number of new programs and regimes have been introduced to respond to the global health crisis of Kovid-19 and the development of regional and global socio-economic factors.
Please be informed that the cash subsidy program for pregnant women and children under 2 years old is the first national social assistance program that has a nationwide scope and uses the entire state budget. As of now, this program has been running for more than 3 years since it was first launched in June 2019.
Separately, the implementation of the cash support program for poor and vulnerable families during the 27-month Kovid-19 fight provided 691,709 poor, vulnerable households, equivalent to 2,731,273 At a cost of about 805.71 million US dollars.
