(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Expert Group on International History and International Relations has analyzed that the Russia-Ukraine war will not lead to the escalation of a nuclear war.
The analysis was made during a roundtable discussion organized by the Royal Academy of Cambodia under the theme "New World Order and the Dangers of Nuclear War" on the morning of October 14, 2022.
He added that the current fighting between the Russian army and the Ukrainian army has confirmed that Russia's military and armed forces are strong and that there are other strategies that Russia can use against Ukraine. Modern weapons of the West.
Dr. believes that nuclear war is long because nuclear weapons are very powerful, so countries around the world, as well as superpowers with nuclear weapons in their hands, are well aware of the devastating effects of using them in the fire of war. Through this, it is clear that the use of nuclear weapons in the Russia-Ukraine war is not possible.
In particular, Dr. Kamathul, Vice President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, similarly claimed that Dr. Diep Sophal's view that the use of nuclear weapons unless the United States and Russia evacuate their people to the moon. Only then could nuclear war erupt.
"The situation between Russia and Ukraine has been going on for more than eight months, but there is no sign that either side has won," said Dr. Kamathul. The war proved to be extremely difficult for Europe as well as the world.
"The war between Russia and Ukraine, I have a short answer in case the United States and Russia have not yet evacuated its people from this planet to live on the moon, nuclear war may not exist," he said.
The Russian-Ukrainian war has reached a new stage where Russia has fired missiles at Kiev and other major Ukrainian cities, causing many deaths and injuries and destroying infrastructure.
