Community Fair Creates Jobs for People in Protected Area Communities in Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): A delegation from the Ministry of Environment, led by Ms. Mom Thany, Secretary of State and Chair of the Community Exhibition Project Working Group, met with community members in Kampong Thom Protected Area who are learning how to repair motorcycles at Kampong Thom Polytechnic Institute on October 13, 2022.
On that occasion, Ms. Mom Thany said that skills are very important for young people as well as participate in the economic development of our family and country. This training encourages people in the community to learn a specific skill to have a real career choice, reduce dependence on natural resources and help the community to prosper.
She added that the Community Expo project is a strong support mechanism to help develop the capacity of people living in and near protected areas to prosper through the implementation of a clear plan is to train various skills that have the potential to respond. To market needs, the establishment of close ties between communities and development partners, as well as the establishment of consultative forums between communities and target traders.
The Secretary of State said that people in the communities of protected areas in Kampong Thom province have received training in various skills, including motorcycle repair skills of the community exhibition project, as part of providing important business options to help increase their family economy. He is on the ground.
In the meantime, Ms. Mom Thany handed over the budget of the Community Exhibition Project to the participants who are members of the community of Choam Thlok Nature Reserve, who have completed two motorcycle repair courses, each of which received a budget of 3.6 million riels. This budget is given to them to create a business to improve the livelihood of local families.
It should be noted that the Community Exhibition Project was launched in April 2020 with the aim of creating jobs, increasing income, reducing or completely eliminating the use of natural resources, and is a project of good cooperation between the Ministry of Environment and relevant ministries and institutions. Local authorities.
