Multiculturalism is the existence of many cultures coexisting in physics, geography, or society as a whole. It includes all the differences that exist in a culture, be it religion, language, race or gender.
Multiculturalism is a principle that recognizes the diversity of existing cultures in all spheres and promotes the right to diversity. According to sociology or anthropology, multiculturalism is the indication that certain cultures coexist within the same geography or social space, but it does not necessarily imply that there is influence or exchange between them. When communities manage to maintain change in respect and tolerance, experts call it multicultural.
Features of multiculturalism:
* Promote respect and tolerance for differences. * Prohibit discrimination, racism and related concepts. * Establish harmonious coexistence. * Create exchanges between different groups.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in order to achieve this goal, as the chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia has set the theme "ASEAN works together: solve all challenges together."
