Prey Veng Province Needs 500 Tons of Rice Seed, Senior Officials of the Ministry of Agriculture Inspect and Assess the Impact to Rehabilitate in Time
(Prey Veng): Mr. Has Sareth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, led a professional delegation to inspect the extent of damage to rice and other crops of the people in Prey Veng to take immediate action to restore in time.
In fact, on October 12, 2022, a delegation from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries held a meeting with the Prey Veng Provincial Administration to inspect and assess the flood damage and rehabilitation measures. This meeting was attended by Mr. Chea Somethy. Provincial governors as well as relevant departments, units, 13 municipal authorities.
On that occasion, Mr. Ouk Samnang, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, reported on the results of the municipal administration, according to the preliminary report, as of October 12, 2022, throughout Prey Veng province, the impact of rice on floods. 6,349 hectares, 4,511 hectares damaged and 1,243 hectares of mixed crops, and nearly 500 tons of rice seeds are needed for rehabilitation.
Mr. Has Sareth said that his team was set up to cooperate with the Prey Veng Provincial Administration in order to expedite the monitoring and assessment of the impact of flood damage on rice and mixed crops due to flooding in order to provide rice seeds and Combined crops to affected farmers.
Mr. Has Sareth added that the Ministry of Agriculture has cooperated with the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the National Committee for Disaster Management to provide rice seeds and mixed crops to affected farmers to rehabilitate in a timely manner by implementing existing mechanisms. Provided in Sub-Decree No. 124 dated July 30, 2021 on the Establishment of the Cambodian Food Reserve System, report regularly on the work activities implemented to the Ministry.
A senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture also instructed the district administration, the director of the district agriculture office to pay attention to inspect and provide results of damage to rice and mixed crops of farmers in their localities. Provincial and Ministry level in a timely manner and verify to collect the actual data in requesting seeds to him in a timely manner.
After the meeting, Has Sareth led the team to the flood-affected areas and met with the affected people.
