(Phnom Penh): Cambodia has set a target to attract 700,000 Vietnamese tourists by 2023 and 1 million by 2024, as the two sides agreed to further strengthen and expand cooperation in the field of tourism. Each achieves this goal.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon asked the Vietnamese Ambassador to help achieve the goal of attracting 700,000 Vietnamese tourists by 2023 and 1 million by 2024 during the first eight months of 2022. Cambodia has received more than 230,000 Vietnamese tourists.
"While the world has not yet recovered from the Kovid 19 pandemic, the global economic situation is uncertain, and promoting tourism with neighboring countries or the region is of the utmost importance," he said. Further cooperation in tourism to promote mutual tourism movement by land, air and water.
At the same time, the two sides also agreed to promote better waterway connectivity, especially from the tourist port in Koh Tral to the tourist port of Kampot, while the tourist port is ready to open during the second quarter of 2023. Face too.
As for air connectivity, both sides have pushed for connecting flight destinations between a number of tourist destinations, including Siem Reap-Koh Tral, Sihanoukville-Halong, Siem Reap-Haiphong, Siem Reap-Kanter, as these destinations are all major destinations. Significance of both countries. The two sides also agreed to promote self-driving tourism through both countries and to third countries.
The Minister requested the Vietnamese side to continue to provide scholarships for training and human resource development in the tourism sector to meet the demand for employment in the tourism sector. In the past, the Vietnamese side has provided scholarships and short courses to Cambodian students / trainees studying tourism professionals.
The two sides agreed to increase business exchanges and visits between the public and private sectors, especially the private sector, as the private sector is an important agency in bringing tourists. In addition, it will encourage the organization and participation of tourism events together to promote the promotion of tourist destinations between Cambodia and Vietnam.
