Eye Health Day, Ministry of Health calls on people to come for eye examination at least once every 2 years, if you are over 40 years old and have other diseases to come every year
On this occasion, the Ministry of Health calls on all citizens to visit your eye care facilities in Phnom Penh and other provinces in the Kingdom of Cambodia at least every two years. Once.
Especially for people over 40 years of age with a family history of glaucoma (high blood pressure or vision impairment), diabetes or high blood pressure, a history of chronic smoking, wearing glasses. Then your high power level (high cataracts) must go to the eye doctor every year.
The Minister said that the eye is an entity for seeing has an important function for everyone that can not be lacking. Through the eyes, we can get information and knowledge around us from 80% to 90%. Blindness adversely affects the lives and well-being of patients and their families.
Eye and vision protection is a top priority for everyone, whether they have eye problems or vision problems. This may not be easy or common, but investing in health care Making us see is one of the greatest gifts we can give ourselves.
In Cambodia, blindness and poor vision are a public health issue that requires all of us to take care to reduce as much as possible, as 90% of blind people And poor eyesight is avoidable and treatable.
Under the wise and wise leadership that made Cambodia peaceful and prosperous, by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the achievements of "Blind Prevention and Management" have been achieved. 2% in 1995 to 0.37% in 2019.
The Ministry of Health has developed the Third National Strategic Plan for the Prevention and Control of Blindness 2021-2030, with the ambitious goal of "reducing the prevalence of blindness to 0.35% by 2030."
This year's World Eye Health Day is celebrated on October 13, 2022 under the theme "Love Your Eyes" with the aim of:
* Focus the world's attention on eye health as a global issue * Raise awareness of eye health among all citizens, families and communities * It is important for decision makers to prioritize ideas Eye Health Initiative * Helps promote eye health services for all citizens and everywhere.
Here are some of the highlights we have achieved over the past 27 years:
Infrastructure Currently, the vision building is operational in Phnom Penh and the provinces: - In Phnom Penh, there are 4 hospitals providing ophthalmology services and senior ophthalmology departments at the national hospital. In the provinces, there are 22 provincial hospitals and 18 eye care centers.
* Goals for implementing eye health programs
On the occasion of the World Eye Health Day, October 13, 2022, all citizens are invited to check your eyes at the vision services in Phnom Penh and the provinces in the Kingdom of Cambodia. At least every two years.
People over the age of 40 with a family history of glaucoma (high blood pressure or vision problems), diabetes or high blood pressure, a history of chronic smoking, wearing glasses And your high eye power level (high cataracts) must go to the eye doctor every year.
