Cambodia-Vietnam Police Agree on Seven Points to Ensure Security and Order in Border Areas
The meeting proceeded according to the program and agenda planned by the two sides, exchanging content and experiences in the cooperation between the police forces of the two border provinces, contributing to further promoting all-round cooperation between Cambodia. Vietnam speaks in general and separately between the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia and the Ministry of Police of Vietnam, especially to ensure security and order in the border area between the two countries.
At the meeting, the two sides agreed on the following contents:
* First, continue to contribute to the promotion of traditional friendly relations, focusing on cooperation to strengthen security and order along the borders of the two countries.
* Second: Increase cooperation in exchanging information related to pollution in the situation of incitement, incitement to deceive people in the provinces bordering the two countries.
* Third: Increase patrols, monitoring, dissemination, raising the awareness of the people in the border areas to respect the independence, national sovereignty, laws, customs and traditions of each country, strictly abide by the border management statutes, contribute to building the border line, peace, friendship, cooperation and Development
* Fourth: Promote propaganda activities to inspire people in border areas to participate in the movement to prevent transnational crime in order to ensure security in villages, communes, districts of border provinces on both sides.
* Fifth, to promote and increase cooperation with the competent forces in the border areas of the two countries in the search and prevention of all kinds of criminal offenses, drug offenses, activities organized by brokers and criminals. Illegal people crossing the border, illegal gambling activities, human trafficking and forced labor, etc.
* Sixth, continue to strengthen the existing mechanisms and establish a timely communication system between the provincial police commissioners bordering the two countries to exchange or receive information to resolve incidents effectively and in a timely manner.
* Seventh: Continue to hold meetings on cooperation to strengthen security and order along the border between the Cambodian National Police Force and the Vietnamese People's Police Force in shifts and decisions of the leaders of both sides.
Finally, the heads of delegations of the two sides signed the minutes of the meeting on October 12, 2022 in Tay Ninh province, Socialist Republic of Vietnam in Khmer and Vietnamese. The meeting ended in a happy atmosphere in the spirit of unity, friendship and cooperation.
