(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Planning is very proud that poor family identification data is widely used by the Royal Government and development partners for social protection interventions for poor people or poor families.
* Since 2007, poor household data has been used by the Ministry of Health and other organizations to provide health services to poor households.
* In 2008, when Cambodia was hit by a catastrophic flood, poor families with equity cards were considered especially for social assistance interventions as food aid.
* Poor households data is used for food, labor programs and scholarships for poor primary school students
* 2019 Cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age from poor families to contribute to reducing poverty and improving the well-being of mothers and babies, as well as contributing to child malnutrition Pregnancy up to 2 years, and promotes growth both physically and mentally.
* 2020 Cash Support Program for Poor and Vulnerable Families During the Fight Against Kovid-19.
* And in 2022, the Royal Government is preparing a cash subsidy program for vulnerable families during further inflationary pressures.
The event also commemorates the 15th anniversary of the implementation of the Poor Household Identification Program, in which the construction of the Poor Household Database has become the cornerstone of Cambodia's social protection system and continues to be an important mechanism for the Royal Government and stakeholders. To continue to help poor and vulnerable families in Cambodia as well.
