Dr. Kao Thach made this encouragement when he and his colleagues inspected the rice procurement of farmers of Phu Kok Ki and Ung Khong rice mills in Bakan district and visited 25 farmers. Families affected by the floods destroyed rice and mixed crops in Pursat province's Kandeang district on October 12.
According to farmers in Pursat province, more than 400 hectares of their paddy fields are now completely destroyed by the floods, as they have to pay high production costs of nearly 4 million riels per hectare. At the same time, the price of fertilizers, oil and pesticides increased, but the yield of rice was not good.
In response to the farmers' remarks, Dr. Kao Thach mentioned the reasons for the rise in raw material prices, especially oil, due to the war between Ukraine and Russia and the spread of the 19-kovid disease. A while ago.
In order to reduce the high cost of rice cultivation, he suggested some points to farmers should examine the possibility to reduce the use of rice seeds to save and reduce the cost of seeds, examine the possibility of changing rice cultivation. There is a market and high prices and reduce the use of excessive fertilizers to help reduce production costs and save money.
In addition, the possibility of studying the use of solar energy instead of gasoline to pump water to feed the fields and can save money to buy fuel. Follow the information related to the weather forecast to avoid planting in bad weather. Most importantly, farmers should be able to keep track of expenses to keep track of their investment costs each year.
He encouraged farmers to contact the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank in case of need for additional credit to rehabilitate rice crops after the floods recede.
On that occasion, Dr. Kao Thach supported you with rice, fish sauce, soy sauce, noodles and some money to solve the challenges facing now.
