Samdech strongly believes that the statement on "Building a Sustainable, Environmentally and Stronger Future: Inspiring Women Entrepreneurship in ASEAN" which we discussed today will be supported and approved in The 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits will be held in November 2022.
Samdech Techo's speech was made at the closing ceremony of the 2nd ASEAN Women's Summit under the theme "Building a Sustainable, Environmental and Stronger Future: Inspiring Women Entrepreneurship in ASEAN".
On that occasion, Samdech Techo thanked the leaders of ASEAN and partner countries for their commitment and strong will to move forward together in inspiring women entrepreneurship in ASEAN in accordance with the President. Tracks put out.
Samdech continued that recognizing the need to strengthen entrepreneurship and economic empowerment of women is an important step and a necessary and indispensable factor.
Samdech expressed his pleasure and optimism, noting that ASEAN members have a common vision and a common position to continue to promote gender equality, empowerment and support for women as values. Great for the development of the ASEAN Community as a whole, especially in the context of a sustainable regional economic recovery, environment and resilience after the Kovid-19 crisis.
"The governments of all ASEAN countries have an obligation to ensure equality for women in access to education, vocational training, ownership of financial resources management, and the right to participate in decision-making," he said. "And leadership so that every woman has full opportunities in socio-economic, commercial and political aspects."
The economies of ASEAN countries are heavily dependent on women-led micro, small and medium enterprises. In fact, Cambodia has micro, small and medium enterprises up to 98% of the total number of enterprises that contribute to the national economy about 58% and provide about 73% of total employment.
In Cambodia, women account for about 61% of the total number of micro and small enterprises. This has led the Royal Government of Cambodia to identify and promote the empowerment of women as the backbone of national socio-economic development by increasing investment in gender equality and promoting the role of women in development in all areas and in all areas. Level.
