Russia arrests eight suspects in Crimea bombing
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russia's Federal Security Service (FSB) on Wednesday said it had arrested five Russians and a total of three Ukrainians and Armenians in connection with an explosion that damaged a Crimean bridge. Last Saturday last weekend. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, October 12, 2022.
The FSB claimed that the bombing was carried out by the intelligence department of Ukraine's Defense Ministry and its director, Kyrylo Budanov. Ukraine has not come forward to claim responsibility for the Crimean bridge incident, but some Ukrainian officials have hailed the damage.
Last Saturday's blast on the Crimean bridge destroyed a section of the bridge's roadblock, causing temporary talks to be suspended. It also destroyed a number of fuel tanks transported by rail from southern Russia to the Crimean peninsula.
