He stressed that the economies of ASEAN countries are highly dependent on small and medium-sized enterprises led by women. In fact, Cambodia has micro, small and medium enterprises up to 98% of the total number of enterprises that contribute to the national economy about 58% and provide about 73% of total employment.
"In Cambodia, women make up and account for about 61% of the total number of small and medium enterprises," he said. This has led the Royal Government of Cambodia to identify and promote the empowerment of women as the backbone of national socio-economic development by increasing investment in gender equality and promoting the role of women in development in all areas and in all areas. Level.
He said that within the framework of ASEAN, both now and in the future, women will continue to play an important role, especially in the restoration and promotion of ASEAN economic growth in a sustainable and environmentally friendly manner. This requires solidarity and cooperation to create an ecosystem that is conducive to the growth of women entrepreneurs and to work together to address challenges.
He added that women's entrepreneurship in ASEAN has been facing many obstacles in the development and management of enterprises, especially in rural areas. On the other hand, most women start micro-business and are offline, with the vast majority having not yet registered their business, which can make it difficult for the government to identify and provide support. Necessary.
In order to address the above challenges as well as inspire the potential of women entrepreneurs and make it easier to seize new opportunities and potentials, we should examine and pay attention to the following:
* First: Establish an ecosystem that responds to the needs of micro, small and medium enterprises and women entrepreneurs, as well as improve the legal framework and social mindset that hinders the potential of women in the economy.
* Fourth: Expand the coverage of the social protection system, policy measures to support family health and response to women's family care and domestic work, as well as public investment in care and social welfare services.
It should be noted that the 2nd ASEAN Women's Summit, which was attended by the top leaders of ASEAN and partner countries, is a testament to the strong commitment to unity and cooperation. The height of women's entrepreneurship.
