(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Sour, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, this morning, October 12, 2022, explained the procedures and procedures for resolving labor disputes of former workers and employees of NagaWorld Casino. It has been more than a year since Cambodia was hit by the Kovid 19 crisis.
Mr. Heng Sour claimed that the dispute between the workers and NagaWorld Company, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, has been resolved four times, which ended with both the Ministry and the court mechanism. This dispute is a dispute that occurred before April 2021.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training emphasized that there are four stages in resolving labor disputes, including:
* First: Reconciliation phase at the company * Second: In case of conciliation at the company level, do not continue to reconcile at the ministry level * Third: In case of disagreement at the ministry level, proceed to the Arbitration Council * Fourth: In case The Arbitration Council issues an order and both parties do not agree to proceed with the case.
Mr. Heng Sour said that the last dispute between the workers and NagaWorld after mediation in the Ministry to the Arbitration Council and the Arbitration Council issued an order, but the workers refused to accept the order. At the same time, the worker has set conditions for the employer to comply with the order, which he has already refused.
According to Heng Sour, in this case of joint labor dispute, the Ministry has received a request from the former NagaWorld staff representative for the Ministry to reconcile, but the process of resolving this joint labor dispute can not be reversed, that is, at the end of a phase. That has to go one step further, there is no going back. This case has to reach the court stage.
Heng Sour, a spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said: "We have now received a request from a former Naga staff representative to reconcile the Ministry, but the Ministry has reconciled at the company, at the Ministry and pushed "To the arbitrator, so it can not be pushed back to the ministry, that is, to go to court, unless there is a new object from the company to the ministry to the arbitrator again."
Regarding this dispute, Mr. Heng Sour emphasized that the Ministry has made efforts to mediate 19 meetings from all parties, since the end of March 2021. He saw that the problem was stuck at the point where the staff demanded to return to work, and the company did not accept, willing to pay the construction according to the law in force.
He added that Ministry of Labor officials are mediators, not judges who have the right to decide, so the ministry can only explain the legal aspects to both parties for mutual understanding and the ministry has no right to coerce. Let either party accept what is their idea. In particular, in the judiciary, it is a trial, so at least a decision has power in practice.
However, he called on all parties to provide a high level of understanding and to take the law as the basis, because unions do not belong to any one person and employers can not dismiss the wrong workers. But he sees that in the past, the company has followed the procedures of layoffs. Minister of Labor instructs factory monitors to suspend employment contracts to avoid factory closure
