This Afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Opening Ceremony of the 2nd ASEAN Women's Summit
(Phnom Penh): As the chair of ASEAN, on Wednesday afternoon, October 12, 2022, Cambodia will host the 2nd ASEAN Women's Summit, which will be chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chair of ASEAN.
During the Second ASEAN Women's Summit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will deliver a keynote address at the opening and closing of the meeting. In addition, there are interventions from special speakers.
The meeting will look at current barriers and trends, as well as opportunities that may affect women's access to entrepreneurship and entrepreneurial ecosystems in the context of the Kovid 19 epidemic, as well as changes in the work environment and revolution. Digital in ASEAN.
The meeting will also identify opportunities that will drive the recovery, growth and resilience of small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), create an equitable business environment for women to compete, grow and lead and inspire innovative entrepreneurial potential; Women's creativity in ASEAN.
The ASEAN Women's Summit is expected to reaffirm ASEAN's commitment to supporting and promoting women's entrepreneurship to the regional agenda, recognizing the important role, potential and strengths of leaders. All women and girls in ASEAN to pave the way for the rehabilitation and future planning of ASEAN in the post-Kovid 19 crisis.
The meeting is also expected to establish practical partnerships and cooperation between ASEAN governments, the private sector and key stakeholders in promoting the women's entrepreneurship agenda in the region.
