Officials: The Royal Government has introduced compulsory insurance to improve people's livelihoods and reduce the financial burden caused by accidents.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Bou Chanphirou, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, reaffirmed that in order to improve the living standards of the people and reduce the financial burden caused by unforeseen accidents, the Royal Government of Cambodia has introduced insurance as Obligations since 2002.
In addition, Mr. Bou Chanphiro said that under the existing laws and regulations, there are three types of compulsory insurance: third party liability insurance, compulsory insurance of passenger means and compulsory insurance for construction sites. Build.
The Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia emphasized that these three types of compulsory insurance are currently effective in Cambodia and require strong cooperation from relevant ministries and institutions, active support from the private sector and understanding. Positive from the public.
Mr. Bou Chanpirou added that among these collaborations, education and public awareness are very important in contributing to the development of compulsory insurance services in Cambodia.
He said that the Cambodian Insurance Regulator has been actively promoting a number of priority activities, including organizing seminars throughout the capital, provinces, targeting insurance sharing programs, video production for broadcast on television, social media and Website as well as organizing programs with universities in the past.
Mr. Bou Chanphiru said that in addition to contributing to the development of the insurance market, especially human resources, the Cambodian insurance regulator is committed to promoting the training of insurance professionals.
In this regard, the Cambodian Insurance Regulator has issued guidelines on vocational training for insurance agents in order to establish a common curriculum to be applied to all insurance companies that carry out vocational training for insurance agents in Cambodia. . This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Bou Chanpirou.
By the end of 2021, the Cambodian Insurance Regulator has approved 20 training courses offered by 4 general insurance companies, 11 life insurance companies and 5 micro-insurance companies.
Mr. Bou Chanphiro made the remarks while attending the "Future of Insurance in Cambodia" program organized by the American Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia at the Rosewood Hotel, Phnom Penh on October 6, 2022.
