Mao Thora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, praised the establishment of the Cambodian Cashew Federation as one of the priority activities set out in the draft national policy on cashews.
He said that the birth of the Cambodian Cashew Federation will be an important driving force in promoting the Cambodian cashew sector in the international market.
Mr. Mao Thora said, "The Cashew Federation will be an important driving force in promoting the implementation of policies more effectively and responding to the needs of the local and global market and contribute to the promotion of the Cambodian cashew sector in the international market. More.
Mr. Reach Ra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, also made seven recommendations to the newly formed Cashew Federation, including:
1. Remember that the Cashew Federation is not for the benefit of individuals or groups, but for the common good of growers, processors and exporters.
2: Must maintain a strong internal unity.
3. To manage financial resources in a transparent and accountable manner.
4. Implement consistently the vision, goals, objectives and action plans as stated in the statute and necessary work, as well as other practical requirements.
5. To cooperate well with the Ministry of Commerce and coordinate cooperation with other relevant ministries and institutions as well.
6. Liaise with national and international organizations to seek technical assistance, human resource training and project implementation with the Ministry of Commerce and relevant ministries.
