The postal development policy 2022-2030 aims to develop the postal sector and the postal service market to serve businesses, enterprises and people effectively, sustainably and innovatively to contribute to the socio-economic development of the country.
In order to achieve the above vision and objectives, this policy has set four goals as follows:
1. Improve postal sector management to ensure the improvement of service quality and protect the interests of consumers through the development of policy, legal and regulatory frameworks.
2. Modernize postal services, develop infrastructure, expand the postal network to reach a wider population, and use digital technology to support the delivery of postal services more efficiently and to meet the needs of consumers and to support commercial services. Digital Government Electronics and Public Services.
3. Facilitate the private sector to do business in the postal sector, transport and distribution of postal services by promoting fair competition within a clear legal framework and participation in the development of the postal industry in the form of investment by local and foreign investors; Public-private partnership.
4. Promote the role of Cambodia Post in providing postal services by promoting the diversification of innovative postal services and products and the use of digital technology.
