(Tbong Khmum): After a series of rains at the end of the rainy season, flooded hundreds of hectares of people's crops, especially rice, many roads were damaged, making it very difficult to travel. On this issue, Dr. Cheam Chansophorn, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, on October 11, 2022, led the relevant professional officers to directly inspect along one road in Kong Chey commune, Ou Raing Ov district.
After the direct inspection, Dr. Cheam Chansophoan said that as a first step, the provincial administration will take measures to fill the damaged areas to facilitate the travel of people temporarily. Further steps and for specialized departments such as the Department of Public Works and Transport, the Department of Rural Development to study in detail to submit a proposal to the Ministry of Rehabilitation.
As of October 11, there are no detailed reports on how many roads in Tbong Khmum province have been damaged because the rain continues to fall almost every day and the Mekong River is still not flowing, he said. Still fading. However, the roads that were damaged by the provincial administration will be temporarily filled with stones so as not to obstruct the daily commute of the people.
According to Ky Danarith, director of the Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, many roads in Tbong Khmum province were damaged after a series of rains at the end of the rainy season. He said that the first step is only to temporarily pour stones to facilitate people's travel, can not be repaired immediately, because now the rain continues to rain almost every day.
He said that when it rains, the ministry will study in detail to repair, but most of the damaged roads are projects of the Department of Rural Development.
