Organizes 2022 Volunteer Meeting and Evaluation Meeting
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) in Cambodia has organized its 2022 Volunteer Meeting, which will last for three days from October 5 to 7, 2022 at the Annie Hotel. Phnom Penh. This is the first volunteer meeting after sending volunteers back in December 2021.
The purpose of this meeting is to provide a number of training sessions, such as project management, Khmer language capacity building, and evaluation of the work activities of the volunteers who have been working in each partner institution.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has made great efforts to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and has achieved remarkable results. The KOICA office in Cambodia trusts the Royal Government of Cambodia to control the spread of the virus well, which is why KOICA has decided to send Korean volunteers back to Cambodia. Since December 2021.
As a result, there are currently 34 KOICA volunteers doing their volunteer work in a number of provinces and capitals, including Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Siem Reap, Pursat, Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Kandal, Takeo, Prey Veng, Kampot and Phnom Penh. Youth development, computer education, nursing, early childhood education and music education.
KOICA Cambodia Office sends professional Korean volunteers to Cambodia to share experiences, knowledge and skills to improve the lives and livelihoods of the people and to strengthen ties between the two countries. Both since 2003. As of October 2022, KOICA has sent 802 volunteers to Cambodia.
So far, the volunteers have worked with at least 25 ministries and sub-national institutions in Cambodia on various specialties. 300 families
