Samdech Techo stated that although the Royal Government has suspended the organization of the Royal Water Festival in Phnom Penh, the Royal Government has allowed the organization of the Water Festival in the provinces where some provinces have already organized and Some are also preparing.
Samdech Techo stated that the ASEAN Summit and related meetings are very busy, with many heads of state and international leaders attending, thus leading to some road closures to facilitate traffic for international visitors. At the same time, Samdech Techo would like to ask for the understanding and forgiveness of the people for the roadblocks and traffic jams.
Samdech Techo stated that when organizing the ASEAN Summit, the Royal Government has designated Sokha Hotel Phnom Penh, which has about 700 rooms as the venue for the meeting, and Samdech and the Cambodian delegation will stay in the hotel directly to facilitate the meeting.
On this occasion, Samdech Techo Prime Minister ordered to maintain security for the leaders who attended the ASEAN meeting and related meetings as high as possible by water, land and air.
