Khmer United National Party and Kampuchea Niyum Party issued a joint statement committed to strictly implement the unity agreement based on five principles
(Phnom Penh): The Khmer United National Party and the Kampuchea Niyum Party on October 10, 2022 issued a joint statement committed to strictly implement the unity agreement based on four principles.
1. Respect the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
2: Implement the spirit of the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991 in order to unite the nation, national reconciliation, continue to move forward in the cause of national democracy, freedom, rule of law and build a new future for Cambodia.
3. Loyal to society, motherland and people and protect the territorial integrity, sovereignty and independence.
4. Honesty, trust and respect for each other with brotherhood and dignity, avoid incitement, slander, insults and divisions by any means.
5. Adhere to the principles of internal democracy in order to achieve common goals and visions for the society to participate in non-violent political competition through free and fair elections.
Both parties have called for democratic political parties, democratic politicians, students, intellectuals, youth and women to unite as the new liberal democratic political force.
The Khmer United National Party and the Kampuchea Niyum Party have stated that they adhere to the constructive, honest and constructive democratic dialogue in order to build a party with strong internal democracy for the Khmer people, patriots, liberal democrats towards building democracy. Freedom, the rule of law and a truly dignified and prosperous society in Cambodia.
