Extraordinary Chambers in the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia -'s Martin Zakaing,'s Civil Party Attorney, Donates 1,400 Documents to the Documentation Center of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Martin Zakaing, Lawyer for the Civil Parties of the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia, announces the donation of 1,400 documents to the Documentation Center of Cambodia. This is according to the Documentation Center of Cambodia told Fresh News on October 10, 2022.
DC-Cam is pleased to announce the generous donation of 1,400 Civil Party documents to the DC-Cam archives. The third group of Civil Party lawyers, Martin Zakaing, generously donated the documents to the Documentation Center of Cambodia.
DC-Cam strongly expects to work with individual Civil Parties, victims, family members of survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime, as well as other stakeholders to facilitate the analysis of public distribution of specific documents. And the wider use of education and research on historical documents that embody this rich information is of immense value.
Justice should not or will not end when the court issues its final verdict. The facilitation of the analysis and dissemination of specific information, as well as the additional use for educational purposes, and the distribution of all these documents confirm the next steps to enable Cambodia to achieve real justice for its victims. Of the Khmer Rouge regime.
With the generous donation of Ms. Martin Zakaing, the Documentation Center of Cambodia looks forward to fulfilling the aspirations of individual Civil Parties, victims, as well as surviving family members of the Khmer Rouge regime to ensure the lives of individuals These will continue to contribute to the education of the next generation as well as to the achievement of justice in Cambodia and serve as a legacy of international law for post-conflict society.
