(Kiev): Russian President Vladimir Putin has warned of further retaliation if attacks on Russia continue. His warning came just hours after Russian forces fired dozens of missiles at cities across Ukraine. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday, October 10, 2022.
The Russian president made the warning at the opening of a National Security Council meeting on Monday. Putin said Russia launched long-range missile strikes against Ukraine's energy, military and communications infrastructure today in retaliation for attacks on a strategic bridge connecting Russia and the Crimean peninsula over the weekend. Ago.
"If the attacks continue against Russia, the serious response will continue," Putin said. The magnitude of our response will be the same as the magnitude of the threat to Russia. "If there is another attempt on terrorism on our territory, Russia's response will be even worse."
In a statement on Sunday, Putin accused Ukraine of being behind the bombing of the Crimean bridge and called it an act of terrorism. The bridge served as one of the most important means of supply for Russian forces in southern Ukraine.
