(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) on October 10, 2022 issued a press release on the meeting to disseminate security work and registration of political party agents for the examination of the list and Voter Registration 2022.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Dim Sovannarom, a member of the NEC and chaired the meeting to promote security work for voter registration and voter registration. Voting names and registration of political party agents.
Mr. Dim Sovannarom also mentioned the issues to be protected as a priority, the establishment of sub-national structure mechanisms and measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 at polling stations.
Based on the calendar of the 2022 voter list and voter registration, the registration date for political party agents starts from October 13, 2022 to February 11, 2023.
Mr. Dim Sovannarom continued that as of October 9, 2022, 5 political parties have transferred the right to their representatives to sign the application for registration of political party agents (Form 1007) for registration. Names and registration for the 2022 election include: the Cambodian People's Party, the Khmer United National Party, the Cambodian Youth Party, the Khmer Economic Development Party and the Candlelight Party.
Responding to questions from stakeholders attending the meeting on security at polling stations, the NEC stated that security related to election work was divided into two: security for the election and security during the election. Check the voter list and voter registration.
For the examination of the voter list and voter registration, the NEC cooperated with the Ministry of Interior to use the existing police force in the communes. When moving the polling station to the village, the police must also go to protect the voter registration process.
Regarding the number of political party agents, the NEC informed that political parties can nominate any number of party agents, but when working, there are only two political party agents, one full in the office. One voter name and one reserve person are outside the voter registration office.
