The statement of the Minister of Culture and Fine Arts was made during the opening ceremony of the 2022 National Bassac Theater Festival under the theme "Culture of Peace".
This program aims to preserve and promote the art of bassac, a priceless national cultural heritage, with the presence of many bassac artists from capitals and provinces who have applied to participate in the competition. Its ability to direct the story, the art, the way of writing and the ability to perform.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona also said that both the Bassac Theater and other Cambodian cultural arts, if the Cambodians do not try to preserve, no foreigner to help maintain.
"Even if you do not win a modern concert, you have to make an effort to make our traditional art good, exciting and wonderful, especially to attract the older generation as well as the younger generation," she said. Bassac has a Khmer identity in Khmer blood and a Khmer soul.
Dr. Phoeung Sakona said that the development of bassac has slowed down and this is due to a lack of support. She called for the support of the bassac from the masses, especially from the youth, so that the bassac can be revived as in the past.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona also reminded that for Cambodia in the past, the Bassac theater was very prosperous and people put mats and blankets to visit. Each bassac performance takes several nights and the public is constantly watching. She added that after 1979, Bassac also had a lot of acting activities, but now it is declining due to lack of human resource support and other issues.
He added that of the more than 60 groups, some have only the captain, while some have no performance. In addition, due to the mixed Kovid 19 disease factor is also the reason for the decline of bassac.
Bassac was originally called Treung Khlok and originated in Kampuchea Krom in Basak district, Preah Trapeang province. During the 1930s, the Trung Khlok drama was performed by two brothers in Phnom Penh and some provinces along the Bassac River and became very popular, initially called the theater from Bassac district and later abbreviated. Shortly called Bassac Theater and is still famous today.
Chheang Chhada Pheak, Acting Director of the Department of Performing Arts, added, "This festival is a platform for learning and exchanging knowledge and skills. Even we know a lot about the difficulties of each artist, meaning we know what each group needs and what they lack. "Through this festival, we find some points that we need to help strengthen the bassac."
"Kbach Huon, the method of directing and writing this article, it is important that we know that we are a professional unit to help them move forward," he said. We are looking for more ways, we also see that the bassac is declining because some groups have limited performance on the story, writing, directing and Huan walked in awkwardly.
According to Mr. Chheang Chhadapheak, only 10 bassac groups have applied for the 2022 National Bassac Theater Festival, as the jury found that all the groups still had some shortcomings. Complement such as writing, directing (short, concentrated, not long), martial arts and costumes.
The winner of the 2022 National Bassac Theater Festival, the Bassac Drama Group "Raksmey Culture of Kep Province" has expressed a desire to see big sponsorships for all bassac troupes, such as sponsoring contemporary concerts.
Nhet Tim, who led the team to the 2022 National Bassac Theater Festival, told Fresh News that if there were any sponsors from big companies to have a bassac performance and sponsor a championship competition. Bassac theater will help this ancient art field to grow like in the past. He added that public support through participation in the Bassac Theater is also an important part.
"If the sponsorship of the Bassac Theater is the same as the sponsorship of the Bassac Concert, there will be a resurgence," he said. "When we do not have the support and interest of philanthropists, we lose the resources (successors) who want to preserve this ancient art."
Mr. Nhet Tim added that when there is a lack of support, there is not only a lack of human resources, but also a lack of costs to form a theater group. In fact, today, the bassac theater needs modernization, such as lighting techniques, speakers and other stage equipment, all of which require cost.
