(Kampong Thom): A total of 370 families affected by the flood in Taing Kork district, Kampong Thom province received donations from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to solve difficulties and shortages in times of trouble. Floods this rainy season.
These donations were handed over to the people through Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Kampong Thom Province on October 10, 2022, including people from Kork Trabek village, Tuol Ta Mom area. And Boeung Kreah area of Sralao commune, Taing Kork district, a total of 370 families received 25 kg of rice, 1 can of fish, 1 can of soy sauce and 1 can of fish sauce.
On the other hand, the President advised the village / commune authorities to pay more attention to the issue of clean water and to repair the damaged pump well in order to have water for people to use and drink, because during this flood season, be careful of flooding. Health, medicine and clean water are important needs of the people.
The head of the Royal Government Working Group instructed to prepare rice seeds when the water recedes, farmers in Kork Trabek, Tuol Ta Mom and Boeung Koh Reas villages will be able to cultivate rice on their land while the work is being prepared. For farmers from the lower level to the upper level already.
At the same time, Mr. Thong Khon also urged the people not to cut down the flooded forest, not to catch fish or commit fishing crimes to participate in the protection of the flooded forest, increase fish species in the Tonle Sap Lake, maintain the stability of natural resources. He also advised people not to gamble or commit crimes to avoid the dangers caused by those illegal acts.
(Phnom Penh): On Monday afternoon, October 10, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the General Assembly of the Cambodian National Scouts.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech for more than half an hour, the following are the main contents of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen have been unanimously approved by the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian National Scouts to be teachers of the Cambodian National Scouts. Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked for this decision.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his appreciation and appreciation to Dr. Hang Chuon Naron and the leaders of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Cambodian National Scouts for their efforts to promote the Cambodian National Scout Movement to grow like other countries. By building a force to take turns with potential and loyalty to the Royal Government in the development of the motherland.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen dedicated the achievements of the Cambodian National Scouts to Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An and the scouts who have worked hard and dedicated their physical and mental strength to develop the Cambodian National Scout Movement in the past.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled that on July 8, 1999, he met with Mr. Kim Koo-yong, former Director of the Office of the World Scout Movement in the Asia-Pacific Region, to organize the Cambodian National Scout Movement.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that since then, Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An has made significant contributions to the organization of the first General Assembly from 26 to 27 April 2006 and has led this movement. Recognized as a full member of the World Scout Movement on July 1, 2008.
* Speaking at this point, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded of the hardships caused by the war, not only brought about the destruction of the nation, even the Cambodian National Scout Movement, the Cambodian Red Cross and other movements were divided. They will compete for the acceptance of international institutions.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech is proud of the progress of the Cambodian National Scout Movement throughout the country with the building of more than 170,000 Scout members in children and youth in schools and communities of all walks of life. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Cambodian National Scout is an active youth organization with a clear policy and program to change the attitudes of young Cambodians and become good citizens and role models with mutual understanding and tolerance. From individuals, families and communities.
