The Ambassador also expressed his congratulations to Samdech Techo for leading Cambodia to rapid development, and Germany was pleased to join and help Cambodia on its journey to success.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, the Ambassador expressed his commitment in front of Samdech Techo Prime Minister that in the diplomatic mission in Cambodia, he will do his best to promote relations and cooperation, especially to promote Invest more in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed and congratulated Stephen on his appointment as Ambassador to Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked the German government and people for helping Cambodia. Samdech Techo said that all of Cambodia's successes and developments were inseparable from German aid. More recently, German aid has helped prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
In order to strengthen the relationship and cooperation between Cambodia and Germany, the new German Ambassador has invited leaders of the country's top institutions as well as ministries. The Ambassador expressed his high commitment to contribute to improving relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Germany.
Germany is a country that has contributed a lot to the development of Cambodia after recovering from the flames of war. For the past 28 years, Germany has supported Cambodia's socio-economic development in the areas of demining, education, culture, good governance, rural development, energy, social protection and decentralization, contributing significantly to poverty reduction in Cambodia.
As for the economic sector, the two countries continue to enjoy strong and growing trade relations, while Germany is Cambodia's largest export market among EU member states, with bilateral trade volume exceeding 1 billion US dollars in In recent years.
According to a report by the Council for the Development of Cambodia, by 2021, Germany has provided about $ 670 million in grants, equivalent to about 2.6 percent of the total aid provided by development partners to Cambodia.
