Mr. Chea Chanto: No matter how far away the area is, as long as there is peace, the place will be developed like other areas
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chea Chanto, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Kampong Thom Province, said that no matter how far away the area is, as long as there is peace, the place is acceptable. Develop like any other area.
Mr. Chea Chanto's remarks were made on the occasion that he and his wife, Ms. Khieu Sina, and Samdech Preah Puth Chey Mony, Dr. Khim Sorn, President of the Secretariat of the Board of Priests of Cambodia and the Chief of Phnom Penh, were invited and invited. Presiding over the funeral of Khan Seima Chhlang Preah Vihear and the wedding of Wat Tipkaram, also known as Wat Pov Veay, located in Pov Veay village, Peam Bang commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province.
Mr. Chea Chanto called on all monks and people living in Pov Veay commune to unite in maintaining peace in order to protect the achievements of the ancient heritage and the achievements that have been worked hard to build for the benefit of future generations. Later came to know and live in peace in peace, because there is nothing more precious than peace.
He added that if we maintain good and stable peace, we will be able to continue to build and develop more new achievements, including in the field of Buddhism. Apparently, like the new Preah Vihear pagoda, the huge Pov Wei pagoda appears floating on the surface of the Tonle Sap Lake, this is a testament.
He continued that we did not expect that this remote area has developed as it is today, these are not due to the merits of peace and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the participation of the great unity of the people. .
Please note that this new temple, Wat Pov Veay, is a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen through Mr. Chea Chanto and Mrs. Khieu Sina.
On that occasion, Samdech Preah Puth Chey Mony, Dr. Khim donated a generator according to the dedication of the Chief Bishop of Wat Pov Veay, and Mr. Chea Chanto and Mrs. donated 50 million Riels to build achievements in the pagoda and distributed generous gifts. There were 55 people, grandparents, 830 people and 250 students, as well as the staff who worked in the program.
