Nearly 10,000 Sanskrit grammar books distributed to Buddhist students for further study
(Phnom Penh): Nearly 10,000 Sanskrit grammar books translated by Bhikkhu Udomviriyo Mohasum Sothea, Pali-Sanskrit Professor of Buddhism at Sihanoukville University and sponsored by Samdech Preah Puth Chey Mony, Dr. Khim Sorn and Buddhist supporter Ieng Sotheara also distributed to 2,638 students to study and understand more for their own knowledge and for teaching to the next generation.
On that occasion, Samdech Preah Udom Panha Duong Phang confirmed that the light of the Dharma could be as bright as it is today, because the head of the Royal Government liberated and expelled the wicked on January 7, 1979. Following the path of Buddhism and having all the monks and Buddhists keep and take back Buddhism, then we all continue to listen to the Dharma, which is the light for all Buddhists.
Samdech Preah Udom Panha Duong Phang continued that without the head of the Royal Government providing peace, rights, freedom and obedience to Buddhism, perhaps the people would not have the law and could enter into Buddhism.
Buddhist supporter Ieng Sotheara also said that Sanskrit is a part of the Khmer language, so every Khmer child can not get rid of this language, must learn and participate in promoting this Sanskrit language. To ensure the sustainability of the Khmer language and to help make the Khmer language more prosperous for future generations.
Mr. Ieng Sotheara added that this Sanskrit grammar book is a very important reference document for Khmer language scholars who can help the society, help Buddhism, especially in researching a large number of inscriptions, most of which are Also write in Sanskrit, so as a child, Khmer children must learn Sanskrit and continue to help them grow.
In order for Sanskrit grammar books to penetrate more and more young people, Mr. Ieng Sotheara added that in addition to the sermons, the books will be distributed now and will be distributed to various educational institutions. In order to make a study base for the students, there will also be a non-profit publication.
At the same time, the great Buddhist supporter Ieng Sotheara also called on all learners, especially young people, should be interested in learning more Pali and Sanskrit to benefit themselves and society both now and in the future.
Senior Minister Kun Kim Tells Victims of Samdech Techo's Order to Restore Agricultural Procurement After Low Tide
(Banteay Meanchey): The staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Operator on the Battlefield of Disaster, Senior Minister Kun Kim, on Sunday afternoon, October 9, continued to fly to Banteay Meanchey province to manage the work of rehabilitating farmers. Re-ordered by Samdech Techo.
Natural disasters are unfortunate events that have occurred worldwide that no country has been able to control. For Cambodia, although it is not possible to control or avoid all those disasters, the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, especially through the National Committee for Disaster Management, with Senior Minister Kun Kim as the direct operator, never sat and watched. The suffering of the affected people.
During the distribution ceremony for the flood victims, Senior Minister Kun Kim conveyed the greetings of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all the victims. The Senior Minister also expressed his condolences to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for the impact caused by the floods.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister also informed the people about the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen regarding the rehabilitation of procurement for planting after the low tide. Samdech Techo issued an order to release rice seeds and crops and intervene to help people immediately on this cultivation. In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Acting Minister of Agriculture, has already assigned a working group to work on this.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also called on the people to be ready with all relevant authorities to replant.
In addition to bringing donations to the affected people, the Senior Minister also inspected the flooded rice fields of farmers. After meeting with the provincial authorities to put out a plan to restore the people's cultivation.
During the meeting, Senior Minister Kun Kim mentioned Samdech Techo's strict order to intervene to restore the people's cultivation after the water receded.
The senior minister instructed the Department of Agriculture and the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology to work together to thoroughly study each geography that needs to be rehabilitated as the weather continues to face and prolong flood damage.
The senior minister stressed that no matter what the circumstances, it is necessary to study the rehabilitation and supply of rice seeds to farmers who are severely affected after the floods recede.
