(Phnom Penh): On Monday afternoon, October 10, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the closing ceremony of the Cambodian National Scout Conference.
On Sunday, October 9, 2022, the leaders of the Council and the Executive Committee of the National Scout of Cambodia at the National, Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan all over the country gathered at the opening of the 4th General Assembly 2022-2026 to review the work in The old mandate and set out an action plan for the new mandate. In particular, make the Cambodian National Scouts more active in the interests of society.
In the General Assembly held on Sunday and one Monday morning, the leaders of the Council and the Executive Committee of the National Scouts of Cambodia at the national, provincial, municipal, district and khan levels throughout the country unanimously decided on a large number of works for implementation in New mandate.
It should be noted that the National Scout of Cambodia was first established as the Cambodian Scouts of Cambodia was established in 1934 under the leadership of Prince Sisowath Monireth with other leaders. The first generation of Cambodian Cambodian Scouts expanded and spread to 7-8 provinces and more than 1,000 members.
The Cambodian National Scouts were completely lost under Pol Pot's Democratic Kampuchea regime. Under the initiative and encouragement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Cambodian National Scouts were re-established in 2000 and restructured from the national to the grassroots level.
The Cambodian National Scouts were recognized as a full member of the World Scout Movement on July 1, 2008 and were solemnly announced at the 38th General Assembly on July 14-18, 2008. South Korea.
The Cambodian National Scout Movement is a movement for children and youth and non-formal education that supports the education system of the Royal Government of Cambodia. The Cambodian National Scout is also a voluntary educational movement for children, youth, non-political and open to all, regardless of gender, origin, nationality or creed, and in accordance with the objectives, principles and methods of scouting.
