Khmer Civilization Expert: What is the history of Khmer rice wine?
What is the history of Khmer rice wine?
Khmer civilization expert Rath Sandab said that today there are many types of wine, such as rice or wine, palm wine, beer, grape wine or red wine, whiskey and other wines. In terms of "rice wine or wine" of our Khmer is a history from ancient times.
Mr. Rath Sandab continued that the history of this wine or rice wine, we see the appearance since ancient times. Because of the low embossed carvings on the Bayon temple during the reign of King Jayavarman VII in the 12th century AD, it depicts the life of the rich Khmer people and the drinking of wine from pottery and urns. As Chiv Ta Kwan described, Cambodians made wine.
