Please see the details of Ms. Men Neary Sopheak's interview as follows: Ministry encourages high school students to choose tourism education
(Sihanoukville): Due to the high demand of the labor market in both ASEAN countries and the ASEAN region, the Ministry of Tourism has encouraged high school students to study tourism vocational skills such as front office, food and beverage services, housekeeping, and tour guides. Decent income.
In each seminar, the Undersecretary of State informed that the injection of Kovid-19 vaccine to people all over the country has made the tourism sector in 2022 to recover rapidly. In fact, in the first eight months of 2022, Cambodia received nearly 1 million international tourists, an increase of 720% compared to the same period in 2022 and more than 8.6 million domestic tourists, an increase of 255.7% compared to the same period last year The same time in 2021.
In line with the increase in the number of tourists and the need for human resources in the tourism sector, the Undersecretary of State encouraged the students of the above four high schools, as well as students elsewhere to turn to choose a career in tourism according to the discipline. Such as front office skills, food and beverage services, housekeeping, tour guides, etc., which are specialties for both short, medium and long term and have a reasonable income.
The Under-Secretary of State further stated that through the study of tourism professional skills in accordance with ASEAN standards under the quality control training of the Ministry of Tourism, students will be able to move to find work in other countries in the ASEAN region through Mutual Recognition Agreement on ASEAN Tourism Professionals
Mr. Ny Phally said that the specialties of tourism professionals are also divided according to the degree level through the study period, such as the level of certification, short-term study, associate degree, bachelor's degree, master's degree and doctoral degree.
Please be informed that the Ministry of Tourism's outreach workshop was supported and applauded by the management, teachers and students of the four high schools and better understood the importance of tourism professionals in the socio-economic development. And promote the prestige of Cambodia as a tourist destination with quality services and good hospitality.
