Senior Minister Kun Kim Receives Samdech Techo's Order to Meet with Provincial Authorities Around Tonle Sap Lake
(Phnom Penh): As the staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the operator on the battlefield of disaster, Senior Minister Kun Kim always connects with the people and the authorities every time there is a disaster to assess the situation and respond to the problem. Just in time.
In a meeting with the authorities in Kampong Thom and Siem Reap provinces, Senior Minister Kun Kim mentioned Samdech Techo's decisive order to intervene to restore the people's cultivation after the water recedes.
The Senior Minister emphasized that Samdech Techo was born from a farmer family and had a deep understanding of the difficulties and needs of farmers, so he set out an urgent priority direction for the operation to provide rice seeds and mixed crops. Citizens for rehabilitation.
The senior minister stressed that no matter what the circumstances, it is necessary to study how to rehabilitate and provide rice seeds to farmers who are severely affected after the floods recede.
According to the report, nine districts in Siem Reap province were affected by the floods, including 32,465 hectares of rice fields, affecting 25,623 families. Of that, 2,783 hectares of rice fields were damaged, while the size of the damage is planned to be rehabilitated in the first phase of 1,500 hectares.
Separately, Kampong Thom province affected 27,345 hectares of rice crops, damaged 9,500 hectares, equivalent to 1,5223 families.
It should be noted that on the night of October 8, 2022, Samdech Techo Prime Minister issued an order to Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Acting Minister of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, to release rice seeds and other mixed crops to restore people's cultivation. People return after the water recedes.
