Deputy PM Aun Porn Moniroth Establishes Flood Impact Management Team
(Phnom Penh): On October 9, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance and Acting Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, decided to set up a working group to accelerate monitoring and assessment of impacts. Damage to rice and mixed crops due to floods to be able to provide rice seeds and mixed crops to affected farmers to be able to restore crops in time.
In this decision, the Deputy Prime Minister established three main working groups, including: Joint Responsibility Working Group, Field Inspection Working Group in Target Provinces and Reporting Working Group.
In this decision, it is stated that all working groups have the role and duty to coordinate with relevant institutions and sub-national administrations to speed up the examination and assessment of the actual situation of the impact, damage, possibility of rehabilitation of rice and mixed crops. Floods due to cooperation with the National Committee for the Management of the Cambodian Food Reserve System and the National Committee for Disaster Management.
The working group also has the role and task of inspecting and evaluating the actual situation of the impact, damage and feasibility of flood-affected crops in collaboration with the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the National Committee for Disaster Management to provide seeds. Rice and mixed crops to affected farmers to rehabilitate in time.
