World Conference on Constitutional Justice Committed to Implementing the Fundamental Principles of Democracy, the Rule of Law and Human Rights
(Phnom Penh): The World Conference on Constitutional Justice, held from October 2 to 8, 2022 in Bali, Indonesia, has closed. The World Conference on Constitutional Justice (WCCJ), held under the theme "Justice, Constitution and Peace", is committed to implementing the fundamental principles of democracy, the rule of law and human rights at the core of the World Conference on Constitutional Justice.
Dr. M. Chhun Lim, Chairman of the Constitutional Council, led the delegation. The Constitutional Council of Cambodia also led the delegation to participate in this conference. His Excellency Dr. M. Chhun Lim led the delegation back to Cambodia on October 8 after the conference closed.
According to the Constitutional Council, the conference, which was attended by 583 participants from 94 countries, discussed four main topics:
1. Implementing the wider powers of the Constitutional Court, including the relevant authorities, examining the constitutionality of the law and resolving election disputes is a major contribution to social peace.
2. The protection of human rights is a prerequisite for conflict resolution and peace. The Constitutional Court, through the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms, has contributed to the maintenance of social peace and the strengthening of peaceful relations between members of society.
3. Examining the regularity of the election process of the Constitutional Court and ensuring the observance of the Constitution by all state actors is to strengthen the constitution of institutions and representatives of the people, as well as other activities.
4. Settlement of disputes by the Constitutional Court is a precautionary measure in contributing to the maintenance of social peace. Principles of justice and basic rights, and this is a factor that can solve problems and conflicts in society.
