(Kratie): Forces from the Snuol District Police Inspectorate under the direction of Major General Ou Sobona, Kratie Provincial Police Commissioner, cracked down on drug use cases by detaining six suspects and several packages of drugs. Stone bridge point, Tran village, Svay Chreah commune, Snoul district, Kratie province.
According to a police report obtained by Fresh News on the evening of October 8, 2022, the anti-drug force of the Snuol District Police Inspectorate initially cracked down on illegal drug use and detained the suspects. 3 people on the night of October 6, 2022.
According to the confessions of the three suspects, they bought drugs from Oeun Ben alias Touch, 32, of Thnal village, Snuol commune, Snuol district, Kratie province. On the morning of October 7, 2022, with the coordination of the procedure by Mr. Ke Bunnara, Prosecutor of Kratie Provincial Court, the specialized force in cooperation with the Svay Chres Administrative Police Force continued to detain two more suspects.
The first: Oeun Ben alias Touch and the second: Sol Piseth, 17 years old, both live in Thnal village, Svay Chres commune, Snoul district, Kratie province. Confiscated exhibits included 30 packs of white gram powder suspected to be drugs, 1 electronic scale for weighing drugs, some smoking equipment and 1 mobile phone.
Oeun Ben, alias Touch, confessed that he bought drugs from Sorn Oun, alias Koon, who lived in the above commune. After that, the specialized force continued to arrest the suspect named Sorn Oun, alias Koun, 37 years old (a former subject who used to be imprisoned), searched and found 5 big packages of drugs, 1 electronic scale for weighing drugs, Bags for sharing some drugs and 1 mobile phone and 1 car.
All six suspects, along with the above exhibits, are currently being held in custody at the Snuol District Police Inspectorate to build a case to be sent to the provincial specialized office to proceed with the procedure.
