The section of National Road No. 3 (Kampot-Veal Renh) has been built and upgraded many times, but the section of road about 20 kilometers above is often damaged after a short time.
On October 7, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, accompanied by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, inspected the condition of the road. The damage was so severe that the road was only 20 kilometers long and the team spent almost two hours driving through it.
In front of the Deputy Prime Minister, Aun Porn Moniroth, the technician informed the Deputy Prime Minister that the road was damaged due to the condition of the soil there, which was more than 18 meters deep and very waterlogged. Therefore, if you want to build this road for a long time, you need to use high construction technology.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth agreed on this issue because he had known about it since he was Secretary of State at the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The road construction technician also suggested three technical options that can make this road last longer, especially the foundation. Without those technical means, this road will not last long.
Through the three techniques presented, it requires a lot of money. During the discussion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol was informed that Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth needed a budget of about 70 million US dollars.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth accepted the issues raised by the construction technicians and also agreed to choose this high technology for construction so that the road would not be damaged as soon as Samdech Techo decided not to Pave the new road.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth informed that he had already made a request to the Chinese government to help provide a loan for the construction of this section of road. According to the Deputy Prime Minister, the Chinese government has been asked to divert the 2023 budget, which will be used to build other infrastructure, to build this section instead, as it is necessary for use. But the result is to wait for a response from the Chinese government.
