Please be informed that World Vision's humanitarian aid was distributed to 145 families, each family received: 25 kg of rice, 2 bottles of cooking oil, 1 bag of fish, 1 small box of noodles, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce, 2 sticks of salt, 2 kg of soap 4 bars and 1 kg of viso powder.
In response to the floods of 2022, World Vision has provided a total of 615 families in Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap, Preah Vihear and Kampong Thom. World Vision also offers water purification products for 15 days.
It should also be noted that as of October 8, the Provincial Disaster Management Committee has provided assistance to a total of 1,937 families, which are the most vulnerable families.
