(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has organized a series of educational, dissemination and awareness-raising sessions on "Importance of Elections" for students in 25 public and private educational institutions in the capital and provinces. Starting from Oddar Meanchey province on October 6 and Banteay Meanchey province on October 8, 2022.
In this outreach course, with the cooperation of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, in order to raise the awareness of young people in a democratic society and to promote the participation of young people in election events to be more effective.
Mr. Mok Dara, Deputy Secretary General of the NEC, stated that the outreach course aims to spread awareness among young people about the basics of the right to vote through voter registration towards the decision to elect their representatives. Elections are the core of democracy.
He believes that this outreach course will be part of encouraging young people of voting age to come and register to vote at the NEC's deadline. This year's voter registration will take place from October 20 to December 8, 2022.
Please be informed that in this outreach course, there were presentations by senior officials of the NEC on four topics, including:
* History and process of voting * Annual voter registration and voter registration * Importance of voting through youth participation in a democratic society * Youth participation in the electoral phase.
It should be noted that the participants in the education, dissemination and awareness raising on the importance of the election in public and private educational institutions in the two provinces, a total of about 600 people are professors, teachers, election officials and students.
