China seeks new ways to address aging society
There are currently 267 million people over the age of 60 in China. In order to provide a happy life for the elderly, the Chinese government has implemented relevant national strategies, continue to revise some important documents, such as the "Law on the Benefit of the Elderly".
From 2012 to 2022, for the past 10 years, China has continued to improve the social security system for the elderly, the elderly care system and the health support system for the elderly, etc. The total central government budget has invested 35.9 million. Hundreds of millions of Chinese yuan in building pension services for the elderly in the community covers more than half of urban communities and more than half of rural communities.
China is striving to find and follow its unique path to tackle the problem of aging society, which society as a whole respects the elderly, cares for the elderly, so that hundreds of millions of Chinese elderly people can benefit from the results of the version. Economic and social forms Live happily and happily in their old age.
(Phnom Penh): Officials of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts say that most of the current Cambodian films are of poor quality due to limited production capacity as well as lack of production budget.
Speaking at a press conference on the 3rd National Short Film Festival of Cambodia 2022 at the Rosewood Hotel on October 7, 2022, Mr. Sin Chansaya, Advisor to the Ministry of Culture, said that the film now has no sound, big screen and comfort. Not yet. Production problems, production capacity and lack of funds are all big issues.
According to a senior official of the Ministry of Culture, the cinema in modern Cambodia is good, but most Cambodian films can not be screened due to the limited level of films. He compares that if a supermarket always puts in substandard goods, there are no buyers.
In order to encourage young people to develop their creative abilities to contribute to the development of the Cambodian film industry, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts will organize the 3rd National Short Film Festival of Cambodia in 2022 under the slogan "Short films are a step towards long films". On December 16, 2022 and closed on December 20, 2022 at Chaktomuk Conference Hall and cinemas in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Sin Chansaya also said, "Our Ministry of Culture expands the understanding of film production. "So our festival is not to show off, but we come together to see which young people are willing to step into the professional film industry."
He sees that the capacity of producers is still limited because when entering the field, he understands that there are many difficulties. Today, there are very few highly trained and talented producers. Due to lack of funds, some producers have to perform themselves and shoot their own, which is different from his skills, he also makes the result of the film is not good.
At the same time, Pok Borak, director of the Film and Cultural Promotion Department of the Ministry of Culture, said that at least 30 Cambodian films could be produced, but a maximum of two could be exported to foreign markets.
In addition, he mentioned the production of content as a short film posted on social media, and the majority is not quality at all. No quality is one thing, but without meaning, education and inclusion of pornography is even more worrying.
On behalf of the Ministry of Culture, Pok Borak did not support such ignorant production. However, he asked the producers to think carefully about the production of the content of the short film.
According to officials at the Ministry of Culture, the ministry still maintains an education mechanism for producers who produce films that are affected, but for producers who are stubborn and do not listen, it is necessary to accept legal mechanisms. The Ministry of Culture always respects the producers' compositions as stated in the Global Legal Standards on Expression.
At the same time, Mr. Ek Buntha, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Cultural Technology of the Ministry of Culture, said that the production of each film is not simple and only a very talented producer is worth producing. Therefore, the Ministry of Culture has been working hard to find the next generation of young people who can help promote this sector to grow.
Please be informed that the National Short Film Festival of Cambodia is established alternately with the National Short Film Festival of Cambodia every two years by the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, with the Department of Film and Cultural Promotion as its staff. The second National Short Film Festival of Cambodia was held in 2018 but missed in 2020, while the National Short Film Festival of Cambodia was missed in 2019 but was held in 2021 for the fifth time.
The announcement of the Ministry of Culture states that the 3rd National Short Film Festival of Cambodia also has a competition by accepting short films from producers to evaluate the winners and prizes from 1st to 3rd place. Well. The deadline for applications is November 15, 2022.
Selection Criteria and Screening Rights All participating short films will be screened publicly at Chaktomuk Conference Hall and cinemas in Phnom Penh for 3 days from 17 to 19 December. 22022.
