(Battambang): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior and Chairman of the Battambang and Prey Veng Provincial Working Group, inaugurated this morning, October 08, 2022, at the Stung Sangker River Water Forum in Battambang City, Battambang Province.
Speaking on that occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng expressed his congratulations and appreciation to the Battambang Provincial Administration, as well as all the architects, engineers and workers who led and had high responsibility in building this water forum quickly. By quality and aesthetics.
Samdech Sar Kheng claimed that through this luxurious water forum and by organizing the beauty of Stung Sangke and Stung Sangke rich in water, this year's Battambang Boat Race will be held happily, creating a more festive atmosphere. To the people who participated in the entertainment when Kovid-19 was relieved.
Samdech stated that boat racing is a traditional sport, a mass sport, but this sport shows the preservation of the traditions, customs and unity of the people. At the same time, it is also a contribution to the promotion of national culture, and the Royal Government, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has promoted all kinds of sports.
On that occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also informed the ceremony about the upcoming project to build the Independence Monument in Battambang province. Samdech Tha Independence Monument, together with the construction and other aesthetics, Battambang will be more attractive to tourists.
Please be informed that the new water forum is 36 meters long, 16 meters wide and 15.05 meters high. It took 5 months to study the plan and 4 months to build it. 2022 and completed on October 1, 2022, using 98 pillars and using 5 professional engineers and the average workforce of 80 to a maximum of 134 people.
The new Water Forum is designed in the style of architectural works from the style of ancient pagodas, the old provincial hall and the Royal Palace. Beautiful. The roof tiles are studied and used in the Water Forum project, the roof tiles are Khmer tiles that are used on the roofs of houses, roofs, roofs of old temples and so on.
The column section above the column head is fitted with a tilt or support called a handle. Separately, along the pillars around the building are designed and equipped with wall supports. As for the provincial water platform building, it was designed with a lot of open space, so the architects equipped the exterior screens with curved arches to reduce the amount of rainwater entering the building.
