Supporters gather to pray and mourn the 131 victims of the stampede at Indonesia National Stadium
(Indonesia): Indonesians gathered on Friday to pray and mourn the 131 people who died in a football stampede six days ago while calling for an immediate investigation into the disaster. One of the world's deadliest stadiums for victims to rest in peace. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Friday, October 7, 2022.
Most of the dead were suffocating as they fled in panic to try to escape after police fired tear gas in an attempt to disperse the crowd.
Widodo, a 53-year-old football fan, said after the prayer: "Many fans have demanded an immediate solution to the case so that the souls of the dead can go to their deaths."
In connection with this incident, the President of Indonesia has decided to suspend all other matches of the domestic football league that is scheduled to take place, as well as to monitor and re-evaluate in detail the order of football matches in the country. Such as security procedures during the game.
Tang Kork District Governor Inspects Flood Situation in Pong Rong Commune and Calls on Caution
(Kampong Thom): After several consecutive days of rain, some places in Cambodia, including Taing Kork district, Kampong Thom province, have been flooded, and the river level is gradually rising in Pong Ror commune. However, the flooding of the river in the commune did not affect the rice crop as the flooded rice fields became the fishing grounds of the people.
Concerned about the safety of the people and under the guidance of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom, Mr. Hak Mong Huot, Governor of Taing Kork district led officials to inspect the flood situation.
Mr. Hak Mong Huot called on all people to be more careful about the floods caused by the rising river in recent days, which caused floods inundating some villages and roads.
He added that as the weather in the region is experiencing more rain in the coming days, therefore, caution should be exercised. In particular, be careful of young children, do not let them play in the water and call on people to pay more attention to health and food safety.
The governor of Taing Kork district also instructed the commune administration to monitor and report the flood situation on a daily basis to the district administration in order to provide timely assistance in case of more serious situations.
