(Phnom Penh): On Friday, October 7, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, spent the whole day from dawn to dusk to complete some important work related to customs and ministry. Public Works and Transport.
At around 8 am, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, accompanied by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, and the leaders of the two ministries inspected the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway management process.
Understanding the expressway management process, the Deputy Prime Minister received a presentation from the staff of the investment company as well as Senior Minister Sun Chanthol on the traffic management system on the expressway, especially some procedures at the toll booth.
After listening, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth gave some suggestions on the payment of vehicle owners when traveling on the expressway. The Deputy Prime Minister also proposed improvements on some issues related to the expressway.
After inspecting the expressway management process, the Deputy Prime Minister continued on the expressway to Sihanoukville. In Sihanoukville, the Minister of Economy and Finance presided over the inauguration of the Customs and Excise Office at four other locations.
In Sihanoukville, the Deputy Prime Minister also inspected two wastewater treatment plants under construction by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. During the inspection visit, the Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth and Senior Minister Sun Chanthol discussed the management of wastewater with great care.
After completing his mission in Sihanoukville, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth continued his journey to Kampot. Labor Mission in Kampot Province, Deputy Prime Minister inspected the section of National Road No. 3 (Kampot-Veal Renh) which is badly damaged.
During the inspection, the Deputy Prime Minister also listened to some issues related to this section of the road and listened to the technical explanation of the construction of this section of the road to make it last longer, while the soil condition there is a type of soil. High technology to last a long time.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth confirmed that he had submitted a proposal to the Chinese government to consider returning the unnecessary project in 2023 to the National Road No. 3 project instead, as the construction of this road is very necessary.
After concluding the talks, the Deputy Prime Minister also traveled to Kampot to inspect the construction of a tourist port in Kampot. The road from Vilren to Kampot town, about 20 kilometers long, was badly damaged, making it difficult to travel. The damaged section of the road is only about 20 kilometers long, but it takes up to two hours to drive through.
After crossing this difficult road, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth continued his visit to Kampot tourist port. The port was built to attract tourists by sea, especially with neighboring Vietnam and Thailand.
Kampot Tourism Port has been completed with an estimated US $ 18 million loan from the Asian Development Bank (ADB). The port is built on an area of about 4 hectares.
During his visit to the tourist port, the Deputy Prime Minister made a number of recommendations related to port management, solving challenges and advising to consider attracting tourists to Cambodia.
