He urged health workers at all levels to visit people and provide health education in order to change attitudes towards malaria prevention and treatment.
The Minister provided additional important recommendations to the Malaria Control Center and all relevant partners as follows:
* Identify vulnerable populations (mobile population and forest-related businesses) in the management area so that everyone can intervene effectively
* Villages with high rates of malaria transmission should conduct blood tests on the general population in the village and conduct collective treatment on the target population and check carefully before applying to pregnant women and children.
* Urge all officials to cooperate, especially the provincial health department, local authorities and health partner organizations in each province need to implement the National Strategic Plan for Malaria Eradication to be effective in order to eradicate malaria. 2025
* National Center for Malaria Control, Provincial Health Department and all relevant partner organizations jointly review the progress of work, risk factors and opportunities to discuss together to find solutions on the scope of current response activities and expand the implementation of geographical appropriateness. Is successfully meeting the indicators set in the strategy for the eradication of malaria.
