The main tourist port in Kampot province is located next to Dang Prek, a tributary in Teuk Chhou district, about 6 km from Kampot city. Construction of the seaport on more than 4 hectares of land began construction in 2018 and was completed in June 2022.
Many necessary infrastructures have been built to serve the berths of cruise ships and buildings for tourists. According to the report, the infrastructure to be built includes: a port more than 123 meters long and more than 11 meters wide, passenger and restaurant buildings, roads, garbage collection buildings, technical buildings, public bathrooms, reservoirs, ponds and systems. Some other infrastructure.
Kampot Tourism Port was built under an ADB loan of more than $ 18 million. Construction process by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
After the completion of construction on October 7, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, accompanied by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport and Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, visited and discussed some work to Launch this port.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Mony raised a number of ideas related to the management, launch and provision of various services for the tourism sector.
According to the technical officer, there are some obstacles in the port related to the preference of cruise ships. Currently, only small boats with a capacity of 300 to 400 passengers are allowed to dock. In order for the large tourist cruise ships to dock, further deepening of the ship's orbit was required.
Please note that Kampot tourist port can be connected to the port in Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Koh Rong and also to the port of Koh Tral and other ports in Vietnam and Thailand.
