According to a report by Leang Keo, chief of the Kdei Doung Administrative Police Station, the drowning child was 16-year-old Chak Kanha, a resident of Kampong Kor Leu village, Kampong Kor commune, a student at Peam Kreng Secondary School. At the scene, 4 students came to visit the flooded road (Koh Ta Hem area) in O Sambour village, Kdei Dong commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province, but 3 people were rescued on time.
