The Romans considered the lunar year to be 355 days, not 354 days because it was an even number, although the actual lunar year had 354,367 days. However, the end still requires that at least one of the 12 months be an even number of days. Therefore, King Nouma decided to choose February for only 28 days and use this month to pay homage to the Roman emperors because of the unlucky number of days.
