Minister Chea Van Det urges stakeholders to take some necessary steps to develop postal sector in line with policy
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, on October 7, 2022, urged all stakeholders to implement some necessary tasks to develop the postal sector in accordance with the policy.
This promotion was made on the occasion of Mr. Chea Vandeth's participation in the celebration of World Post Day 2022, the first postal forum and the Phnom Penh Post Service Fair this morning, October 7, 2022.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Chea Vandeth emphasized that he would like to take this opportunity to encourage and encourage all stakeholders to carry out the necessary work to develop the postal sector in accordance with the following policies:
First, to participate in the preparation of a detailed action plan for implementation in the period from 2022 to 2030, according to the list of priority activities presented in the policy appendix.
Second, to cooperate responsibly in the activities under each strategy under the coordination of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications in the short, medium and long term from 2022 to 2030.
Third, strictly enforce the relevant laws and regulations to improve the quality of postal services and consumer protection, as well as to manage the development of the entire postal sector.
Fourth, digitalize in the production and delivery of postal services and promote research and innovation in the postal sector.
Fifth, seize the opportunity to grow e-commerce both domestically and across borders, focusing on improving the quality and reliability of postal delivery services. E-commerce and postal services are mutually reinforcing forces.
While e-commerce promotes the development of the postal service market, the improvement of postal delivery services contributes significantly to the growth of e-commerce and investment attraction in this area.
Sixth, follow up on the new decisions and strategies of the Global Postal Union to organize the implementation in accordance with the context of the development of the postal sector in Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Chea Vandeth said that the postal sector is considered to have the potential to contribute to sustaining economic growth and improving the quality of life of the people in Cambodia, linked to daily life in both urban and rural areas. .
The Minister of Posts and Telecommunications emphasized that the development of this sector in a sustainable and global manner is a topic that is focused not only in Cambodia but also in the regional and international framework. .
Mr. Chea Van Det said that for Cambodia, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has achieved the development of physical infrastructure in the country everywhere from urban to rural, which can help facilitate Providing more efficient delivery service.
(Koh Kong): Mr. Sok Sothy, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province, held a meeting on October 6, 2022 to discuss the current status of the implementation of the project to improve livelihoods, marine and land conservation in Koh Kong province. .
