Death news! Ratanakkiri Provincial Councilor Sok Vuthy dies in motorcycle crash
(Rattanakiri): Mr. Sok Vuthy, Member of Rattanakiri Provincial Council, passed away when his family and authorities took him to the hospital after the motorcycle crashed at 18:40 on October 6, 2022 in front of Laban Primary School. Circus, O'Kandel village, Sangkat Boeung Kanseng, Banlung city, Ratanakkiri province.
Lieutenant Colonel Mao Phearum, Deputy Chief of Traffic Office of Ratanakkiri Provincial Police, told Fresh News on the morning of October 7 that Sok Vuthy, 66, a member of Ratanakkiri Provincial Council, resides in Tes Anlong Village, Boeung Kanseng Commune, Banlung City. After being sent to the emergency room at the provincial referral hospital.
According to Mr. Mao Phearum, a 16-year-old motorcyclist named Sim Lay, a resident of Thmor Da Village, Sangkat Boeung Kanseng, Banlung City, was seriously injured (bleeding head, nose, feet and body) and was receiving emergency treatment at the Provincial Referral Hospital. From the authorities as well.
Lt. Col. Mao Phearum also confirmed that the motorcycle must be stored at the traffic office to complete the case according to the procedure. The body was handed over to the family to be taken to a traditional ceremony in Phnom Penh with the utmost grief.
Remarkably, Mr. Sok Vuthy, Member of Provincial Council and Member of Ratanakkiri Provincial Red Cross Committee, happily participated with the provincial leadership in the development of the province, both in terms of empire and Buddhism, in humanitarian work.
Mr. Sok Vuthy is a friendly and virtuous person to the general public.
