BANGKOK: The number of people in a mass shooting at a child care center in northeastern Thailand on Thursday has risen to 38, mostly children, local Thai authorities have reported. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Thursday, October 6, 2022.
Thai police also said the gunman went to kill his family before committing suicide.
Such shootings are rare in Thailand. In 2020, a Thai soldier shot dead 29 people and wounded 57 in the hours before the shooting ended after the gunman was shot dead by Thai special forces.
