At the same time, Mr. Khuong Sreng also advised to reorganize the infrastructure of Victory Blvd and the section of National Road No. 6 in Phnom Penh to the border of Kandal province with the guidance of the 14 district authorities to cooperate while Cambodia Host the 32nd SEA Games Summit and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023.
This instruction was made on the afternoon of October 6, 2022 in the meeting to prepare for the cooperation of the ASEAN Summit 2022 and the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023 with Participate from 14 district authorities and other relevant departments.
Mr. Khuong Sreng added that after the rainy season, we always repair the road to facilitate people's travel, but for this year, it is even more special to host the summit and the SEA Games. 32nd and the 12th ASEAN Para Games in 2023, which must be given high attention.
Mr. Khuong Sreng added that this work does not depend on the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, it must be the participation of the 14 district authorities to cooperate and participate in this work to run smoothly, such as to check the sewer. Broken lights, stone barriers split the road to report repairs.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that we have a lot of big events, with Cambodia to host the summit and to host the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games in 2023. Therefore, the work to be done is to make Phnom Penh beautiful to receive delegates from more than 40 countries to meet in Phnom Penh.
It should be noted that 56 roads in Phnom Penh Capital Administration have been being improved, including major boulevards that have been repaired, such as Sisowath Quay, Russian Federation Road 47, National Road 6A and Mekong Road. The work will be completed 100% by the end of this month. For flower decoration, garden lighting is also the main work to be improved. What do you know about the massacre in Thailand?
BANGKOK: A gunman opened fire on at least 34 people in the northeastern province of Thailand before shooting his family and committing suicide, Thai police said on Thursday.
The victims who lost their lives there included 23 children. The suspect was identified as 34-year-old Panya Khamrab. According to Thai media, the gunman was a former police officer who was fired in 2021 for drug use, and locals are well aware that he was People are also addicted to drugs.
In this horrific attack, the gunman was armed with a pistol, a shotgun and a knife. It was not immediately clear why the gunman committed the atrocity, while an investigation is under way. But Thai police have made a preliminary conclusion that it may be due to drug effects.
According to a report released last September, there are more than 4 million unregistered firearms in Thailand and 6 million registered. The report also said that selling cheap guns online made it easier for the general public to buy guns without going through strict censorship.
Tomorrow, the court will announce the verdict in the case of Mr. Son Chhay on the complaint of the NEC in the case of defamation and continue the trial on the complaint of the Cambodian People's Party
(Phnom Penh): As planned, on the morning of October 7, 2022, tomorrow, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court will hear the verdict in the case of Mr. Son Chhay, Vice President of the Candlelight Party, which was filed by the National Organizing Committee. Election (NEC).
Please be informed that after the hearing of the accused Son Chhay in the defamation case related to the accusation of "vote theft" for one morning on September 29, 2022, the court decided to postpone the verdict. To October 7, 2022.
Ky Tech, a lawyer representing the Cambodian People's Party, confirmed to Fresh News that the court is scheduled to hear two of Son Chhay's cases on September 29, 2022, including the first case. Defamation case filed by NEC and another case filed by CPP.
However, after the hearing in the first case from morning until 12 noon, the court decided to take the second case to trial on October 7, 2022, while the verdict in the first case is to be announced on the same day. The court's decision follows a request for an extension of time from Son Chhay and his lawyer. This was confirmed by Mr. Ky Tech, a lawyer of the Cambodian People's Party.
Mr. Son Chhay, represented by the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, was charged with "public defamation" in a complaint filed by the National Election Committee (NEC) and the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) in connection with a media report. Alleging that the results of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election in 2022 were rigged.
In a complaint filed with the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on June 14, 2022, Mr. Kitech claimed that Mr. Chhay's unsubstantiated allegations in previous interviews with some media outlets were fraudulent. , Distorting the truth is giving false information with the intention of blaming the CPP in good faith.
As for the NEC complaint, the NEC asked the court to convict Son Chhay for public defamation under Article 305 of the Criminal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia and to demand that Son Chhay write a letter of apology to the NEC. 683 prisoners request commutation and pardon on the occasion of Water Festival and National Independence Day
