(Phnom Penh): Most people think that "owls" can turn their heads 360 degrees, but some opinions do not agree with this view until a new study by scientists and also showed New evidence and arguments to shed light on this skepticism and uncertainty.
According to scientists, "owls can not turn their heads around, they can only turn 270 degrees."
What people see as being able to turn their head 360 degrees may be due to confusion through the naked eye. The scientists explained that the owl was able to do this because of its special backbone and muscles, as well as its 14-wheeled skeleton, which was specially designed to allow the bones to move freely. Also, because of the larger wings on both sides and its thick feathers, it also deceives our eyes.
