Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted this during the opening speech of the International Party Conference via video on the afternoon of Thursday, October 6, 2022. The International Party Conference was held directly in Russia under the theme "Environmental Policy and Sustainable Development". The conference brings together leaders of political parties around the world in a hybrid format, with live and online participants.
The conference aims to exchange views and experiences related to the environment and sustainable development to jointly address major humanitarian challenges.
Samdech Techo, the leader of the party leading the Royal Government of Cambodia, said that in the face of many challenges in the world, all political parties really play an important role in contributing to the improvement of environmental sustainability and sustainable development, as well as Ensure the improvement of life, well-being and prosperity of the people and the planet as a whole.
He added that due to high economic growth, Cambodia became a low middle income country in 2015 and will continue to achieve high middle income status by 2030. At the same time, Cambodia has been striving to increase its participation in addressing global environmental challenges, including climate change, in line with the principle of "shared responsibility, but at different levels based on individual capabilities."
"As a small country with low greenhouse gas emissions, Cambodia is committed to tackling global climate change by triple the national budget for counter-climate change activities," he said. "Climate change will set a target of reducing emissions by about 42 percent by 2030."
The leader of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) drew the attention of political party leaders that environmental issues do not know the country's borders, so only international cooperation and solidarity can effectively solve global environmental challenges and save the planet. Our planet from disasters for our people forever.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his belief that the countries of the world can really work together to solve environmental problems, especially climate change, through solidarity and cooperation, for example, the implementation of the Montreal Protocol, which has been reduced and Leads to eliminating ozone depleting substances.
Samdech Techo expressed Cambodia's commitment at the conference that Cambodia is ready and needs partners, both public and private, to help achieve their commitment to respond to environmental issues as well as climate change.
