Natural disasters! Lightning strike kills 1 and injures 5 in Kampong Ror district, Svay Rieng province
(Svay Rieng): Heavy rain mixed with thunder and lightning caused the death of a man and seriously injured five people while the victim was herding buffalo and sitting in the rain under a acacia tree at 3:35 In the afternoon of October 5, 2022 in Roth village, Nhor commune, Kampong Ror district, Svay Rieng province.
According to the district police, the dead man was named Khim San, 69 years old, a farmer living in Roth village, Nhor commune, Kampong Ror district. The families of the five victims were taken to their respective departments for treatment.
According to the victim in the lightning strike, "Before the incident, it rained heavily and she and five other villagers ran to shelter under the acacia tree. At that time, the victim Standing alone, then suddenly heard the sound of lightning, a man named Khim San fell to his death immediately and five people were seriously injured, causing surprise.
Sources said that after the incident, local authorities arrived and examined the body in collaboration with doctors, concluding that the body was indeed killed by lightning. Authorities recorded and handed over the body to the family for a traditional ceremony with great emotion.
Local authorities have called on residents to evacuate in the event of heavy rain, wind and lightning, and to turn off their phones and to report any incidents to local authorities in order to facilitate timely rescue interventions.
Tomorrow, the Ministry of Culture will hold a press conference on the organization of the 3rd Cambodia National Short Film Festival after a two-year absence due to Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): On October 7, 2022, tomorrow, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts will hold a press conference on the organization of the 3rd National Short Film Festival of Cambodia at the Rosewood Hotel in Phnom Penh, as well as a presentation to support partners while the festival This was missed two years ago due to the global epidemic.
The National Short Film Festival of Cambodia is established alternately with the National Short Film Festival of Cambodia every two years by the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, with the Department of Film and Cultural Promotion as its staff. The second National Short Film Festival of Cambodia was held in 2018 but missed in 2020, while the National Short Film Festival of Cambodia was missed in 2019 but was held in 2021 for the fifth time.
Pok Borak, Director of the Department of Film and Cultural Promotion, told Fresh News that a press conference on the organization of the 3rd National Short Film Festival of Cambodia will be held to further disseminate the announcement of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, especially Present to support partners so that they understand the advantages of organizing this important event.
Phnom Penh Capital Administration Shows the Date and Venue of Candidates for the 2022 Prison Officers for the Ministry of Interior
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has issued a notification showing the date and place of the examination for candidates to be included in the Ministry of Interior's prison officials for 2022. This is according to the letter from Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Chairman of the Phnom Penh Examination Commission, which was received by Fresh News on the morning of October 6, 2022.
Candidates can check the name, table number and room number in the list of candidates which will be posted on Saturday, October 08, 2022 at 09:00 at Chea Sim Santhor Mok High School Examination Center. Candidates must apply medical measures in the area of the examination center by keeping the distance and wearing a mask, except the guardian requesting to remove the mask for verification. For more information, candidates can contact the place where they applied for the exam registration.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia considers the North Korean missile launch as a threat to regional security and condemns this action (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen this morning, October 6, 2022. It is not a joke that North Korea has fired missiles through Japan, which is a threat to regional security, and Cambodia condemns this.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on the occasion of opening the conference "Vision of Cambodia 2022" to discuss the recovery of Cambodia after the Kovid 19 crisis, claimed that the missile launch was not just a launch into the sea, this is a cross-country shooting. One country, and they want to shoot at any part of Japan.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia said: "The unfortunate thing yesterday is that the missile launch from North Korea through Japan is not a joke. Cambodia condemned the talks with the Cuban Prime Minister. This is a threat to regional security, not a shooting into the sea, but a cross-country shooting.
Shooting across a country means that if I want to shoot into Tokyo or shoot into any part of Japan, I can shoot because I have already crossed the country. In this regard, Cambodia has taken a clear position.
Please be reminded that during the bilateral meeting with the Prime Minister of Cuba Manuel Marquez, who is visiting Cambodia on Tuesday, October 4, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen informed his counterpart that he condemned the missile launch across Japan. Made by the Democratic People's Republic of Korea.
The Prime Minister said that the behavior of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea was dangerous and another violation of UN Security Council resolutions.
On October 6, 2022, North Korea test-fired two more short-range ballistic missiles into the East Sea or the Sea of Japan after Pyongyang condemned the United States for convening a council meeting. UN security and joint military exercises between Washington and Seoul.
