Key remarks and full speeches by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the opening of the conference "Vision of Cambodia 2022" to discuss the recovery of Cambodia after the Kovid crisis 19
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 6, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the opening ceremony of the conference "Vision of Cambodia 2022". The "Vision of Cambodia" conference is an important forum to bring together experts to discuss topics related to economic and social issues as input for solving challenges and finding opportunities to promote development in Cambodia.
On the occasion of the opening of the conference, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech and talk for about an hour below the main content and the full speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested political parties and civil society to understand the Royal Government's announcement of financial assistance to the poor because this is not an election campaign, but to help the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is considered as a leading country that has managed and recovered from the crisis of Kovid-19 well. In an environment where many countries around the world continue to experience epidemics, the Royal Government has been trying to turn the crisis into an opportunity by accelerating deepening reforms to improve the business environment and strengthen competitiveness. Of Cambodia
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requests the people in Preah Dak commune to keep calm. Samdech Techo announces that he will send Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara and Mrs. Phoeung Sakona to meet with the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has not yet considered dismantling the buildings in Preah Dak village. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government is studying the restoration of the eastern subsoil, which used to have a storage capacity of up to 300,000 cubic meters. This rehabilitation is likely to affect some people in Preah Dak village.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requests the Cambodia Vision Conference to review and discuss whether Cambodia can achieve the 2030 Sustainable Development Goals?
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that North Korea's missile launch is a threat to regional security.
