Figures show that from January to September 2022, the CDC approved a total of 150 investment projects under the investment of 3,500 million US dollars, of which Cambodian investors have led the way in investing more than 1,700 million US dollars. 50.94% of total investment, doubled compared to the same period in 2021, with an investment of nearly $ 700 million and a share of only 20.74%.
Dr. Hong Vannak, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, told Fresh News on October 6 that while foreign investment flows have declined in recent years after repeated crises, they have been hampered. Finance, therefore, is an opportunity to encourage local investors who still have the capital to take the opportunity to invest and organize their services or products to compete in the market, while the Royal Government of Cambodia has a policy to promote local investment.
"Local investors, especially those with large capital, do not hesitate because their capital can be rotated while there is no large inflow of foreign investment, so they take this opportunity," he said. The company they can afford is investing. For example, investing in the construction of houses, houses for sale or organizing various business crafts.
He said that the crisis that Cambodia as well as the world is facing may be an obstacle to prevent the decision of foreign investors to be reluctant or hesitant to invest in Cambodia, even though Cambodia has investment laws. Which facilitates foreign investment and implementation of various agreements.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary General of the CDC, stated that the Council for the Development of Cambodia will continue to promote and attract investment by continuing to strengthen investment maintenance mechanisms and continue to participate in the implementation of various reform measures of the Royal Government, especially measures. Facilitate investment for domestic and foreign investors.
According to the Council for the Development of Cambodia, in the first nine months of this year, investment in agriculture and agro-industry was 7 projects with a capital of over 104 million USD, 132 industrial projects with a capital of nearly 1,400 million US dollars, and 3 tourism projects. With more than 164 million US dollars in capital and infrastructure, there are eight projects with a total capital of nearly 1.8 billion US dollars.
